<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="EZK" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Ezekiel</para>

<para style="toc1">Ezekiel</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="EZK 1"/>

<para style="s">Ezekiel’s Vision by the River Kebar</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 137:1–9</char></note>And it came to pass in the thirtieth year, in the fourth <char style="add">month</char>, on the fifth of the month, as I <char style="add">was</char> in the midst of the captivity by the River Kebar, <char style="add">that</char> the heavens were opened, and I saw visions of God.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from God</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 1:2"/>On the fifth of the month—it <char style="add">was</char> the fifth year of the captivity of king Jehoiachin— <verse eid="EZK 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 1:3"/>the word of YHWH came directly to Ezekiel son of Buzi the priest in the land of the Chaldeans<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Babylonians</char></note> by the River Kebar; And there the hand of YHWH was upon him. <verse eid="EZK 1:3"/></para>

<para style="s">The Four Living Creatures</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 1:4"/>And I looked, and behold, a wind of a tempest was coming from the north, and a great cloud and fire taking hold <char style="add">of it</char>, and a brightness to it all around, and in the midst of it <char style="add">was</char> like the color of amber, from the midst of the fire.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and the center of the fire looked like glowing metal</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; similarly in verse 27</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 1:5"/>And in the midst of it <char style="add">was</char> the likeness of four living creatures. And this <char style="add">was</char> their appearance: The likeness of a man <char style="add">was</char> unto them, <verse eid="EZK 1:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 1:6"/><char style="add">with</char> four faces for each one, and four wings for each one unto them. <verse eid="EZK 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 1:7"/>And their feet <char style="add">were</char> straight feet, and the soles of their feet <char style="add">were</char> like the soles of the foot of a calf, and they sparkled like an eye of polished bronze. <verse eid="EZK 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 1:8"/>And the hands of a man <char style="add">were</char> under their wings on four of their sides. And the faces and wings <char style="add">were</char> unto the four of them, <verse eid="EZK 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 1:9"/>joining each one to her sister; their wings did not turn in their going, <char style="add">each</char> man went to straight ahead. <verse eid="EZK 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 1:10"/>And the likeness of their faces, <char style="add">was</char> the face of a man, and the face of a lion on the right side <char style="add">was</char> unto the four of them; and the face of an ox on the left side <char style="add">was</char> unto the four of them, and the face of an eagle <char style="add">was</char> unto the four of them. <verse eid="EZK 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 1:11"/>And such <char style="add">were</char> their faces. And their wings were spread out above each one; unto each one <char style="add">were</char> two touching one, and two were covering their bodies. <verse eid="EZK 1:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 1:12"/>And each one went toward straight ahead of its face; to the <char style="add">direction</char> that there the spirit was to go, they would go, <char style="add">and</char> they did not turn in their going. <verse eid="EZK 1:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 1:13"/>And the likeness of the living creatures, their appearance <char style="add">was</char> like coals of fire burning, like the appearance of torches; it was going about among the living creatures, and brightness <char style="add">was</char> unto the fire, and from the fire was going forth lightning. <verse eid="EZK 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 1:14"/>And the living creatures <char style="add">were</char> running and returning like the appearance of the lightning. <verse eid="EZK 1:14"/></para>

<para style="s">The Four Wheels</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 1:15"/>And I looked <char style="add">at</char> the living creatures, and behold, a wheel on the earth beside the living creatures, one with his four faces. <verse eid="EZK 1:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 1:16"/>The appearance of the wheels and their workings <char style="add">was</char> like an eye of beryl, and a single likeness unto four of them; and their appearance and of their workings <char style="add">was</char> as it were a wheel in the middle of a wheel. <verse eid="EZK 1:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 1:17"/>Upon their four sides, in their going they went, <char style="add">and</char> they did not turn aside in their going. <verse eid="EZK 1:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 1:18"/>And <char style="add">unto</char> their rims <char style="add">was</char> height to them and fearsomeness to them, and their rims <char style="add">were</char> full of eyes all around for the four of them. <verse eid="EZK 1:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 1:19"/>And in the going of the living creatures, the wheels went beside them; and in the lifting up of the living creatures from the earth, the wheels were lifted up. <verse eid="EZK 1:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 1:20"/>Upon which the spirit was to go, there they would go; there the spirit <char style="add">was</char> to go, and the wheels would rise alongside them, for the spirit of the living creatures <char style="add">was</char> in the wheels. <verse eid="EZK 1:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 1:21"/>In their going they go, and in their standing they stand; and in their being lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up together with them, for the spirit of the living creatures <char style="add">was</char> in the wheels. <verse eid="EZK 1:21"/></para>

<para style="s">The Divine Glory</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 1:22"/>And the likeness over the heads of the living creatures <char style="add">was</char> the firmament, like an eye of awe-inspiring crystal, stretched out over their heads above. <verse eid="EZK 1:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 1:23"/>And under the firmament their wings <char style="add">were</char> straight, each one toward its sister; for each one <char style="add">were</char> two <char style="add">as</char> a covering for them, and for each one <char style="add">were</char> two covering for them their body. <verse eid="EZK 1:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 1:24"/>And I heard the voice of their wings, like the voice of many waters, like the voice of Shaddai,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> in their going—the voice of a tumult like the voice of an army—and in their standing, they would slacken their wings. <verse eid="EZK 1:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 1:25"/>And there was a voice from over the firmament that <char style="add">was</char> over their heads; in their standing they would slacken their wings. <verse eid="EZK 1:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 1:26"/>And from above the firmament that <char style="add">was</char> over their heads, in appearance like a stone of sapphire, <char style="add">was</char> the likeness of a throne, and on the likeness of the throne <char style="add">was</char> a likeness like the appearance of a man over it from above. <verse eid="EZK 1:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 1:27"/>And I saw as an eye of amber, like the appearance of fire, a house for it all around, from the appearance of His loins and above; and from the appearance of His loins and downward, I saw as the appearance of fire and brightness to it all around. <verse eid="EZK 1:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 1:28"/>As the appearance of a rainbow that comes to be in the cloud on a day of rain, so <char style="add">was</char> the appearance of the brightness surrounding. It <char style="add">was</char> the appearance of the likeness of the glory of YHWH. And I saw <char style="add">it</char>, and I fell upon my face, and I heard a voice speaking. <verse eid="EZK 1:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="EZK 2"/>

<para style="s">Ezekiel’s Call</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 2:1"/>And He said to me: “Son of man,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Son of Adam</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; here and throughout Ezekiel</char></note> stand on your feet, and I will speak to you.” <verse eid="EZK 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 2:2"/>And the Spirit came into me as He spoke to me and set me on my feet, and I heard the One speaking to me. <verse eid="EZK 2:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 2:3"/>And He said to me, “Son of man, I am sending you to the sons of Israel, to a rebellious nation that has rebelled against Me; they and their fathers have transgressed against Me until this very day. <verse eid="EZK 2:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 2:4"/>And the sons <char style="add">are</char> hard of face and strong of heart; to them I am sending you, and you shall say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 2:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 2:5"/>And they, whether they hear, or whether they refuse—for they <char style="add">are</char> a rebellious house—they will know that a prophet has been in their midst. <verse eid="EZK 2:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 2:6"/>And you, son of man, do not be afraid of them or of their words; do not be afraid—if briers and thorns <char style="add">are</char> with you and among you scorpions are sitting!—Of their words, and do not be afraid of their faces, and do not be dismayed, for they <char style="add">are</char> a rebellious house. <verse eid="EZK 2:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 2:7"/>And you shall speak My words to them, whether they hear or whether they refuse—for they <char style="add">are</char> rebellious. <verse eid="EZK 2:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 2:8"/>And you, son of man, you must hear what I am going to say to you: Do not come to be rebellious like <char style="add">this</char> house of rebellion! Open your mouth and eat what I am giving to you.” <verse eid="EZK 2:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 2:9"/>And I looked, and behold, a hand was stretched out to me, and behold, in it <char style="add">was</char> a scroll of a book. <verse eid="EZK 2:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 2:10"/>And He spread it out before my face, and it was written on the face and on the back; and written on it <char style="add">were</char> lamentations, and mourning, and woe. <verse eid="EZK 2:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="EZK 3"/>

<para style="s">Ezekiel Eats the Scroll</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 3:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Revelation 10:1–11</char></note>And He said to me, “Son of man, what you find, you must eat. Eat this scroll, and go speak to the house of Israel!” <verse eid="EZK 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 3:2"/>And I opened my mouth, and He caused me to eat this scroll. <verse eid="EZK 3:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 3:3"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, feed your belly and fill your bowels with this scroll that I am giving to you!” </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 3:3">And I ate, and it was as sweet as honey in my mouth. <verse eid="EZK 3:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 3:4"/>And He said to me, “Son of man, go, come into the house of Israel, and speak with My words to them. <verse eid="EZK 3:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 3:5"/>For not to a people of unfathomable speech and heavy tongue are you being sent, <char style="add">but</char> to the house of Israel— <verse eid="EZK 3:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 3:6"/>not to many peoples of unfathomable speech and heavy tongue, whose words you cannot understand. If I had not sent you to them, they would have listened to you. <verse eid="EZK 3:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 3:7"/>And the house of Israel are not willing to listen to you, because they are not willing to listen to Me! For all the house of Israel, they <char style="add">are</char> strong of forehead and hard of heart. <verse eid="EZK 3:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 3:8"/>Behold, I have made your face strong against their faces, and your forehead hard against their foreheads. <verse eid="EZK 3:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 3:9"/>I have made your forehead like a diamond stronger than flint. Do not be afraid of them, and do not be dismayed at their faces, for they <char style="add">are</char> a house of rebellion.” <verse eid="EZK 3:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 3:10"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, all My words that I speak to you, take into your heart, and hear with your ears. <verse eid="EZK 3:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 3:11"/>And go, come to the captivity, to the sons of your people, and speak to them and say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord YHWH!’—Whether they hear or whether they refuse.” <verse eid="EZK 3:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 3:12"/>And the Spirit lifted me up, and I heard behind me the voice of a great quaking: ‘Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the glory of YHWH from His place!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the wind</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 14</char></note>’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">behind me a voice as the glory of YHWH rose from its place!</char></note><verse eid="EZK 3:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 3:13"/>And the voice of the wings of the living creatures, touching each one to her sister, and the voice of the wheels beside them, and the a voice of a great quaking. <verse eid="EZK 3:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 3:14"/>And the Spirit lifted me up and took me away, and I went in bitterness, in the heat of my spirit. And the hand of YHWH upon me <char style="add">was</char> strong. <verse eid="EZK 3:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 3:15"/>And I came to the captivity at Tel-abib, those dwelling by the River Kebar, and I sat there <char style="add">where</char> they were sitting, and I sat there seven days being desolate in their midst. <verse eid="EZK 3:15"/></para>

<para style="s">A Watchman for Israel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 3:16"/>And it came to pass at the end of seven days, that the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 3:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 3:17"/>“Son of man, I have made you a watchman for the house of Israel; and hear a word from My mouth, and give them a warning from Me. <verse eid="EZK 3:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 3:18"/>In My saying to the wicked, ‘You will surely die!’ And you do not warn him, and you do not speak to warn the wicked from his wicked way to save his life, that wicked one will die in his iniquity,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for his iniquity</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 19</char></note> and his blood I will require from your hand. <verse eid="EZK 3:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 3:19"/>And you, if you warn the wicked and he does not turn back from his wickedness and from his wicked way, he will die in his iniquity and you will have delivered your own soul. <verse eid="EZK 3:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 3:20"/>And in the turning away of a righteous one from his righteousness so that he does iniquity, and I set a stumbling block before him, he will die because you did not give him warning—in his sin<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for his sin</char></note> he will die—and his righteousness that he did will not be remembered, and his blood I will require from your hand. <verse eid="EZK 3:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 3:21"/>And you, if you warn the righteous not to sin—the righteous one—and he does not sin, he shall surely live, because he was warned and you will have delivered your own soul.” <verse eid="EZK 3:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 3:22"/>And the hand of YHWH was upon me there, and He said to me: “Rise, go out into the plain, and there I will speak with you.” <verse eid="EZK 3:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 3:23"/>And I arose and went out into the plain, and behold, there the glory of YHWH was standing, like the glory that I saw by the River Kebar. And I fell upon my face. <verse eid="EZK 3:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 3:24"/>And the Spirit came into me and set me upon my feet, and He spoke with me and said to me: “Go, shut yourself up in the midst of your house. <verse eid="EZK 3:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 3:25"/>And you, son of man, behold, they will place around you ropes, and they will bind you with them so that you cannot go out in their midst. <verse eid="EZK 3:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 3:26"/>And your tongue I will make cling to the roof of your mouth, and you will be mute, and you will be for them as a man unable to rebuke, for they <char style="add">are</char> a house of rebellion. <verse eid="EZK 3:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 3:27"/>And in My speaking with you, I will open your mouth, <char style="add">then</char> you shall say to them, ‘Thus says the Lord YHWH!’—The one hearing, let him hear, and the one refusing, let him refuse. For they <char style="add">are</char> a house of rebellion. <verse eid="EZK 3:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="EZK 4"/>

<para style="s">A Sign of Jerusalem’s Siege</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 4:1"/><char style="add">“</char> And You, son of man, take for yourself a clay tablet, and place it before your face; and engrave upon it a city, Jerusalem. <verse eid="EZK 4:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 4:2"/>And you shall place against it a siege, and build against it a siege wall, and heap up against it a mound, and set against it camps, and set against it battering rams all around. <verse eid="EZK 4:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 4:3"/>And you, take for yourself a plate of iron and set it up <char style="add">as</char> a wall of iron between you and between the city, and set firm your face against it; and it shall come to be under siege, and you shall lay siege against it. This <char style="add">is</char> a sign for the house of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 4:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 4:4"/>And you, lie down upon your left side, and set the iniquity of the house of Israel upon it—for the number of the days that you lay down on it, you shall bear their iniquity. <verse eid="EZK 4:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 4:5"/>For I have given to you the years of their iniquity according to the number of the days—three hundred and ninety days. And you shall bear the iniquity of the house of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 4:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 4:6"/>And you shall complete these, and you shall lie down on your right side <char style="add">this</char> second <char style="add">time</char>, and you shall bear the iniquity of the house of Judah forty days—a day for a year. A day for a year I have given for you. <verse eid="EZK 4:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 4:7"/>And toward the siege of Jerusalem you shall set firm your face, and <char style="add">with</char> your arm uncovered, and you shall prophesy against it. <verse eid="EZK 4:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 4:8"/>And behold, I will lay upon you cords so that you cannot turn yourself over from one side to another, until your completing the days of your siege. <verse eid="EZK 4:8"/></para>

<para style="s">The Defiled Bread</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 4:9"/>And you, take for yourself wheat, and barley, and beans, and lentils, and millet, and spelt, and give them into a single vessel, and make <char style="add">from</char> them for yourself bread. The number of the days that you are laying down on your side—three hundred and ninety days—you shall eat it. <verse eid="EZK 4:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 4:10"/>And your food that you eat <char style="add">is</char> by weight twenty shekels<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">20 shekels</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 8 ounces or 228 grams of food.</char></note> for a day; from time until time you shall eat it. <verse eid="EZK 4:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 4:11"/>And you shall drink water by measure, a sixth of a hin;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A sixth of a hin</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 0.65 quarts or 0.61 liters of water.</char></note> from time until time you shall drink <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="EZK 4:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 4:12"/>And a cake of barley you shall eat it, and with the dung of the excrement of a human you shall bake it before their eyes.” <verse eid="EZK 4:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 4:13"/>And YHWH said: “So the sons of Israel shall eat their defiled bread among the Gentiles, to which I will drive them there.” <verse eid="EZK 4:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 4:14"/>And I said, “Ah, Lord YHWH! Behold, never has my soul been defiled. And carcass and torn thing I have not eaten from my youth until now, and unclean flesh has not come into my mouth.” <verse eid="EZK 4:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 4:15"/>And He said to me: “See, I am giving to you dung of a cow instead of dung of human, and you shall make your bread over it.” <verse eid="EZK 4:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 4:16"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, behold, I am going to cut off the staff<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">supply</char></note> of bread in Jerusalem, and they will eat bread by weight and with anxiety, and they will drink water by measure and with dread, <verse eid="EZK 4:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 4:17"/>so that they lack bread and water, and they be dismayed, a man and his brother, and waste away in their iniquity! <verse eid="EZK 4:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 4"/>

<chapter number="5" style="c" sid="EZK 5"/>

<para style="s">The Razor of Judgment</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 5:1"/><char style="add">“</char> And you, son of man, take for yourself a sharp sword; the razor of a barber take it to yourself and pass <char style="add">it</char> over your head and over your beard; take for yourself scales of weighing, and you shall divide the hair. <verse eid="EZK 5:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 5:2"/>A third with fire you shall burn in the midst of the city at the completion of the days of the siege; and you shall take a third and strike <char style="add">it</char> with the sword around <char style="add">it</char>; and a third you shall scatter to the wind; and I will unsheathe a sword after them. <verse eid="EZK 5:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 5:3"/>And you shall take from them a few in number, and you shall bind them in your skirts. <verse eid="EZK 5:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 5:4"/>And some of them you shall take again and cast them into the midst of the fire, and you shall burn them in the fire; from there will go out a fire into all the house of Israel! <verse eid="EZK 5:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 5:5"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘This <char style="add">is</char> Jerusalem; in the midst of the nations I have set her, and all around her the countries. <verse eid="EZK 5:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 5:6"/>And she has rebelled against My ordinances for wickedness more than the nations, and against My statutes more than the countries that <char style="add">are</char> around her—for My ordinances they have refused, and My statutes, they have not walked in them!’ <verse eid="EZK 5:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 5:7"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because of your⁺ turbulence above the nations that <char style="add">are</char> around you⁺, in My statutes you⁺ have not walked, and My ordinances you⁺ have not done—nor have you⁺ done<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">you have even done</char></note>’ according to the ordinances of the nations that <char style="add">are</char> around you⁺! <verse eid="EZK 5:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 5:8"/>Therefore thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you—even I! And I will do in your midst judgments in the eyes of the nations; <verse eid="EZK 5:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 5:9"/>and I will do among you what I have not done, and that which I will do not like it again, because of all your abominations! <verse eid="EZK 5:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 5:10"/>Therefore fathers shall eat the sons in your midst, and sons shall eat their fathers; and I will execute on you judgments, and I will scatter all your remnant to every wind.’ <verse eid="EZK 5:10"/></para>

<para style="s">Famine, Sword, and Dispersion</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 5:11"/>Therefore, <char style="add">by</char> the life of Me—a declaration of the Lord YHWH—surely because you have defiled My sanctuary with all your detestable things and with all your abominations, My eye will not at all show pity, and I also will not have pity, and I—I will diminish <char style="add">you</char>! <verse eid="EZK 5:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 5:12"/>A third of you—they will die by pestilence and they will be consumed by famine in your midst; and a third will fall by the sword all around you; and a third I will scatter to all the winds and I will unsheath a sword after them! <verse eid="EZK 5:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 5:13"/>And My nose shall be completed and My fury I will cause to rest upon them, and I will be avenged; and they will know that I, YHWH, have spoken <char style="add">it</char> in My zeal, in my completing My fury against them! <verse eid="EZK 5:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 5:14"/>And I will make you a desolation and a reproach among the nations that <char style="add">are</char> around you, before the eyes of everyone passing by. <verse eid="EZK 5:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 5:15"/>And you will be<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> DSS, LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And it will be</char></note> a reproach and a taunt, a warning and a horror to the nations that <char style="add">are</char> around you, in my making against you judgments in anger and in fury and with rebukes of fury—I, YHWH, have spoken— <verse eid="EZK 5:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 5:16"/>in my sending against them the evil arrows of famine, which shall be for destruction, which I will send to destroy you⁺; and the famine I am adding upon you⁺, and I will cut off unto you⁺ the staff<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">supply</char></note> of bread. <verse eid="EZK 5:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 5:17"/>And I will send against you⁺ famine and evil beasts, and they will bereave you; and pestilence and blood will pass through you, and the sword I will bring upon you!—I, YHWH, have spoken.” <verse eid="EZK 5:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 5"/>

<chapter number="6" style="c" sid="EZK 6"/>

<para style="s">Judgment against Idolatry</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 6:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Deuteronomy 12:29–32</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Deuteronomy 4:15–31</char></note>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 6:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 6:2"/>“Son of man, set your face toward the mountains of Israel, and prophesy against them, <verse eid="EZK 6:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 6:3"/>and say: ‘O mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord YHWH! Thus says the Lord YHWH to the mountains, and to the hills, to the ravines, and to the valleys: Behold, I—I am bringing against you⁺ a sword, and I will destroy your⁺ high places. <verse eid="EZK 6:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 6:4"/>And your⁺ altars will be desolate, and your⁺ incense altars will be broken; and your⁺ slain I will cast down before your⁺ idols. <verse eid="EZK 6:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 6:5"/>And I will lay the corpses of the sons of Israel before their idols, and I will scatter your⁺ bones all around your⁺ altars. <verse eid="EZK 6:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 6:6"/>In all your⁺ dwelling places the cities will be laid waste, and the high places will be made desolate, so that your⁺ altars may be destroyed and made desolate, and your⁺ idols may be broken and made to cease, and your⁺ incense altars may be cut down, and your⁺ works may be blotted out! <verse eid="EZK 6:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 6:7"/>And the slain will fall in your⁺ midst, and you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 6:7"/></para>

<para style="s">A Remnant to Be Blessed</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 6:8"/>And I will leave a remnant, in their being unto you⁺ escapees of the sword among the nations, in your⁺ being scattered in the lands. <verse eid="EZK 6:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 6:9"/>And your⁺ escapees will remember Me in the nations to which they are carried captive there, how I was broken by their prostituting heart that turned away from Me, and by their eyes seeking prostitution after their idols; and they will be loathsome in their own sight for the evils that they did by all their abominations. <verse eid="EZK 6:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 6:10"/>And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. Not in vain have I spoken that I would bring upon them this evil! <verse eid="EZK 6:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 6:11"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: Strike with your hand, and stomp with your foot, and say, “Ah!” For all the evils of the abominations of the house of Israel! For by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence they will fall! <verse eid="EZK 6:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 6:12"/>The one far off will die by the pestilence, and the one near will fall by the sword, and he who remains and is besieged will die by the famine. And I will complete My fury upon them. <verse eid="EZK 6:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 6:13"/>And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, in the coming of their slain into the midst of their idols, all around their altars, at every high hill, on all the tops of the mountains, and under every green tree, and under every thick oak—<char style="add">each</char> place that they gave there a pleasing aroma to all their idols. <verse eid="EZK 6:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 6:14"/>And I will stretch out My hand against them, and I will make the land a desolation and a wasteland, from the wilderness to Diblah,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Most Hebrew manuscripts; Vulgate and a few Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Riblah</char></note> in all their dwelling places. And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH!’” <verse eid="EZK 6:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 6"/>

<chapter number="7" style="c" sid="EZK 7"/>

<para style="s">The Hour of Doom</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 7:1"/>And came to be the word of YHWH to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 7:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 7:2"/>“And you, son of man, thus says the Lord YHWH to the land of Israel, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:2">‘An end has come, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:2">the end upon the four corners of the land! <verse eid="EZK 7:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 7:3"/>Now the end <char style="add">is</char> upon you—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:3">and I will send My nose against you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:3">and I will judge you according to your ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:3">and I will recompense upon you all your abominations! <verse eid="EZK 7:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 7:4"/>And My eye will not have pity on you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:4">and I will not have pity; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:4">for your ways I will recompense against you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:4">and for your abominations <char style="add">that</char> are in your midst. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:4">And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 7:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 7:5"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:5">‘Disaster! A unique disaster!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">An unprecedented disaster</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, as in most Hebrew manuscripts; some Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Disaster after disaster</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:5">Behold, it is coming! <verse eid="EZK 7:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 7:6"/>An end has come; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:6">the end has come! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:6">It has roused itself against you. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:6">Behold, it is coming. <verse eid="EZK 7:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 7:7"/>Doom has come to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:7">O dweller of the land; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:7">the time has come, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:7">the day <char style="add">is</char> near—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:7">of tumult, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:7">and not of rejoicing in the mountains! <verse eid="EZK 7:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 7:8"/>Now soon I will pour out My fury upon you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:8">and will complete My anger My anger; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:8">and I will judge you according to your ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:8">and I will recompense upon you for all your abominations. <verse eid="EZK 7:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 7:9"/>And My eye will not have pity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:9">and I will not have pity; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:9">according to your ways I will recompense upon you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:9">and your abominations will be in your midst. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:9">And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:9">the One striking. <verse eid="EZK 7:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 7:10"/>Behold, the day! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:10">Behold, it is coming! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:10">The doom has gone forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:10">the rod has blossomed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:10">the arrogance has budded. <verse eid="EZK 7:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 7:11"/>Violence has risen up </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:11">into a rod of wickedness—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:11">none of them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:11">and none of their multitude, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:11">and none of their wealth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:11">and nothing of eminence among them. <verse eid="EZK 7:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 7:12"/>The time has come, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:12">the day has drawn near! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:12">Let the buyer not rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:12">and let the seller not mourn; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:12">for wrath <char style="add">is</char> upon all their multitude. <verse eid="EZK 7:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 7:13"/>For the one selling will not return to what has been sold </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:13">while they live their life; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:13">for the vision <char style="add">is</char> to the whole multitude, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:13"><char style="add">and</char> it will not turn back; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:13">and a man cannot by his iniquity </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:13">strengthen his life. <verse eid="EZK 7:13"/></para>

<para style="s">The Desolation of Israel</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 7:14"/>They have blown on the trumpet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:14">and made ready everything; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:14">and there is not one going to the battle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:14">for My wrath <char style="add">is</char> against all their multitude. <verse eid="EZK 7:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 7:15"/>The sword <char style="add">is</char> is outside, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:15">and pestilence and famine inside the house. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:15">The one who <char style="add">is</char> in the field will die by the sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:15">and the one who <char style="add">is</char> in the city, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:15">famine and pestilence will devour him. <verse eid="EZK 7:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 7:16"/>And their fugatives will escape, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:16">and they will be on the mountains like doves of the valleys, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:16">all of them mourning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:16">each one for his iniquity. <verse eid="EZK 7:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 7:17"/>Every hand will go limp, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:17">and every knee will go as waters. <verse eid="EZK 7:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 7:18"/>And they will be girded with sackcloth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:18">and shuddering will cover them; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:18">and on every face <char style="add">is</char> shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:18">and on all their heads baldness. <verse eid="EZK 7:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 7:19"/>Their silver they will throw into the streets, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">and their gold will become like refuse; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:19">their silver and their gold will not be able to deliver them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">on the day of the wrath of YHWH. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:19">Their souls they cannot satisfy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">and their stomachs they cannot fill, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:19">for a stumbling block </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:19">their iniquity has become. <verse eid="EZK 7:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 7:20"/>And the beauty of His ornament, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:20">in majesty he set it, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:20">and the images of their abominations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:20">their detestable things they made with it. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:20">Upon thus </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:20">I have made it for them like refuse. <verse eid="EZK 7:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 7:21"/>And I will give it into the hands </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:21">of strangers as plunder, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:21">and to the wicked of the earth as spoil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:21">and they will defile it. <verse eid="EZK 7:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 7:22"/>And I will turn away My face from them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:22">and they will defile My treasured place—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:22">and robbers will come into it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:22">and they will defile it! <verse eid="EZK 7:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 7:23"/>Make a chain! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:23">For the land is filled with with the judgment of blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:23">and the city is full of violence. <verse eid="EZK 7:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 7:24"/>And I will bring the evil of the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:24">and they will possess their houses; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:24">and I will cause to cease the pride of the strong, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:24">and their holy places will be defiled. <verse eid="EZK 7:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 7:25"/>Anguish comes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:25">and they will seek peace and <char style="add">there is</char> none. <verse eid="EZK 7:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 7:26"/>Disaster upon disaster will come, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:26">and rumor will be upon rumor; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:26">and they will seek a vision from a prophet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:26">and the law will perish from the priest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:26">and counsel from the elders. <verse eid="EZK 7:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 7:27"/>The king will mourn, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:27">and the prince will be clothed with desolation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:27">and the hands of the people of the land will tremble; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:27">according to their own way I will deal with them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 7:27">and by their own judgment I will judge them; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 7:27">and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 7:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 7"/>

<chapter number="8" style="c" sid="EZK 8"/>

<para style="s">The Vision of Idolatry in the Temple</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 8:1"/>And it came to pass in the sixth year, in the sixth <char style="add">month</char>, on the fifth of the month, <char style="add">that</char> I was sitting in my house, and the elders of Judah were sitting before me, and fell upon me there the hand of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 8:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 8:2"/>And I looked, and behold, a likeness as the appearance of fire; from the appearance of His loins and downward <char style="add">was</char> fire, and from His loins and above <char style="add">was</char> like the appearance of brightness, like the color of amber.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as glowing metal</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 8:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 8:3"/>And He sent out the form of a hand, and He took me by a lock of my hair; and the Spirit lifted up me between the earth and between the heavens, and brought me to Jerusalem in visions of God, to the door of the inner gate facing north, where <char style="add">was</char> the seat of the image of jealousy which provokes to jealousy. <verse eid="EZK 8:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 8:4"/>And behold, there <char style="add">was</char> the glory of the God of Israel, according to the vision that I had seen in the plain. <verse eid="EZK 8:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 8:5"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, lift up now your eyes <char style="add">to</char> the way northward.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 8:5">And I lifted my eyes <char style="add">to</char> the way northward, and behold! From the north of the Gate of the Altar<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the gate of the altar</char></note> <char style="add">was</char> this image of jealousy in the entrance. <verse eid="EZK 8:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 8:6"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, are you seeing what <char style="add">they</char> are doing? The great abominations that the house of Israel is doing here to keep Me far off from My sanctuary? And still you will turn <char style="add">and</char> you will see greater abominations!” <verse eid="EZK 8:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 8:7"/>And He brought me to the door of the court; and I looked, and behold, one hole in the wall. <verse eid="EZK 8:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 8:8"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, dig now into the wall.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 8:8">And I dug into the wall, and behold, one opening. <verse eid="EZK 8:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 8:9"/>And He said to me: “Go in and see the evil abominations that they are doing here!” <verse eid="EZK 8:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 8:10"/>And I went in and saw. And behold, every manner of creeping thing and detestable beast, and all the idols of the house of Israel were engraved on the walls all around, <verse eid="EZK 8:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 8:11"/>and seventy men from the elders of the house of Israel—and Jaazaniah son of Shaphan standing in their midst—standing before them; and each man his censer in his hand, and the fragrance of a cloud of incense was rising up. <verse eid="EZK 8:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 8:12"/>And He said to me: “Have you seen, Son of man, that which the elders of the house of Israel are doing in the dark, each man in the inner chambers of his imagery? For they say, ‘YHWH <char style="add">is</char> not seeing us, <char style="add">for</char> YHWH has forsaken the land.’” <verse eid="EZK 8:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 8:13"/>And He said to me: “Again you will turn <char style="add">and</char> will see greater abominations that they are doing!” <verse eid="EZK 8:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 8:14"/>And He brought me to the entrance of the gate of the house of YHWH that <char style="add">was</char> toward the north, and behold, there the women were sitting <char style="add">and</char> weeping <char style="add">for</char> Tammuz.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Tammuz</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, meaning </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Sprout of Life</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, was a Sumerian god of fertility.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 8:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 8:15"/>And He said to me: “Have you seen, son of man? Again you will turn <char style="add">and</char> will see greater abominations than these!” <verse eid="EZK 8:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 8:16"/>And He brought me into the inner court of the house of YHWH, and behold, at the opening of the temple of YHWH, between the porch and between the altar, <char style="add">were</char> about twenty-five men with their backs toward the temple of YHWH and <char style="add">with</char> their faces toward the east; and they were worshiping eastward to the sun. <verse eid="EZK 8:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 8:17"/>And He said to me: “Have you seen, son of man? Is it a light thing for the house of Judah to do the abominations that they do here, that they should fill the land <char style="add">with</char> violence and turn back to provoke Me to anger? For behold, they are sending the branch to their nose! <verse eid="EZK 8:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 8:18"/>I also will act in fury. My eye will not show pity, and I will not have pity, and though they cry into My ears <char style="add">in</char> a great voice, not at all will I hear them!” <verse eid="EZK 8:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 8"/>

<chapter number="9" style="c" sid="EZK 9"/>

<para style="s">Execution of the Idolaters</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 9:1"/>And He called out in my ears <char style="add">in</char> a great voice, saying: “Let come near those appointed to deal <char style="add">with</char> the city, and each man <char style="add">with</char> a weapon of destruction in his hand.” <verse eid="EZK 9:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 9:2"/>And behold, six men, each man coming from the way of the upper gate that is facing to the north, and a man <char style="add">with</char> the weapon of slaughter in his hand; and one in their midst clothed with linen, and the inkhorn of a scribe at his side. And they went in and stood beside the altar of bronze. <verse eid="EZK 9:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 9:3"/>And the glory of the God of Israel had gone up from the cherub, where it had been upon it, to the threshold of the temple. And He called to the man clothed in linen, who <char style="add">had</char> the inkhorn of a scribe at his side; <verse eid="EZK 9:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 9:4"/>and YHWH said to him: “Pass over in the midst of the city, in the midst of Jerusalem, and mark a mark upon the foreheads of the men, those sighing and those groaning over all the abominations that are being done in its midst.” <verse eid="EZK 9:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 9:5"/>And to these <char style="add">others</char> He said in my ears: “Pass over in the city after him, and strike! Do not let your⁺ eye show pity, and you⁺ shall not have pity. <verse eid="EZK 9:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 9:6"/>Aged, young man, and maidens, and little children, and women you⁺ will slay to destruction; and upon every man, upon him who <char style="add">has</char> the mark, you⁺ will not come near. And at My sanctuary you⁺ will begin!” </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 9:6">And they began with the elder men who <char style="add">were</char> before the face of the house. <verse eid="EZK 9:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 9:7"/>And He said to them: “Defile the house and fill the courts <char style="add">with</char> the slain! Go forth!” </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 9:7">And they went forth, and they struck in the city. <verse eid="EZK 9:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 9:8"/>And it came to pass in their striking, that I was left, and I fell on my face and cried out and said: “Ah, Lord YHWH! Are You going to destroy all the remnant of Israel in Your pouring out Your fury upon Jerusalem?” <verse eid="EZK 9:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 9:9"/>And He said to me: “The iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah <char style="add">is</char> great exceedingly greatly, and the land is full of blood, and the city is full of perversity; for they say, ‘YHWH has forsaken the land, and YHWH is not seeing!’ <verse eid="EZK 9:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 9:10"/>And I also—My eye will not show pity, and I will not have pity, their deeds on their own head I have put!” <verse eid="EZK 9:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 9:11"/>And, behold, the man clothed in linen, who <char style="add">had</char> at his side the inkhorn, was returning word, saying: “I have done according to that which You commanded me.” <verse eid="EZK 9:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 9"/>

<chapter number="10" style="c" sid="EZK 10"/>

<para style="s">God’s Glory Exits the Temple</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 10:1"/>And I looked, and behold, at the firmament that <char style="add">was</char> over the head of the cherubim <char style="add">was</char> like a stone of sapphire, as the appearance of the likeness of a throne, was seen above them. <verse eid="EZK 10:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 10:2"/>And He spoke to the man clothed in linen, and He said: “Go to the midst of the wheel, to beneath the cherub, and fill your hands with coals of fire from between the cherubim, and scatter <char style="add">them</char> over the city!” And he went <char style="add">in</char> before my eyes. <verse eid="EZK 10:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 10:3"/>And the cherubim were standing on the south side of the house, at the going in of the man, and the cloud filled the inner court. <verse eid="EZK 10:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 10:4"/>And the glory of YHWH went up from the cherub, over the threshold of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was filled with the brightness of the glory of YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 10:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 10:5"/>And the voice of the wings of the cherubim was heard as far as the outer court, like the voice of El-Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">El-Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God Almighty</char></note> in His speaking. <verse eid="EZK 10:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 10:6"/>And it came to pass in His commanding the man clothed in linen, saying, “Take fire from between the wheels, from between the cherubim,” that he went in and stood beside a wheel. <verse eid="EZK 10:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 10:7"/>And the cherub sent forth his hand from between the cherubim to the fire that <char style="add">was</char> between the cherubim, and he took and put <char style="add">it</char> into the hands of the one clothed in linen, and he took <char style="add">it</char> and went out. <verse eid="EZK 10:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 10:8"/>(And was seen unto the cherubim the form of the hand of a man under their wings.) <verse eid="EZK 10:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 10:9"/>And I looked, and behold, four wheels beside the cherubim, one wheel beside the one cherub, and one wheel beside the one cherub; and the appearance of the wheels <char style="add">was</char> like the eye of a stone of beryl. <verse eid="EZK 10:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 10:10"/>And their appearance <char style="add">was</char> one likeness unto four of them, as <char style="add">if</char> it were a wheel in the midst of the wheel. <verse eid="EZK 10:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 10:11"/>In their going toward four directions, they did go; they did not turn aside in their going; for the place where the head turned, toward it they would go; they did not turn aside In their going. <verse eid="EZK 10:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 10:12"/>And all of their body—their rims, and their hands, and their wings, and the wheels, <char style="add">were</char> full of eyes all around, wheels as their four. <verse eid="EZK 10:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 10:13"/>The wheels, unto them it was called in my ears, “The whirling wheels.” <verse eid="EZK 10:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 10:14"/>And four faces <char style="add">were</char> unto each one: The face of the first <char style="add">was</char> the face of a cherub, and the face of the second <char style="add">was</char> the face of a man, and the face of the third a lion, and the face of the fourth an eagle. <verse eid="EZK 10:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 10:15"/>And the cherubim rose upward. This <char style="add">was</char> the living creature that I saw by the River Chebar. <verse eid="EZK 10:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 10:16"/>And in the going of the cherubim, the wheels went beside them; and the cherubim, in the lifting up of their wings, rose up from the earth, <char style="add">and</char> the wheels did not turn, also they <char style="add">were</char> beside them. <verse eid="EZK 10:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 10:17"/>In their standing still and in their rising up <char style="add">they</char> were raised up with them, for the spirit of the living creature <char style="add">was</char> in them. <verse eid="EZK 10:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 10:18"/>And went out the glory of YHWH from upon the threshold of the house, and it stood over the cherubim. <verse eid="EZK 10:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 10:19"/>And the cherubim lifted up their wings, and they were raised up from the earth before my eyes; and in their going out, also <char style="add">were</char> the wheels beside them. And they stood <char style="add">at</char> the entrance of the gate of the house of YHWH <char style="add">in</char> the east, and the glory of the God of Israel <char style="add">was</char> over them from above. <verse eid="EZK 10:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 10:20"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the living creature that I saw under the God of Israel by the River Kebar; and I knew that they <char style="add">were</char> cherubim. <verse eid="EZK 10:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 10:21"/>Four—four faces <char style="add">were</char> unto each one, and four wings unto each one, and the likeness of the hands of a man <char style="add">was</char> under their wings. <verse eid="EZK 10:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 10:22"/>And the likeness of their faces, they <char style="add">were</char> the faces that I had seen by the River Kebar, their appearances and themselves. Each one to straight ahead of its face they would go. <verse eid="EZK 10:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 10"/>

<chapter number="11" style="c" sid="EZK 11"/>

<para style="s">Evil in High Places</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 11:1"/>And the Spirit lifted me up and brought me to the east gate of the house of YHWH, facing eastward. And behold, at the entrance of the gate <char style="add">were</char> twenty-five men, and I saw in their midst Jaazaniah son of Azzur, and Pelatiah son of Benaiah, princes of the people. <verse eid="EZK 11:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 11:2"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, these <char style="add">are</char> the men devising iniquity and counseling evil counsel in this city, <verse eid="EZK 11:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 11:3"/>those saying, ‘<char style="add">It is</char> not near <char style="add">for</char> building houses? She <char style="add">is</char> the pot,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">cauldron</char></note> and we <char style="add">are</char> the meat!’ <verse eid="EZK 11:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 11:4"/>Therefore prophesy against them; prophesy, O son of man.” <verse eid="EZK 11:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 11:5"/>And fell upon me the Spirit of YHWH, and He said to me, “Say, thus says YHWH: Thus you⁺ have said, O house of Israel—and the <char style="add">things</char> coming upon your⁺ spirit I know. <verse eid="EZK 11:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 11:6"/>You⁺ have multiplied your⁺ slain in this city, and its streets you⁺ have filled <char style="add">with</char> the slain. <verse eid="EZK 11:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 11:7"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: Your⁺ slain that you⁺ have set in its midst, they <char style="add">are</char> the flesh, and she <char style="add">is</char> the pot; and you⁺ will be brought out from her midst. <verse eid="EZK 11:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 11:8"/>The sword you⁺ have feared, and the sword I will bring upon you⁺, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 11:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 11:9"/>And I will bring you⁺ out from her midst, and I will give you⁺ into the hands of strangers, and I will execute judgments against you⁺. <verse eid="EZK 11:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 11:10"/>By the sword you⁺ will fall, <char style="add">and</char> at the border of Israel I will judge you⁺. And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 11:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 11:11"/>She will not be a pot for you⁺, <char style="add">nor</char> will you⁺ be in her midst as meat; at the border of Israel I will judge you⁺, <verse eid="EZK 11:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 11:12"/>and you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. For in My statutes you⁺ have not walked, and My ordinances you⁺ have not done, and according to the ordinances of the nations that <char style="add">are</char> around you⁺ you⁺ have done.” <verse eid="EZK 11:12"/></para>

<para style="s">A Promise of RestorationJeremiah 32:36–44</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 11:13"/>And it came to pass in my prophesying that Pelatiah son of Benaiah died. And I fell on my face and cried out <char style="add">in</char> a great voice, and said: “Ah, Lord YHWH! <char style="add">Are</char> You going to make to a complete end of the remnant of Israel?” <verse eid="EZK 11:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 11:14"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 11:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 11:15"/>“Son of man, your brothers, your relatives, the men of your kindred, and all the house of Israel—all of it, <char style="add">are</char> those whom those dwelling in Jerusalem have said to them, ‘Get far away from YHWH; this land has been given to us as a possession.’ <verse eid="EZK 11:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 11:16"/>Therefore say, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Although I have set them far away among the nations, and although I have scattered them among the lands, I have been for them for a little while a sanctuary in the lands to which they have gone there.’ <verse eid="EZK 11:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 11:17"/>Therefore say, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘And I will gather you⁺ from the peoples, and will assemble you⁺ from the lands to which you⁺ have been scattered in them, and I will give to you⁺ the land of Israel.’ <verse eid="EZK 11:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 11:18"/>And they will go there, and they will turn aside all her detestable <char style="add">things</char> and all her abominations from her. <verse eid="EZK 11:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 11:19"/>And I will give to them a single heart, and I will give a new spirit within them; and I will turn away the heart of stone from their flesh, and I will give to them a heart of flesh, <verse eid="EZK 11:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 11:20"/>so that they may walk in My statutes and they may keep My ordinances and may do them; and they will be unto Me for a people, and I will be unto them God. <verse eid="EZK 11:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 11:21"/>And to those whose heart their detestable <char style="add">things</char> and whose heart their abominations is going after, their deeds I will recompense upon their own heads! An utterance of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 11:21"/></para>

<para style="s">God’s Glory Leaves Jerusalem</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 11:22"/>And the cherubim lifted up their wings, and the wheels <char style="add">were</char> beside them, and the glory of the God of Israel <char style="add">was</char> over them from above. <verse eid="EZK 11:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 11:23"/>And the glory of YHWH went up from the midst of the city, and it stood on the mountain that <char style="add">is</char> on the east of the city. <verse eid="EZK 11:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 11:24"/>And the Spirit lifted me up and brought me to Chaldea,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Babylonia</char></note> to the captivity, in a vision by the Spirit of God; and went up from me the vision that I had seen. <verse eid="EZK 11:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 11:25"/>And I spoke to the captivity all the words of YHWH that He had shown to me. <verse eid="EZK 11:25"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 11"/>

<chapter number="12" style="c" sid="EZK 12"/>

<para style="s">Signs of the Coming Captivity</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 12:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 12:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 12:2"/>“Son of man, you are dwelling in the midst of the house of rebellion, which <char style="add">has</char> eyes unto them to see, and they do not see, and ears unto them to hear, and they do not hear; for they <char style="add">are</char> a house of rebellion! <verse eid="EZK 12:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 12:3"/>And you, son of man, take up for yourself vessels for exile, and go into exile by day before their eyes; and you will go into exile from your place to another place before their eyes. Perhaps they will see, though they <char style="add">are</char> a house of rebellion. <verse eid="EZK 12:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 12:4"/>And you shall bring out your vessels like vessels for exile by day before their eyes, and you shall go out in the evening before their eyes, like those going into captivity. <verse eid="EZK 12:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 12:5"/>Before their eyes you shall dig for yourself through the wall, and go out through it. <verse eid="EZK 12:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 12:6"/>Before their eyes, you shall bear <char style="add">them</char> on <char style="add">your</char> shoulders in the darkness <char style="add">and</char> carry <char style="add">them</char> out; you shall cover your face so that you cannot see the land, for I have given you as a sign for the house of Israel.” <verse eid="EZK 12:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 12:7"/>And I did just as I was commanded. My vessels I brought out as vessels for captivity by day, and in the evening I dug for myself through the wall with <char style="add">my</char> hand; in the darkness I brought <char style="add">them</char> out on <char style="add">my</char> shoulder, I bore <char style="add">them</char> before their eyes. <verse eid="EZK 12:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 12:8"/>And the word of YHWH came to me in the morning, saying: <verse eid="EZK 12:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 12:9"/>“Son of man, have they not said to you—the house of Israel, <char style="add">this</char> house of rebellion, ‘What <char style="add">are</char> you doing?’ <verse eid="EZK 12:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 12:10"/>Say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘This burden <char style="add">concerns</char> the prince in Jerusalem, and all the house of Israel who are in their midst.’ <verse eid="EZK 12:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 12:11"/>Say, ‘I <char style="add">am</char> a sign to you⁺.’ As I have done, so will it be done to them—into exile, into captivity, they will go! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some translators close the quotation at the end of the verse.</char></note><verse eid="EZK 12:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 12:12"/>And the prince who <char style="add">is</char> in their midst, on <char style="add">his</char> shoulder he will bear <char style="add">it</char> in the darkness, and he will go out; they will dig through the wall to bring <char style="add">them</char> out through it; he will cover his face so that he might not see with <char style="add">his</char> eyes, he, the land. <verse eid="EZK 12:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 12:13"/>And I will spread My net over him, and he will be caught in My snare; and I will bring him to Babylon, <char style="add">to</char> the land of the Chaldeans; and he will not see it, and there he will die. <verse eid="EZK 12:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 12:14"/>And all who <char style="add">are</char> around him <char style="add">as</char> his help, and all his troops, I will scatter to every wind, and I will unsheath the sword after them. <verse eid="EZK 12:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 12:15"/>And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, in My dispersing them among the nations and scattering them throughout the lands. <verse eid="EZK 12:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 12:16"/>I will spare from their people a few—from the sword, from famine, and from pestilence—so that they may recount all their abominations among the nations to which they go there. And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 12:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 12:17"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 12:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 12:18"/>“Son of man, eat your bread with quaking, and drink your water with trembling and with anxiety! <verse eid="EZK 12:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 12:19"/>And say to the people of the land, thus says the Lord YHWH to those dwelling in Jerusalem, <char style="add">and</char> to the land of Israel: ‘They will eat their bread with anxiety, and they will drink their water with dread, so that her land may be emptied of all her fullness, because of the violence of all those dwelling in her. <verse eid="EZK 12:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 12:20"/>And the cities that <char style="add">were</char> inhabited will be dried up, and the land will become a desolation; and you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH!’” <verse eid="EZK 12:20"/></para>

<para style="s">The Presumptuous Proverb</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 12:21"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 12:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 12:22"/>“Son of man, what <char style="add">is</char> this proverb for you⁺ over the land of Israel, saying, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 12:22">‘The days are prolonged, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 12:22">and every vision perishes’? <verse eid="EZK 12:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 12:23"/>Therefore say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘To this proverb I will put an end, and will they use it as a proverb no more in Israel. But rather speak to them: ‘The days are near, and the word of every vision!’ <verse eid="EZK 12:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 12:24"/>For there will be no longer any vision of emptiness, or of smooth divination, in the midst of the house of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 12:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 12:25"/>For I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH! I speak, and the word that I speak will come to pass; it will not drag out any longer, but in your⁺ days, O house of rebellion, I will speak the word and will do it! An utterance of the Lord YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 12:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 12:26"/>And the word came of YHWH to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 12:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 12:27"/>“Son of man, behold, the house of Israel is saying, ‘The vision that he sees is for many days, and times far off he is prophesying.’ <verse eid="EZK 12:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 12:28"/>Therefore say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Not any of My words will be drawn out anymore; the word that I speak, it will be done! An utterance of the Lord YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 12:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 12"/>

<chapter number="13" style="c" sid="EZK 13"/>

<para style="s">Reproof of False Prophets</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 13:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Micah 2:6–11</char></note>And the word came of YHWH to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 13:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 13:2"/>“Son of man, prophesy against the prophets of Israel, those prophesying, and say to the prophets of their own heart, hear the word of YHWH! <verse eid="EZK 13:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 13:3"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: Woe upon the foolish prophets, who are walking after their own spirit, and have seen nothing! <verse eid="EZK 13:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 13:4"/>Like jackals among the ruins, your prophets, O Israel, have become. <verse eid="EZK 13:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 13:5"/>You⁺ have not gone up into the breaches, and walled up the wall around the house of Israel to stand in the battle on the day of YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 13:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 13:6"/>They have seen emptiness and lying divination, saying, ‘Thus says YWHW…,’ and YHWH has not sent them; and they hope to establish <char style="add">their</char> word. <verse eid="EZK 13:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 13:7"/>Have you⁺ not seen a vision of emptiness and spoken a lying divination? You say, ‘An utterance of YHWH…,’ and I have not spoken. <verse eid="EZK 13:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 13:8"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: Because you⁺ have spoken emptiness, and seen a lie, therefore behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you⁺! An utterance of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 13:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 13:9"/>And My hand will be against the prophets who are seeing emptiness, and who divine a lie; they will not belong in the assembly of My people, and in the register of the house of Israel they will not be written, and into the land of Israel they will not come. And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 13:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 13:10"/>Because, even because they have led My people astray, saying, ‘Peace!’ When <char style="add">there is</char> no peace, and one is building a wall, and behold them, they plaster it <char style="add">with</char> whitewash, <verse eid="EZK 13:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 13:11"/>you will say to those plastering <char style="add">with</char> whitewash that it will fall! There will be an overflowing rain, and you⁺, O stones of hail, will fall, and a wind of tempests will tear <char style="add">it</char> down. <verse eid="EZK 13:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 13:12"/>And behold, when the wall has fallen, it will not be said to you⁺, ‘Where <char style="add">is</char> the whitewash with which you⁺ plastered <char style="add">it</char>?’ <verse eid="EZK 13:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 13:13"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: And I will cause to break forth a wind of tempests in My fury, and an overflowing rain there will be in My anger, and stones of hail in <char style="add">My</char> fury to consume! <verse eid="EZK 13:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 13:14"/>And I will break down the wall that you⁺ have plastered <char style="add">with</char> whitewash, and I will make it touch to the ground, and its foundation will be uncovered, and it will fall, and you⁺ will be finished off in the midst of it. And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 13:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 13:15"/>And will I accomplish My wrath against the wall, and against those plastering it <char style="add">with</char> whitewash; and I will say to you⁺: ‘The wall <char style="add">is</char> no more, and those plastering it <char style="add">are</char> no more— <verse eid="EZK 13:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 13:16"/>the prophets of Israel are prophesying concerning Jerusalem, and seeing for her visions of peace, and <char style="add">there is</char> no peace! An utterance of the Lord YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 13:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Reproof of False Prophetesses</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 13:17"/>And you, O son of man, set your face against the daughters of your people, those prophesying from their own heart, and prophesy against them, <verse eid="EZK 13:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 13:18"/>and say, thus says the Lord YHWH: Woe to those sowing charms on all the wrists of their hands, and making veils for the heads of every height, to hunt <char style="add">for</char> souls! Will you⁺ hunt the souls of My people, and the souls of yourselves keep alive? <verse eid="EZK 13:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 13:19"/>And you⁺ profane Me among My people for handfuls of barley, and for pieces of bread, by putting to death people who should not die, and keeping alive people who should not live, by your⁺ lying to My people who listen to a lie. <verse eid="EZK 13:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 13:20"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against your⁺ charms, by which you⁺ hunt there souls like birds; and I will tear them from your⁺ arms, and I will send away the souls that you⁺ hunt like the souls of birds. <verse eid="EZK 13:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 13:21"/>And I will tear off your⁺ veils, and I will deliver My people from your⁺ hands, and they will be no longer in your⁺ hands as prey! And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 13:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 13:22"/>Because you have disheartened the righteous heart <char style="add">with</char> a lie (when I had not grieved him) and strengthened the hands of the wicked, so as not to turn aside from his evil way to save his life, <verse eid="EZK 13:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 13:23"/>therefore emptiness you⁺ will not see, and divination you⁺ will not divine any longer. And I will deliver My people from your⁺ hands, and you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 13:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 13"/>

<chapter number="14" style="c" sid="EZK 14"/>

<para style="s">Idolatrous Elders Condemned</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 14:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Corinthians 8:1–13</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 14:13–23</char></note>And there came to me <char style="add">some</char> men from the elders of Israel, and they sat before me. <verse eid="EZK 14:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 14:2"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 14:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 14:3"/>“Son of man, these men have set up their idols upon their hearts, and a stumbling block <char style="add">for</char> their iniquity they have put before their faces. Can I be sought out in any way by them? <verse eid="EZK 14:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 14:4"/>Therefore you must speak to them and say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Every man man of the house of Israel who sets up his idols in his heart and puts a stumbling block for his iniquity before his face, and comes to the prophet, I, YHWH, will give answer to him in this, according to the abundance of his idolatry, <verse eid="EZK 14:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 14:5"/>so as to capture the house of Israel by their heart, <char style="add">in</char> that they are estranged from Me by all their idols.’ <verse eid="EZK 14:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 14:6"/>Therefore say to the house of Israel, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Turn back and turn away from your⁺ idols, and from all your⁺ abominations turn back your⁺ faces! <verse eid="EZK 14:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 14:7"/>For every man of the house of Israel, or from the foreigners who dwell in Israel, who separates himself from Me and sets up his idols in his heart, and puts a stumbling block for his iniquity before his face, and who comes to a prophet to inquire of him concerning Me, I, YHWH, will answer him Myself. <verse eid="EZK 14:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 14:8"/>And I will set My face against that man, and I will set him as a sign and a proverb, and I will cut him off from the midst of My people. And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 14:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 14:9"/>And a prophet, if he is led astray and has spoken a word, I, YHWH, have enticed that prophet, and I will stretch out My hand against him, and I will destroy him from the midst of My people Israel. <verse eid="EZK 14:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 14:10"/>And they will bear their guilt. As the guilt of the one inquiring, will be the guilt of the prophet, <verse eid="EZK 14:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 14:11"/>so that the house of Israel they will lead astray no longer from Me, and they will not profane themselves anymore with all their transgressions. And they will be unto Me as a people, and I will be unto them God! An utterance of the Lord YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 14:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Four Dire Judgments</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 14:12"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 14:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 14:13"/>“Son of man, when a land sins against Me to act unfaithfully—an unfaithfulness—and I stretch out My hand against it and cut off for it the staff<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">supply</char></note> of bread, and I send on it famine and I cut off from it man and beast, <verse eid="EZK 14:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 14:14"/>even if these three men were in its midst—Noah, Daniel, and Job—<char style="add">only</char> they by their righteousness would deliver their own soul! An utterance of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 14:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 14:15"/>Or if I cause a wild beast to pass through the land and make it barren and it becomes a desolation, with no one passing through before the face of the beast, <verse eid="EZK 14:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 14:16"/><char style="add">even if</char> these three men <char style="add">were</char> in its midst—<char style="add">as</char> I live, a declaration of the Lord YHWH—neither the sons or daughters they could deliver! They alone would be delivered, and the land would become a desolation. <verse eid="EZK 14:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 14:17"/>Or if I should bring the sword against that land and say, ‘Sword, pass through the land!’ And I cut off from it man and beast, <verse eid="EZK 14:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 14:18"/>even if these three men <char style="add">were</char> in the midst of it—<char style="add">as</char> I live, a declaration of the Lord YHWH—they could not deliver the sons and daughters, but they themselves alone would be delivered. <verse eid="EZK 14:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 14:19"/>Or if I should send a pestilence into that land and pour out My fury on it in blood, and cut off from it man and beast, <verse eid="EZK 14:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 14:20"/>even if Noah, Daniel, and Job <char style="add">were</char> in the midst of it—<char style="add">as</char> I live, a declaration of the Lord YHWH—neither the son <char style="add">nor</char> daughter they could deliver! They by their righteousness would deliver <char style="add">only</char> their own soul. <verse eid="EZK 14:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 14:21"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘How much more when <char style="add">these</char> four of My severe judgments—the sword, and famine, and the wild beast, and the pestilence—I send against Jerusalem, to cut off from it man and beast? <verse eid="EZK 14:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 14:22"/>And behold—there will be left in it a remnant, those being brought out, sons and daughters; behold, they will be coming out to you⁺, and you⁺ will see their ways and their deeds, and you⁺ will be comforted concerning the disaster that I have brought upon Jerusalem—all that I have brought upon it. <verse eid="EZK 14:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 14:23"/>And they will comfort you⁺ when you⁺ see their ways and their deeds, and you⁺ will know that I have not without cause done all that I have done in it!’ An utterance of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 14:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 14"/>

<chapter number="15" style="c" sid="EZK 15"/>

<para style="s">Jerusalem the Useless Vine</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 15:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 15:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 15:2"/>“Son of man, how is the wood of the vine more than any wood, the <char style="add">vine</char> branch that is among the trees of the forest? <verse eid="EZK 15:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 15:3"/>Is wood taken from it it to use for work? Or do they make from it a peg to hang any vessel on it? <verse eid="EZK 15:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 15:4"/>Behold, it is given to the fire for food; the two of its ends the fire devours, and the middle of it is burned. Is it useful for work? <verse eid="EZK 15:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 15:5"/>Behold, in its being complete, it could not be made for work; how much <char style="add">less</char> when the fire has devoured it and it is burned, can it even be made yet for work! <verse eid="EZK 15:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 15:6"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Just like the wood of the vine among the trees of the forest, which I have given to the fire for food, so I have given those dwelling in Jerusalem. <verse eid="EZK 15:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 15:7"/>And I will set My face against them; from the fire they will come out, and the fire will devour them! And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, in My setting My face against them. <verse eid="EZK 15:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 15:8"/>And I will make the land a desolation, because they have acted unfaithfully—an unfaithfulness’—a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 15:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 15"/>

<chapter number="16" style="c" sid="EZK 16"/>

<para style="s">Jerusalem’s Unfaithfulness</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 16:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 16:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 16:2"/>“Son of man, make known <char style="add">to</char> Jerusalem her abominations, <verse eid="EZK 16:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 16:3"/>and say, thus says the Lord YHWH to Jerusalem: Your origin and your birth <char style="add">are</char> from the land of the Canaanite; your father <char style="add">was</char> an Amorite, and your mother a Hittite. <verse eid="EZK 16:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 16:4"/>And of your birth, on the day you were born, your cord was not cut, and you were not washed in water for cleansing, and you were not rubbed with salt, and you were not wrapped in swaddling cloths. <verse eid="EZK 16:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 16:5"/>No eye showed pity to you, to do for you one of these <char style="add">things</char> to have compassion on you, and you were thrown out into the face of the field in the loathing of your soul on the day you were born. <verse eid="EZK 16:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 16:6"/>And I passed by you and saw you wallowing in your own blood, and I said to you in your blood, ‘Live!’ And I said to you in your blood, ‘Live!’ <verse eid="EZK 16:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 16:7"/>I made you a myriad like a plant in the field, and you increased and grew and came into the adornment of adornments. <char style="add">Your</char> breasts were established, and your hair sprouted, and you <char style="add">were</char> naked and bare. <verse eid="EZK 16:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 16:8"/>And I passed by you and I saw you, and behold, your time <char style="add">was</char> the time for love! And I spread My wing over you and covered your nakedness, and I swore an oath to you and came into a covenant with you—a declaration of the Lord YHWH—and you came to be unto Me. <verse eid="EZK 16:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 16:9"/>And I washed you with water, and I rinsed off your blood from you, and I anointed you with the oil. <verse eid="EZK 16:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 16:10"/>And I clothed you in embroidered cloth, and gave you sandals of badger skin, and I tied you in fine linen, and I covered you with silk; <verse eid="EZK 16:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 16:11"/>and I adorned you with ornaments, and I put bracelets on your hands and a chain on your neck. <verse eid="EZK 16:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 16:12"/>And I put a ring upon your nose, and earrings upon your ears, and a crown of beauty upon your head. <verse eid="EZK 16:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 16:13"/>And you were adorned with gold and silver, and your clothing <char style="add">was</char> of fine linen, and silk, and embroidered cloth. Fine flour and honey and oil did you eat. You were exceedingly greatly beautiful, and you advanced to royalty. <verse eid="EZK 16:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 16:14"/>And a name for you went forth among the nations on account of your beauty, for it <char style="add">was</char> perfect in My splendor that I had set upon you, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 16:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 16:15"/>And you trusted in your own beauty, and acted as a prostitute upon your name, and you poured out your prostitution on everyone passing by—it was unto him! <verse eid="EZK 16:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 16:16"/>And you took from your garments and made for yourself multicolored high places, and you prostituted yourself on them—things that should not have happened and should not have come to be! <verse eid="EZK 16:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 16:17"/>And you have taken the articles of your beauty from My gold and from My silver that I had given to you, and you made for yourself images of a male and prostituted yourself with them! <verse eid="EZK 16:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 16:18"/>And you took the garments of your embroidery and covered them, and you set My oil and My incense before their faces; <verse eid="EZK 16:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 16:19"/>and My food that I gave to you—the fine flour, and oil, and honey I fed you—and you set it before their face for a pleasing aroma; and it came to pass! An utterance of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 16:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 16:20"/>And you took your sons and your daughters, those whom you bore to Me, and you sacrificed them to them to be devoured! <char style="add">Was</char> your prostitution too little? <verse eid="EZK 16:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 16:21"/>And you have slain My children, and have given them by causing them to pass through to them! <verse eid="EZK 16:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 16:22"/>And in all your abominations and your prostitutions, you did not remember the days of your youth, in your being naked and bare; you were wallowing in your own blood. <verse eid="EZK 16:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 16:23"/>And it came to pass after all your evil—Woe, woe to you, a declaration of the Lord YHWH— <verse eid="EZK 16:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 16:24"/><char style="add">that</char> you built for yourself a mound and you set for yourself a high place in every public square! <verse eid="EZK 16:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 16:25"/>At every head of the road you built your high places, and you made abhorrent your beauty <char style="add">by</char> your opening your feet to all passing by, and you multiplied your prostitutions! <verse eid="EZK 16:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 16:26"/>And you prostituted yourself with the sons of Egypt, your neighbors, greatly fleshly, and you multiplied your prostitutions to provoke Me to anger. <verse eid="EZK 16:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 16:27"/>And behold, I stretched out My hand against you, and I diminished your portion, and I gave you over to the appetite of those hating you, the daughters of the Philistines, who were ashamed of your way of prostitution. <verse eid="EZK 16:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 16:28"/>And you prostituted yourself with the sons of Assyria from your lack of being satisfied, and you prostituted yourself with them, and still you were not satisfied! <verse eid="EZK 16:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 16:29"/>And you multiplied your prostitutions into the land of the merchants of Chaldea,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Babylonia</char></note> and even in this you were not satisfied. <verse eid="EZK 16:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 16:30"/>How weak is your heart,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">How feverish is your heart,</char></note> a declaration of the Lord YHWH, in your doing all these deeds of an imperious prostitute woman, <verse eid="EZK 16:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 16:31"/>in your building your mounds at the head of every road, and your high place you made in every public square. And you were not even like a prostitute because of your scorning of a prostitute’s payment. <verse eid="EZK 16:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 16:32"/><char style="add">You are</char> the woman committing adultery, <char style="add">who</char> in place of her husband does receive strangers! <verse eid="EZK 16:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 16:33"/>To all prostitutes they give a gift, and you—you gave your gifts to all your lovers and bribed them to come to you from all around in your prostitutions. <verse eid="EZK 16:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 16:34"/>And it is the opposite from <char style="add">other</char> women with you in your prostitution; and no one <char style="add">was</char> after you to be a prostitute, and you gave a wage and a wage was not given to you—you are the opposite! <verse eid="EZK 16:34"/></para>

<para style="s">Judgment on Jerusalem</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 16:35"/>Therefore, O prostitute, hear the word of YHWH! <verse eid="EZK 16:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 16:36"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: Because your lust was poured out, and your nakedness was uncovered in your prostitutions with your lovers and with all the idols of your abominations, and because of the blood of your children, which you gave to them, <verse eid="EZK 16:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 16:37"/>therefore, behold, I will gather all your lovers, with whom you took pleasure, and all those whom you loved, along with all those you hated, and I will gather them against you from all around. And I will uncover your nakedness to them, that they may see all your nakedness. <verse eid="EZK 16:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 16:38"/>And I will judge you <char style="add">with</char> the judgments of those committing adultery and shedding blood, and I will bring upon you the blood of rage and jealousy. <verse eid="EZK 16:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="EZK 16:39"/>And I will give you into their hands, and they will overthrow your shrines, and they will break down your high places, and they will strip you of your clothes and take away the articles of your beauty, and they will leave you naked and bare. <verse eid="EZK 16:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="EZK 16:40"/>And they will bring up an assembly against you, and they will stone you with stones, and they will cut you up with their swords. <verse eid="EZK 16:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="EZK 16:41"/>And they will burn your houses with fire, and they will execute judgment against you before the eyes of many women. And I will put an end to your prostitution, and even a <char style="add">single</char> lover you will not pay again! <verse eid="EZK 16:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="EZK 16:42"/>And I will lay to rest My fury against you, and My jealousy will turn aside from you; and I will be quiet, and I will not be angry anymore. <verse eid="EZK 16:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="EZK 16:43"/>Because that you did not remember the days of your youth, and you caused enragement to Me with all these <char style="add">things</char>, behold, I also, will recompense your way on <char style="add">your</char> head! An utterance of the Lord YHWH. And have you not done this wickedness in addition to all your abominations? <verse eid="EZK 16:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="EZK 16:44"/>Behold everyone quoting proverbs will use <char style="add">this</char> proverb against you, saying, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 16:44">‘Like her mother <char style="add">is</char> her daughter.’ <verse eid="EZK 16:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="EZK 16:45"/>You <char style="add">are</char> the daughter of your mother, loathing her husband and her children; and you <char style="add">are</char> the sister of your sisters, those who loathed their husbands and children! Your⁺ mother <char style="add">was</char> a Hittite and your⁺ father an Amorite. <verse eid="EZK 16:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="EZK 16:46"/>And your elder sister <char style="add">is</char> Samaria, she and her daughters, dwelling to the north of you; and your younger sister, dwelling toyour south, <char style="add">is</char> Sodom and her daughters. <verse eid="EZK 16:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="EZK 16:47"/>And not <char style="add">only</char> in their ways did you walk, and according to their abominations you acted—as if too little—and you became more corrupt than they in all your ways! <verse eid="EZK 16:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="EZK 16:48"/>As I live—a declaration of the Lord YHWH—Sodom your sister has not done, she and her daughters, as you have done—you and your daughters! <verse eid="EZK 16:48"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="EZK 16:49"/>Behold, this was the guilt of Sodom your sister: Pride, fullness of bread, and the ease of idleness was unto her and unto her daughters, and the hand of the poor and needy she did not strengthen. <verse eid="EZK 16:49"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="EZK 16:50"/>And they were haughty, and they did an abomination before My face, and I turned them aside as you have seen.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.50 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> A few Hebrew manuscripts and LXX; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as I have seen</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 16:50"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="EZK 16:51"/>And Samaria, according to the half of your sins, did not sin; and you have multiplied your abominations beyond theirs, and you have justified your sisters in all the abominations that you have done. <verse eid="EZK 16:51"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="EZK 16:52"/>So also you, lift up your own shame, that you have brought justification for your sisters in your sins that you made abhorrent beyond theirs. They are more righteous than you, so you too be disgraced and lift up your own shame in your justifying of your sisters. <verse eid="EZK 16:52"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="EZK 16:53"/>And I will turn back their captivity—the captives of Sodom and her daughters,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.53 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And I will restore the fortunes of Sodom and her daughters</char></note> and the captives of Samaria and her daughters—and the captivity of your captives in their midst, <verse eid="EZK 16:53"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="EZK 16:54"/>so that you may bear your shame and be disgraced by all that you did, in your giving comfort to them. <verse eid="EZK 16:54"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="EZK 16:55"/>And your sisters, Sodom and her daughters, will return to their former state, and Samaria and her daughters will return to their former state, and you and your daughters will return to your⁺ former state. <verse eid="EZK 16:55"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="EZK 16:56"/>Has not your sister Sodom come to be as a byword in your mouth in the days of your pride, <verse eid="EZK 16:56"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="EZK 16:57"/>before your wickedness was uncovered? It is like the time of scorn by the daughters of Edom,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.57 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Many Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Vulgate </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Aram</char></note> and all those around her, and the daughters of the Philistines—those despising you from all around. <verse eid="EZK 16:57"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="EZK 16:58"/>Your wickedness and your abominations you will bear, a declaration of YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 16:58"/></para>

<para style="s">The Covenant Remembered</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="EZK 16:59"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: I will do with you as you have done—those having despised the oath by breaking the covenant. <verse eid="EZK 16:59"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="EZK 16:60"/>And I will remember My covenant with you in the days of your youth, and I will establish with you a covenant forever. <verse eid="EZK 16:60"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="61" style="v" sid="EZK 16:61"/>And you will remember your ways, and you will be ashamed, in your taking your sisters, those older than you to those younger than you, when I give them to you as daughters, and not by your covenant. <verse eid="EZK 16:61"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="62" style="v" sid="EZK 16:62"/>And I will establish My covenant with you, and you will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, <verse eid="EZK 16:62"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="63" style="v" sid="EZK 16:63"/>so that you may remember and be ashamed, and there will come to be for you no more an opening of your mouth from the face of your shame, in My making atonement toward you for all that you have done! An utterance of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 16:63"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 16"/>

<chapter number="17" style="c" sid="EZK 17"/>

<para style="s">The Parable of Two Eagles and a Vine</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 17:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 13:24–30</char></note>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 17:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 17:2"/>“Son of man, pose a riddle and present a parable to the house of Israel, <verse eid="EZK 17:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 17:3"/>and say, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:3">‘<char style="add">A</char> great eagle, great of wings and long of pinions,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Pinions</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> are the outer parts of a bird’s wings, including the flight feathers.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:3">full of feathers that <char style="add">are</char> unto it of many colors, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:3">came to Lebanon, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:3">and took <char style="add">from</char> the treetop of the cedar. <verse eid="EZK 17:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 17:4"/>The topmost of its shoots he plucked off </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:4">and he brought it in to a land of trade. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:4">In a city of merchants he set it. <verse eid="EZK 17:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 17:5"/>And he took from the seed of the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:5">and he put it it in a field of seed; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:5">he took it next to abundant waters; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:5"><char style="add">as</char> a willow tree he set it. <verse eid="EZK 17:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 17:6"/>And it grew and became a spreading vine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:6">low of height, turning its branches toward him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:6">and its roots were under it, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:6">and it became as a vine and made branches </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:6">and sent out shoots. <verse eid="EZK 17:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 17:7"/>And there was one great eagle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:7">great of wings and abundant of feathers, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:7">and behold, this vine bent its roots toward him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:7">and its branches it stretched out toward him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:7">to water it from the beds of its planting. <verse eid="EZK 17:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 17:8"/>In a good field, <char style="add">next</char> to many waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:8">it was planted, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:8">to make branches and to bear fruit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:8">to become as a vine of magnificence.’ <verse eid="EZK 17:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 17:9"/>Say, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:9">‘Will it prosper? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:9">Will he not its roots pull up and strip off its fruit, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:9">so it withers—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:9">all of the fresh sproutings of its branch wither? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:9">And not a great arm or many people </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:9">to lift it up by its roots. <verse eid="EZK 17:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 17:10"/>And behold, being planted, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:10">will it prosper? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:10">At the touching of it <char style="add">by</char> the wind from the east, Will it not it will completely wither—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:10">will it wither on the beds of its planting?’” <verse eid="EZK 17:10"/></para>

<para style="s">The Parable Explained</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 17:11"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 17:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 17:12"/>“Say now to the house of rebellion, ‘Do you⁺ not know what these <char style="add">are</char>?’ Say, ‘Behold, the king of Babylon came <char style="add">to</char> Jerusalem, and he took her king and her princes, and he brought them with him to Babylon. <verse eid="EZK 17:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 17:13"/>And he took from the seed of the king, and he cut with him a covenant, and he brought him in under oath—for the mighty ones of the land he had taken away— <verse eid="EZK 17:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 17:14"/>that the kingdom would be brought low and not lift itself up by keeping his covenant that it may stand. <verse eid="EZK 17:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 17:15"/>And he rebelled against him by sending his messengers to Egypt, to give to him horses and many people. Will he prosper? Will he escape, the one doing these <char style="add">things</char>? And can he break a covenant, and escape?’ <verse eid="EZK 17:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 17:16"/>‘<char style="add">As</char> I live,’ a declaration of the Lord YHWH, ‘Will he not—in the place of the king causing him to reign, of whom his oath he despised, and of whom his covenant he broke with him—die in the midst of Babylon. <verse eid="EZK 17:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 17:17"/>And not with <char style="add">his</char> mighty army and <char style="add">his</char> great assembly, will Pharaoh maintain him in the war, in the piling up of a siege mound, and with the building of a wall, to cut off many souls. <verse eid="EZK 17:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 17:18"/>And he despised the oath by breaking the covenant, and behold, he gave his hand, and all these <char style="add">things</char> he did—he will not escape!’ <verse eid="EZK 17:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 17:19"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘<char style="add">As</char> I live, surely My oath that he despised, and My covenant that he broke, will I not recompense upon his head? <verse eid="EZK 17:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 17:20"/>And I will spread over him My net, and he will be captured in My snare; and I will bring him to Babylon, and I will execute judgment upon him there <char style="add">for</char> the unfaithfulness <char style="add">with</char> which he was unfaithful against Me. <verse eid="EZK 17:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 17:21"/>And all his choice troops<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Many Hebrew manuscripts; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And all his fugatives with all his troops</char></note> will fall by the sword, and those remaining will be scattered to every wind! And you⁺ will know that I, YHWH, have spoken.’ <verse eid="EZK 17:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 17:22"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:22">‘I will take from the treetop of the highest cedar, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:22">and I will set <char style="add">it</char> out; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:22">from the topmost of its shoots, a tender one I will pluck off, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:22">and I will plant <char style="add">it</char> on a mountain high and exalted. <verse eid="EZK 17:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 17:23"/>On a mountain in the height of Israel I will plant it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:23">and it will bear boughs </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:23">and it will yield fruit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:23">and it will be majestic as a cedar; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:23">and will dwell under it every bird of every wing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:23">in the shade of its branches they will dwell. <verse eid="EZK 17:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 17:24"/>And all the trees of the field will know </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:24">that I, YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:24">have brought low the high tree, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:24">and have raised high the low tree; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:24">I dried up the green tree </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:24">and I made bud the dry tree. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 17:24">I, YHWH, have spoken, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 17:24">and I have done <char style="add">it</char>.’” <verse eid="EZK 17:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 17"/>

<chapter number="18" style="c" sid="EZK 18"/>

<para style="s">The Soul Who Sins Will Die</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 18:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 18:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 18:2"/>“What <char style="add">is it</char> to you⁺ <char style="add">that</char> you⁺ are quoting this proverb concerning the land of Israel, saying, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:2">‘The fathers eat sour grapes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:2">and the teeth of the sons are set on edge’? <verse eid="EZK 18:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 18:3"/><char style="add">As</char> I live, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, it will not be for you⁺ to quote this proverb any longer in Israel, <verse eid="EZK 18:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 18:4"/>behold, all souls, they <char style="add">are</char> unto Me—as the soul of the father, also the soul of the son—they <char style="add">are</char> unto Me: The soul that is sinning, it will die. <verse eid="EZK 18:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 18:5"/>And a man, if he is righteous and does justice and righteousness; <verse eid="EZK 18:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 18:6"/><char style="add">if</char> on the mountains he has not eaten, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:6">and his eyes he has not lifted up to the idols of the house of Israel, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:6">and the wife of his neighbor he has not defiled, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:6">and toward a woman <char style="add">in her</char> impurity he has not come near; <verse eid="EZK 18:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 18:7"/>he does not and a man oppressed, he does return </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:7">his pledge to the debtor; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:7"><char style="add">with</char> violence he has not robbed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:7">he gives his bread to the hungry </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:7">and he covers the naked <char style="add">with</char> clothing; <verse eid="EZK 18:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 18:8"/>in usury he does not give, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:8">and an increase he does not take; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:8">he turns back his hand from iniquity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:8">he does true judgment between man and man. <verse eid="EZK 18:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 18:9"/>In My statutes, he walks </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:9">and he keeps My ordinances, to act in faithfulness; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:9">he <char style="add">is</char> righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:9"><char style="add">and</char> he will surely live, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 18:9">a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 18:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 18:10"/>And if he begets a violent son, one shedding blood, or <char style="add">who</char> does to a brother one of these <char style="add">things</char>— <verse eid="EZK 18:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 18:11"/>and he has not done all of these <char style="add">things</char>—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:11">for even on the mountains he has eaten, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:11">and the wife of his neighbor he has defiled; <verse eid="EZK 18:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 18:12"/>he has oppressed the poor and needy; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:12">by violence he has plundered; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:12">the pledge he does not return, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:12">and to the idols he has lifted up his eyes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:12">an abomination he has done, <verse eid="EZK 18:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 18:13"/>in usury he has given, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:13">and increase he has taken. </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 18:13">Will he live? He will not live! He has done all these abominations; he will surely die, and his blood will be upon him! <verse eid="EZK 18:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 18:14"/>And behold, <char style="add">If</char> he begets a son, and he sees all the sins of his father that he has done—and he sees and does not do likewise— <verse eid="EZK 18:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 18:15"/>on the mountains he has not eaten; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:15">and his eyes he has not lifted to the idols of the house of Israel; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:15">the wife of his neighbor he has not defiled, <verse eid="EZK 18:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 18:16"/>and he has not oppressed a man; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:16">he has not withheld a pledge <char style="add">with</char> violence he has not robbed; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:16">he has given his bread to the hungry </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:16">and the naked he has covered with clothing; <verse eid="EZK 18:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 18:17"/>he has turned back his hand from the poor;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he withholds his hand from iniquity</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:17">usury and increase he has not taken, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 18:17">My ordinances he has done, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 18:17"><char style="add">and</char> in My statutes has walked. </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 18:17">He will not die for the iniquity of his father; he will surely live. <verse eid="EZK 18:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 18:18"/>His father, because he pressed <char style="add">with</char> oppression, he robbed his brother by violence, and what <char style="add">is</char> not good he has done in the midst of his people, behold, he will die for his iniquity. <verse eid="EZK 18:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 18:19"/>And you⁺ may say, ‘Why should not the son bear the guilt of the father?’ </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 18:19">And the son has done justice and righteousness, all My statutes he has kept and he has done them; he will surely live. <verse eid="EZK 18:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 18:20"/>The soul sinning, it will die. The son will not bear the guilt of the father, and the father will not bear the guilt of the son; the righteousness of the righteous will be upon himself, and the wickedness of the wicked will be upon himself. <verse eid="EZK 18:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 18:21"/>And a wicked one, if he should turn away from all his sins that he has done, and should keep all My statutes, and do justice and righteousness, he will surely live; he will not die. <verse eid="EZK 18:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 18:22"/>All the transgressions that he has done will not be remembered against him; because of the righteousness that he has done, he will live. <verse eid="EZK 18:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 18:23"/>Do I take any delight <char style="add">in</char> the death of the wicked? An utterance of the Lord YHWH. No, in his turning aside from his ways, and he lives? <verse eid="EZK 18:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 18:24"/>And in the turning away of a righteous man from his righteousness, and he has done iniquity according to all the abominations that the wicked one does, he does, then will he live? All the righteousness that he has done will not be remembered because of the unfaithfulness with which he was unfaithful and the sin that he has sinned; in them he will die. <verse eid="EZK 18:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 18:25"/>And you⁺ have said, ‘The way of the Lord is not just.’ </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 18:25">Hear now, O house of Israel: Is it My way <char style="add">that</char> is not just? Is it not your⁺ ways <char style="add">that</char> are not just? <verse eid="EZK 18:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 18:26"/>In the turning away of a righteous one from his righteousness, when he does iniquity and dies in it, because of the iniquity that he has done, he dies. <verse eid="EZK 18:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 18:27"/>And in the turning away of the wicked from the wickedness that he has done, when he does justice and righteousness, he will keep alive his soul. <verse eid="EZK 18:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 18:28"/>And he considers and turns away from all the transgressions that he had done; he will surely live; he will not die. <verse eid="EZK 18:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 18:29"/>And the house of Israel says, ‘The way of the Lord is not just.’ </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 18:29">Are My ways not just, O house of Israel? <char style="add">Is it</char> not your⁺ ways <char style="add">that</char> are not just? <verse eid="EZK 18:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 18:30"/>Therefore each man, according to his ways, I will judge you⁺, O house of Israel, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. Turn away and turn away from all your⁺ transgressions, and iniquity will not be unto you⁺ as a stumbling block. <verse eid="EZK 18:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 18:31"/>Cast away from you⁺ all the transgressions that you⁺ have transgressed by them, and make for yourselves a new heart and a new spirit! For why should you⁺ die, O house of Israel? <verse eid="EZK 18:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 18:32"/>For I do not delight in the death of the one dying, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, turn back and live! <verse eid="EZK 18:32"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 18"/>

<chapter number="19" style="c" sid="EZK 19"/>

<para style="s">A Lament for the Princes of Israel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 19:1"/><char style="add">“</char> And you, take up a lamentation for the princes of Israel, <verse eid="EZK 19:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 19:2"/>and say: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:2">‘What <char style="add">was</char> your mother? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:2">A lioness among the lions! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:2">She stretched out in the midst of young lions; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:2">she reared her cubs. <verse eid="EZK 19:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 19:3"/>And she brought up one of her cubs; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:3">he became a young lion, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:3">and he learned to tear prey; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:3">he devoured men. <verse eid="EZK 19:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 19:4"/>And the nations heard of him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:4">he was caught in their pit, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:4">and they brought him with the hooks </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:4">to the land of Egypt. <verse eid="EZK 19:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 19:5"/>And she saw that she had waited; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:5">her hope had perished, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:5">and she took one of her cubs; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:5">she has made it a young lion. <verse eid="EZK 19:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 19:6"/>And he went about in the midst of the lions; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:6">he became a young lion, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:6">and he learned to catch prey; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:6">he devoured men. <verse eid="EZK 19:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 19:7"/>And he broke down their strongholds,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He knew their widows</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He seized their widows</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:7">and their cities he laid waste, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:7">and the land was devastated </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:7">and all its fullness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:7">by the voice of his roaring. <verse eid="EZK 19:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 19:8"/>And set out against him </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:8">the nations all around from the provinces, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:8">and they spread over him their net; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:8">he was caught in their pit. <verse eid="EZK 19:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 19:9"/>And they put him in the cage with the hooks, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:9">and they brought him to the king of Babylon; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:9">they brought him in the nets </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:9">so that his voice was heard no longer </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:9">on the mountains of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 19:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 19:10"/>Your mother <char style="add">was</char> was like a vine in your vineyard;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some Hebrew manuscripts; most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in your bloodline</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:10">by the waters she was planted; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:10">she was fruitful and full of branches </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:10">from the many waters. <verse eid="EZK 19:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 19:11"/>And there were unto her branches of strength for scepters of rulers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:11">and she towered in height over among the thick branches, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:11">and it was seen in its height, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:11">in the abundance of its branches. <verse eid="EZK 19:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 19:12"/>And she was uprooted in fury; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:12">she was cast down to the ground, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:12">and the wind from the east dried up her fruit; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:12">the branches of her strength were broken and withered; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:12">fire consumed them. <verse eid="EZK 19:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 19:13"/>And now she <char style="add">is</char> planted in the wilderness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:13">in a land of dryness and thirst. <verse eid="EZK 19:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 19:14"/>And fire has gone out from a staff of her branches; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:14">it devoured her fruit, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 19:14">so that there should not be in her </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 19:14">a staff of strength, a scepter for ruling.’ </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 19:14">This <char style="add">is</char> a lamentation, and it is for lamentation.” <verse eid="EZK 19:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 19"/>

<chapter number="20" style="c" sid="EZK 20"/>

<para style="s">Israel’s Rebellion in Egypt</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 20:1"/>And it came to pass in the seventh year, in the fifth, on the tenth of the month, <char style="add">that</char> came men from the elders of Israel to inquire of YHWH, and they sat before me. <verse eid="EZK 20:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 20:2"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 20:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 20:3"/>“Son of man, speak to the elders of Israel, and say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: Have you⁺ come to inquire of Me? <char style="add">As</char> I live, I will not be inquired of by you⁺, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 20:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 20:4"/>Will you judge them? Will you judge <char style="add">them</char>, son of man? Make known to them the abominations of their fathers, <verse eid="EZK 20:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 20:5"/>and say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: On the day of my choosing Israel, I lifted My hand to the seed of the house of Jacob, and I made Myself known to them in the land of Egypt. And I lifted My hand to them, saying, ‘I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH your⁺ God.’ <verse eid="EZK 20:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 20:6"/>On that day I lifted My hand to them to bring them out from the land of Egypt into a land that I had searched out for them, flowing with milk and honey—the glory it <char style="add">is</char> of all the lands! <verse eid="EZK 20:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 20:7"/>And I said to them, ‘Each man must throw away the abominations before his eyes, and with the idols of Egypt you⁺ shall not defile yourselves! I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH your⁺ God.’ <verse eid="EZK 20:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 20:8"/>And they rebelled against Me, and they were not willing to listen to Me. Each man, the abominations of their eyes, they did not cast away, and the idols of Egypt they did not forsake. And I said, I will pour out My fury upon them, to complete My anger against them in the midst of the land of Egypt! <verse eid="EZK 20:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 20:9"/>And I acted for the sake of My name, for it not to be profaned before the eyes of the nations, in the midst of whom they <char style="add">were</char>, who before their eyes I had made Myself known to them, to bring them out from the land of Egypt. <verse eid="EZK 20:9"/></para>

<para style="s">Israel’s Rebellion in the Wilderness</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 20:10"/>And I brought them out from the land of Egypt, and I brought them into the wilderness. <verse eid="EZK 20:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 20:11"/>And I gave to them My statutes, and I made known <char style="add">to</char> them My judgments, which the man shall do them, and he will live by them. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Leviticus 18:5; also in Ezekiel 20:13 and 21.</char></note><verse eid="EZK 20:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 20:12"/>And also My Sabbaths I gave to them to be as a sign between Me and between them, that they might know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, the One sanctifying them. <verse eid="EZK 20:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 20:13"/>And the house of Israel rebelled against Me in the wilderness. In My statutes they did not walk, and My judgments they rejected, which the man shall do them, and he will live by them. And My Sabbaths they defiled greatly. And I said to pour out My fury on them in the wilderness to put an end to them! <verse eid="EZK 20:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 20:14"/>And I acted for the sake of My name, for it not to be profaned before the eyes of the nations, who before their eyes I had brought them out. <verse eid="EZK 20:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 20:15"/>And also I lifted My hand to them in the wilderness not to bring them into the land that I had given, flowing with milk and honey—the glory it is of all the lands, <verse eid="EZK 20:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 20:16"/>because My ordinances they rejected, and My statutes they did not walk in them, and My Sabbaths they profaned, for their heart was walking after their idols. <verse eid="EZK 20:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 20:17"/>And My eye showed pity to them from destroying them, and I did not make a complete end of them in the wilderness. <verse eid="EZK 20:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 20:18"/>And I said to their sons in the wilderness, ‘In the statutes of your⁺ fathers you⁺ shall not walk, and their ordinances you⁺ shall not keep, and with their idols you⁺ shall not defile yourselves. <verse eid="EZK 20:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 20:19"/>I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH your⁺ God; in My statutes you must walk, and My ordinances you must keep and do them, <verse eid="EZK 20:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 20:20"/>and My Sabbaths keep holy, that they may be as a sign between Me and between you⁺, to know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH your⁺ God.’ <verse eid="EZK 20:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 20:21"/>And the sons also rebelled against Me. In My statutes they did not walk, and My judgments they did not keep to do them, which a man shall do them, and he will live by them. My Sabbaths they profaned, and I said to pour out My fury on them to accomplish My anger against them in the wilderness. <verse eid="EZK 20:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 20:22"/>And I turned back My hand, and I acted for the sake of My name not to be profaned in the eyes of the nations who before their eyes I had brought them out. <verse eid="EZK 20:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 20:23"/>I also, I have lifted up My hand to them in the wilderness to scatter them among the nations and to scatter them among the lands, <verse eid="EZK 20:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 20:24"/>because My ordinances they had not done, and My statutes they had rejected, and My Sabbaths they had profaned, and their eyes were after the idols of their fathers. <verse eid="EZK 20:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 20:25"/>And also I gave to them statutes not good, and ordinances by which they could not live. <verse eid="EZK 20:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 20:26"/>And I made them unclean through their gifts, in making pass through all their firstborn, so that I might make them desolate, so that they would know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 20:26"/></para>

<para style="s">Israel’s Rebellion in the Land</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 20:27"/>Therefore, speak to the house of Israel, son of man, and say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: Also in this your⁺ fathers, in their being unfaithful to Me, blasphemed Me in unfaithfulness. <verse eid="EZK 20:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 20:28"/>And I brought them into the land that I had lifted up My hand to give it to them, and they saw all the high hills and every leafy tree, and there they offered their sacrifices, and there <char style="add">was</char> provocation by their offerings, and there they sent <char style="add">up</char> their pleasing aroma, and there they poured out their drink offerings. <verse eid="EZK 20:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 20:29"/>And I said to them, ‘What <char style="add">is</char> this high place <char style="add">to</char> which you⁺ are going there?’ </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 20:29">And its name is called Bamah to this day. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Bamah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">high place</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><verse eid="EZK 20:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 20:30"/>Therefore say to the house of Israel, thus says the Lord YHWH: In the way of your⁺ fathers will you⁺ be defiling yourselves and prostituting yourselves after their abominations? <verse eid="EZK 20:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 20:31"/>For in your lifting up your⁺ gifts, and making your⁺ sons pass through the fire, you⁺ are defiling yourselves with all your⁺ idols, even to this day. And shall I be consulted by you⁺, O house of Israel? <char style="add">As</char> I live, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, I will not be consulted by you⁺! <verse eid="EZK 20:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 20:32"/>And the <char style="add">thing</char> coming up upon your⁺ mind, not at all shall come to pass—that you⁺ say, let us become like the nations, like the tribes of the lands, ministering <char style="add">to</char> wood and stone!’ <verse eid="EZK 20:32"/></para>

<para style="s">Judgment and Restoration</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 20:33"/><char style="add">As</char> I live—a declaration of the Lord YHWH—if not with a mighty hand and with an outstretched arm and with fury poured out I will rule over you⁺! <verse eid="EZK 20:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 20:34"/>And I will bring out you⁺ from the peoples, and I will gather you⁺ from the lands to which you⁺ have been scattered in them, with a mighty hand and with an outstretched arm and with fury poured out. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">receive you</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see also 2 Corinthians 6:17.</char></note><verse eid="EZK 20:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 20:35"/>And I will bring you⁺ into the wilderness of the peoples, and I will enter into judgment with you⁺ there, face to face! <verse eid="EZK 20:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 20:36"/>As I entered into judgment with your⁺ fathers in the wilderness of the land of Egypt,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the wilderness after bringing them out of Egypt</char></note> so I will enter into judgment with you⁺, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 20:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 20:37"/>And I will make you⁺ pass under the rod, and I will bring you⁺ into the bond of the covenant. <verse eid="EZK 20:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 20:38"/>And I will purge from among you⁺ those rebelling and those transgressing against Me; from the land of their sojourning I will bring out them, and into the land of Israel they will not come. And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 20:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="EZK 20:39"/>And you⁺, O house of Israel, thus says the Lord YHWH: Let <char style="add">each</char> man go <char style="add">and</char> serve his idols, and afterward, if you⁺ are not listening to Me; and the name of My holiness you⁺ will profane no more with your⁺ gifts and with your⁺ idols! <verse eid="EZK 20:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="EZK 20:40"/>For on the mountain of My holiness, on the mountain of the height of Israel, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, there they will serve Me—all the house of Israel, all of them in the land. There I will accept them, and there I will seek out your⁺ contributions and the firstfruits of your⁺ sacrifices with all your⁺ holy things. <verse eid="EZK 20:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="EZK 20:41"/>With a pleasing aroma I will accept you⁺, in My bringing you⁺ out from the peoples and in My gathering you⁺ from the lands to which you⁺ have been scattered in them; and I will show My holiness in you⁺ before the eyes of the nations. <verse eid="EZK 20:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="EZK 20:42"/>And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, in My bringing you⁺ to the land of Israel, to the land that I lifted My hand to give it to your⁺ fathers. <verse eid="EZK 20:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="EZK 20:43"/>And you⁺ will remember there your⁺ ways, and all your⁺ deeds with which you⁺ defiled yourselves in them, and you⁺ will be loathsome in your⁺ own sight for all the evils that you⁺ have done. <verse eid="EZK 20:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="EZK 20:44"/>And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, in my dealing with you⁺ for the sake of My name, not according to your⁺ evil ways and your⁺ corrupt deeds, O house of Israel, a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 20:44"/></para>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against the South</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="EZK 20:45"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 20:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="EZK 20:46"/>“Son of man, set your face <char style="add">to</char> the way of Teman,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.46 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the south</char></note> and preach against the south, and prophesy against the forest of the land of the Negev. <verse eid="EZK 20:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="EZK 20:47"/>And say to the forest of the Negev, Hear the word of YHWH, thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I am going to kindle in you a fire, and it will devour in you every moist tree and every dry tree; the blazing flame will not be quenched, and all faces from the south to the north will be scorched by it! <verse eid="EZK 20:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="EZK 20:48"/>And all flesh will see that I, YHWH, have kindled it l it will not be quenched.” <verse eid="EZK 20:48"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="EZK 20:49"/>And I said: “Ah, Lord YHWH! They are saying of me, ‘Is he not one telling parables?’” <verse eid="EZK 20:49"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 20"/>

<chapter number="21" style="c" sid="EZK 21"/>

<para style="s">God’s Sword of Judgment</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 21:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 21:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 21:2"/>“Son of man, set your face toward Jerusalem, and preach against the sanctuaries, and prophesy against the land of Israel, <verse eid="EZK 21:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 21:3"/>and say to the land of Israel, thus says YHWH: ‘Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you, and I will draw My sword from its sheath and I will cut off from you the righteous one and the wicked one! <verse eid="EZK 21:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 21:4"/>Because that I will cut off from you the righteous one and the wicked one, therefore My sword will go forth from its sheath against all flesh, from south to north. <verse eid="EZK 21:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 21:5"/>And all flesh will know that I, YHWH, have drawn My sword from its sheath; it will not return anymore!’ <verse eid="EZK 21:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 21:6"/>And you, son of man, groan with the breaking of loins, and with bitterness groan before their eyes. <verse eid="EZK 21:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 21:7"/>And it will come to pass when they say to you, ‘For what <char style="add">are</char> you sighing?’ That you will answer, ‘Because of the news that is coming; and every heart will melt, and all hands will become feeble, and every spirit will faint, and all knees will turn to water.’ Behold, it is coming, and it will come to pass! An utterance of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 21:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 21:8"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 21:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 21:9"/>“Son of man, prophesy and say, thus says the Lord: Say, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:9">‘A sword, a sword is sharpened, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:9">also polished, <verse eid="EZK 21:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 21:10"/>it is sharpened in order to slaughter a slaughter; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:10">it is polished in order <char style="add">that</char> it may become lightning. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:10">Or should we rejoice <char style="add">in</char> the scepter of My son? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:10">It is despising every such stick? <verse eid="EZK 21:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 21:11"/>And He has given it to be polished, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:11">to grasp it in the palm; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:11">the sword is sharpened and it is polished, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:11">to be given it into the hand of the one slaying. <verse eid="EZK 21:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 21:12"/>Cry and wail, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:12">O son of man! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:12">For it shall be upon my people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:12">it <char style="add">is</char> against all the princes of Israel! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:12">They are cast to the sword they will be upon My people! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:12">Therefore strike upon <char style="add">your</char> thigh.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">beat your breast</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 21:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 21:13"/>For there is a testing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:13">and what if even the scepter </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:13">it is despising </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:13">does not continue!’ </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 21:13">An utterance of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 21:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 21:14"/>‘And you, son of man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:14">prophesy and strike together the palm, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:14">and let the sword come twice—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:14">a third time—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:14">the sword of the slain! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:14">It <char style="add">is</char> the sword of great slaughter </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:14">that is surrounding them, <verse eid="EZK 21:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 21:15"/>in order to melt the heart </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:15">and to increase those stumbling. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:15">Against all their gates </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:15">I have appointed a sword for slaughter. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:15">Ah, it is made as lightning; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:15">it is grasped for slaughter! <verse eid="EZK 21:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 21:16"/>Slash, thrust right, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:16">set it, thrust left, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:16">wherever your face is appointed! <verse eid="EZK 21:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 21:17"/>And I also will strike My palm to My palm, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:17">and My fury I will cause to rest.’ </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 21:17">I, YHWH, have spoken.” <verse eid="EZK 21:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 21:18"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 21:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 21:19"/>“And you, son of man, set for yourself two ways to go for the sword of the king of Babylon! From one land they will come forth, the two of them, and create a signpost—at the head of the way to the city create <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="EZK 21:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 21:20"/>Appoint a way for the coming of the sword to Rabbah of the sons of Ammon and to Judah, into fortified Jerusalem. <verse eid="EZK 21:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 21:21"/>For the king of Babylon stands at the parting of the way, at the head of the two ways, to divine <char style="add">with</char> divination; he shakes the arrows, he inquires of the teraphim, he looks at the liver. <verse eid="EZK 21:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 21:22"/>In his right hand is the divination for Jerusalem, to set up battering rams, to open the mouth with shattering, to lift high the voice with shouting, to set battering rams against the gates, to heap up a mound, and to build a wall. <verse eid="EZK 21:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 21:23"/>And it will be to them like an empty divination in their eyes, those having sworn oaths with them; and he will call to remembrance their guilt, to take them captive. <verse eid="EZK 21:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 21:24"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because you⁺ have made your⁺ iniquity to be remembered, in your⁺ transgressions being uncovered, to cause your⁺ sins to be seen in all your⁺ deeds—because of your⁺ being remembered, you⁺ shall be taken in hand. <verse eid="EZK 21:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 21:25"/>And you, O profane <char style="add">and</char> wicked prince of Israel, <char style="add">for</char> whom </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:25">his day has come, in the time of <char style="add">your</char> punishment at the end— <verse eid="EZK 21:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 21:26"/>thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:26">‘Turn aside the turban </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:26">and lift off the crown; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:26">this <char style="add">will</char> no longer <char style="add">be</char> the same! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:26">The low make high, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:26">and the high make low. <verse eid="EZK 21:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 21:27"/>A ruin, a ruin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:27">I will make it a ruin! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:27">And it will not be </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:27">until He comes whose it is; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:27">to Him I have assigned the judgment.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">until He comes whose it is, to whom I have given it.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 21:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 21:28"/>And you, son of man, prophesy and say, thus says the Lord YHWH concerning the sons of Ammon and concerning their scorn; and you shall say: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:28">‘A sword, a sword </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:28">is opened for slaughter! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:28">Polished for consuming, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:28">in order <char style="add">to be</char> like lightning. <verse eid="EZK 21:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 21:29"/>In seeing falsehood for you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:29">in divining to you a lie, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:29">to put you on the necks </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:29">of the wounded of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:29">whose day has come, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:29">in the time of the iniquity of the end. <verse eid="EZK 21:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 21:30"/>Return <char style="add">it</char> to its sheath! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:30">In the place where you were created, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:30">in the land of your origin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:30">I will judge you. <verse eid="EZK 21:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 21:31"/>And I will pour out on you My anger; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:31">with the fire of My wrath I will blow against you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:31">and I will give you into the hands of brutish men, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:31">craftsmen of destruction. <verse eid="EZK 21:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 21:32"/>For the fire you will be as food; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:32">your blood will be in the midst of the land; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 21:32">you will not be remembered! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 21:32">Indeed I, YHWH, have spoken.’” <verse eid="EZK 21:32"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 21"/>

<chapter number="22" style="c" sid="EZK 22"/>

<para style="s">The Sins of Jerusalem</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 22:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 22:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 22:2"/>“And you, son of man, will you judge, will you judge <char style="add">this</char> city of blood? Then make known to her all her abominations, <verse eid="EZK 22:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 22:3"/>and say, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘O city, pouring out blood in her midst, so that her time may come, and she makes idols upon herself to defile herself! <verse eid="EZK 22:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 22:4"/>By the blood that you have poured out, you have become guilty, and by the idols that you have made, you have defiled yourself; and your days you have brought near, and you have come to your years! Upon thus I have made you a reproach for the nations, and of derision for all the lands. <verse eid="EZK 22:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 22:5"/>Those near and those far from you will mock you, O unclean of name, full of turmoil. <verse eid="EZK 22:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 22:6"/>Behold, the princes of Israel, each man to his arm, have come to be among you in order to pour out blood! <verse eid="EZK 22:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 22:7"/>The father and mother they have belittled among you; against the sojourner they have acted with oppression in your midst; the fatherless and the widow they have mistreated among you. <verse eid="EZK 22:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 22:8"/>My holy things you have despised, and My Sabbaths you have profaned. <verse eid="EZK 22:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 22:9"/>Men of slander are among you in order to pour out blood, and on the mountains they eat among you, <char style="add">and</char> wickedness they do in your midst. <verse eid="EZK 22:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 22:10"/>The nakedness of their fathers they uncover among you; the impurity of the women they violate among you. <verse eid="EZK 22:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 22:11"/>And a man with the wife of his neighbor commits an abomination, and <char style="add">another</char> man his daughter-in-law defiles in wickedness; and a man violates his sister, the daughter of his father, among you. <verse eid="EZK 22:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 22:12"/>They take Bribes among you in order to pour out blood; usury and increase you take, and you cut off your neighbors by extortion, and Me you have forgotten, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 22:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 22:13"/>So behold, I strike My hands against your dishonest gain that you have made, and over the bloodshed that has come to be in your midst! <verse eid="EZK 22:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 22:14"/>Can your heart stand or can your hands remain strong, in the days when I will be dealing with you? I, YHWH, have spoken, and I will act. <verse eid="EZK 22:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 22:15"/>And I will disperse you among the nations, and I will scatter you among the lands, and I will finish off your uncleanness from you. <verse eid="EZK 22:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 22:16"/>And you will profane yourself<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And I have allotted you your inheritance</char></note> before the eyes of the nations, and you will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 22:16"/></para>

<para style="s">The Refining Furnace</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 22:17"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 22:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 22:18"/>“Son of man, the house of Israel has become to Me as dross; they <char style="add">are</char> all bronze, and tin, and iron, and lead in the midst of a furnace; they have become the dross of silver. <verse eid="EZK 22:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 22:19"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because all of you⁺ have become as dross, therefore, behold, I am going to gather you⁺ into the midst of Jerusalem. <verse eid="EZK 22:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 22:20"/>The gathering of silver, and bronze, and iron, and lead, and tin into the midst of a furnace, to blow on it fire to melt <char style="add">it</char>; so I will gather <char style="add">you</char> in My anger and in My fury, and I will leave <char style="add">you</char> and I will melt you⁺! <verse eid="EZK 22:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 22:21"/>And I will gather you⁺ and will blow on you⁺ with the fire of My wrath, and you⁺ will be melted in its midst. <verse eid="EZK 22:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 22:22"/>As silver is melted in the midst of a furnace, so will you⁺ be melted in its midst. And you⁺ will know that I, YHWH, have poured out My fury upon you⁺.’” <verse eid="EZK 22:22"/></para>

<para style="s">Israel’s Wicked Leaders</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 22:23"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying, <verse eid="EZK 22:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 22:24"/>“Son of man, say to her: ‘You <char style="add">are</char> a land that is not cleansed, nor <char style="add">is</char> rain on her, in the day of anger.’ <verse eid="EZK 22:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 22:25"/>The conspiracy of her princes<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of her prophets</char></note> in her midst is like a roaring lion tearing the prey; they have devoured the soul; they have taken treasure and precious things; they have made many widows in her midst. <verse eid="EZK 22:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 22:26"/>Her priests have done violence to My law, and have profaned My holy things; between the holy <char style="add">and</char> the profane they do not separate, and between the unclean <char style="add">and</char> the clean they do not discern; and from My Sabbaths they have hidden their eyes, and I am profaned in their midst! <verse eid="EZK 22:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 22:27"/>Her princes within her <char style="add">are</char> like wolves tearing the prey, to shed blood, to destroy souls, and to break off dishonest gain. <verse eid="EZK 22:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 22:28"/>And her prophets have covered them with whitewash, seeing falsehood and divining for them a lie, saying, ‘Thus says the Lord YHWH,’ and YHWH has not spoken. <verse eid="EZK 22:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 22:29"/>The people of the land <char style="add">with</char> oppression have oppressed, and <char style="add">with</char> robbery have robbed, and the poor and the needy they have mistreated; and the sojourner they oppress without justice. <verse eid="EZK 22:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 22:30"/>And I sought from them a man walling up the wall and standing in the breach before Me, on behalf of the land, that I should not destroy it, and no one did I find. <verse eid="EZK 22:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 22:31"/>And I have poured out on them My anger; with the fire of My wrath I have consumed them; their deeds have I recompensed on their own heads! An utterance of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 22:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 22"/>

<chapter number="23" style="c" sid="EZK 23"/>

<para style="s">The Two Adulterous Sisters</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 23:1"/>And the word came of YHWH to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 23:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 23:2"/>“Son of man, there were two women, the daughters of one mother. <verse eid="EZK 23:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 23:3"/>And they acted as prostitutes in Egypt; in their youth they were prostitutes; there were squeezed their breasts, and there were pressed the nipples of their virginity. <verse eid="EZK 23:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 23:4"/>And their names <char style="add">were</char> Oholah<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Oholah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">her own tent</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">she worships at a tent shrine</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, a metaphor for Samaria as an adulteress with Assyria.</char></note> the elder, and Oholibah<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Oholibah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the tent is in her</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">she is a tent shrine</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, a metaphor for Jerusalem as an adulterous wife.</char></note> her sister. And they were unto Me, and they gave birth to sons and daughters. And their names—Samaria <char style="add">is</char> Oholah, and Jerusalem <char style="add">is</char> Oholibah. <verse eid="EZK 23:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 23:5"/>And Oholah prostituted herself under Me, and she lusted over her lovers, toward Assyria, warriors <verse eid="EZK 23:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 23:6"/>clothed <char style="add">in</char> purple, governors and commanders, young men of desire all of them, horsemen riding on horses. <verse eid="EZK 23:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 23:7"/>And she gave her prostitutions with them, choice men of Assyria, all of them; and with all <char style="add">for</char> whom she lusted, with all their idols she defiled herself. <verse eid="EZK 23:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 23:8"/>And her prostitutions from Egypt she has not left behind; for they had lain with her in her youth, and they pressed the nipples of her virginity, and poured out their lust upon her. <verse eid="EZK 23:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 23:9"/>Therefore I have given her into the hand of her lovers, into the hand of the sons of Assyria, for whom she lusted. <verse eid="EZK 23:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 23:10"/>They have uncovered her nakedness; her sons and daughters they took away, and with the sword they slew her. And she has become a byword among the women, and they executed when judgment against her. <verse eid="EZK 23:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 23:11"/>And her sister Oholibah saw <char style="add">this</char>, and in her lust she became corrupt above her, and her prostitutions <char style="add">were</char> more than the prostitution of her sister. <verse eid="EZK 23:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 23:12"/>She lusted after the sons of Assyria—governors and commanders, warriors clothed in perfection, horsemen riding on horses, young men of desire all of them. <verse eid="EZK 23:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 23:13"/>And I saw that she was defiled; one way <char style="add">is</char> unto the two of them, <verse eid="EZK 23:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 23:14"/>and she had added to her prostitutions, and she looked at men portrayed on the wall, images of Chaldeans<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Babylonians</char></note> portrayed in vermilion, <verse eid="EZK 23:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 23:15"/>girded with belts around their loins, turbans flowing on their heads, <char style="add">with</char> the appearance of officers all of them, in the likeness of the sons of Babylon, Chaldea<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Babylonia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 16</char></note> the land of their origin. <verse eid="EZK 23:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 23:16"/>And she lusted for them at the seeing of her eyes, and she sent messengers to them in Chaldea. <verse eid="EZK 23:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 23:17"/>And the sons of Babylon came to her, into the bed of love, and they defiled her with their lust; and she was defiled by them, and she dislocated her soul from them. <verse eid="EZK 23:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 23:18"/>And she uncovered her prostitutions, and she uncovered her nakedness, and I dislocated My soul from her, as I had dislocated My soul from her sister. <verse eid="EZK 23:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 23:19"/>And she multiplied her prostitutions, to remember the days of her youth, when she had prostituted herself in the land of Egypt, <verse eid="EZK 23:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 23:20"/>and lusted after their lovers, <char style="add">for</char> whom the flesh of donkeys <char style="add">is</char> the flesh, and the emission of stallions <char style="add">was</char> their emission. <verse eid="EZK 23:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 23:21"/>And you revisited the wickedness of your youth, in the pressing by the Egyptians of your nipples, on account of the breasts of your youth. <verse eid="EZK 23:21"/></para>

<para style="s">Oholibah to Be Plagued</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 23:22"/>Therefore, Oholibah, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I am stirring up your lovers against you, from whom you have dislocated your soul, and I will bring them against you from all around: <verse eid="EZK 23:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 23:23"/>The sons of Babylon and all the Chaldeans, Pekod, and Shoa, and Koa, all the sons of Assyria with them—young men of desire, governors and commanders all of them, officers and renowned ones, all of them riding on horses. <verse eid="EZK 23:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 23:24"/>And they will come against you with weapons,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And they will all come against you from the north</char></note> chariots, and wagons, and with a horde of people; buckler and shield and helmet they will array against you all around; and I will give to them judgment, and they will judge you by their own judgments. <verse eid="EZK 23:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 23:25"/>And I will set My jealousy against you, and they will deal with you in anger; your nose and your ears they will turn aside, and your survivors will fall by the sword; they will take your sons and your daughters, and your remnant will be devoured by the fire! <verse eid="EZK 23:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 23:26"/>And they will strip you of your clothes, and they will take away the articles of your beauty. <verse eid="EZK 23:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 23:27"/>And your wickedness I will make cease from you, and your prostitution from the land of Egypt, and you will not lift up your eyes to them, and Egypt you will not remember anymore.’ <verse eid="EZK 23:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 23:28"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I am giving you into the hand of those whom you hate, into the hand of those whom you had alienated your soul from. <verse eid="EZK 23:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 23:29"/>And they will deal with you in hate, and they will take away all your labor, and they will leave you naked and bare, and the nakedness of your prostitutions will be uncovered, and your wickedness, and your prostitutions! <verse eid="EZK 23:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 23:30"/>I will do these <char style="add">things</char> to you upon your prostituting yourself after the nations, upon that you have defiled yourself with their idols. <verse eid="EZK 23:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 23:31"/>You have walked in the way of your sister, and I have given her cup into your hand.’ <verse eid="EZK 23:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 23:32"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 23:32">‘The cup of your sister you will drink, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:32">deep and wide; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 23:32">it will be for laughter and derision, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:32">in its containing a great amount. <verse eid="EZK 23:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 23:33"/>With drunkenness and sorrow you will be filled—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:33">the cup of horror and desolation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:33">the cup of your sister Samaria— <verse eid="EZK 23:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 23:34"/>and you will drink it and drain it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:34">and its shards you will dash </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 23:34">and tear at your breasts! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 23:34">For I have spoken,’ </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 23:34">a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 23:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 23:35"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because you have forgotten Me, and you have cast Me behind your back, you also will bear your wickedness and your prostitutions.’” <verse eid="EZK 23:35"/></para>

<para style="s">Judgment on Both Sisters</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 23:36"/>And YHWH said to me: “Son of man, will you judge Oholah and Oholibah? You must make known to them their abominations. <verse eid="EZK 23:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 23:37"/>For they have committed adultery, and blood <char style="add">is</char> on their hands; with their idols they have committed adultery, and even their sons whom they bore to Me, they made pass through <char style="add">the fire</char> for them as food. <verse eid="EZK 23:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 23:38"/>Moreover this they have done to Me: They have defiled My sanctuary on that day, and My Sabbaths have profaned. <verse eid="EZK 23:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="EZK 23:39"/>For in their slaughtering their children to their idols, they came into My sanctuary on that day to profane it; and behold, thus they have done in the midst of My house, <verse eid="EZK 23:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="EZK 23:40"/>and also that they sent for men to come from afar, to whom a messenger <char style="add">was</char> sent, and behold—they came, those for whom you washed yourself <char style="add">and</char> painted your eyes, and adorned yourself with ornaments. <verse eid="EZK 23:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="EZK 23:41"/>And you sat on a glorious couch, <char style="add">with</char> a table arranged before it, and My incense and My oil you had set on it. <verse eid="EZK 23:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="EZK 23:42"/>And the voice of a crowd at ease <char style="add">was</char> with her, and to men from the multitude of mankind were brought drunkards<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Sabeans</char></note> from the wilderness,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the desert</char></note> and they gave bracelets to their wrists and crowns of beauty upon their heads. <verse eid="EZK 23:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="EZK 23:43"/>And I said of her who was worn out in adulteries, ‘Now will they commit prostitutions with her—and she also!’ <verse eid="EZK 23:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="EZK 23:44"/>And they have come in to her as the coming in to a woman, a prostitute. Thus they went <char style="add">in</char> to Oholah and to Oholibah, women of wickedness! <verse eid="EZK 23:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="EZK 23:45"/>And righteous men, they will pass judgment <char style="add">on</char> them with the judgment of adulteresses, and <char style="add">with</char> the judgment of those shedding blood, because they <char style="add">are</char> adulteresses, and blood <char style="add">is</char> on their hands! <verse eid="EZK 23:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="EZK 23:46"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Bring up against them an assembly, and give them to terror and plunder! <verse eid="EZK 23:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="EZK 23:47"/>And the assembly will stone them <char style="add">with</char> stones and will cut down them with their swords; their sons and their daughters they will slay, they will burn and their houses with the fire. <verse eid="EZK 23:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="EZK 23:48"/>And <char style="add">this</char> wickedness I will make cease from the land, and all the women will be admonished and they will not act according to your⁺ wickedness. <verse eid="EZK 23:48"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="EZK 23:49"/>And they will put your⁺ wickedness upon you⁺, and the sins of your⁺ idols you⁺ will bear. And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> the Lord YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 23:49"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 23"/>

<chapter number="24" style="c" sid="EZK 24"/>

<para style="s">The Parable of the Cooking Pot</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 24:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me in the ninth year, in the tenth month, on the tenth of the month, saying: <verse eid="EZK 24:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 24:2"/>“Son of man, write down for yourself the name of the day, this very day. The king of Babylon has laid siege against Jerusalem on this very day. <verse eid="EZK 24:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 24:3"/>And utter to house the rebellious a parable, and say to them—thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:3">‘Put on a pot; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:3">put <char style="add">it</char> on, and also pour water into it. <verse eid="EZK 24:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 24:4"/>To gather its pieces to it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:4">every good piece—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:4">thigh and shoulder; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:4">fill <char style="add">it</char> with the choicest of limbs. <verse eid="EZK 24:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 24:5"/>Take the choicest of the flock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:5">and pile up the bones under it; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:5">bring to a boil the boiling of it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:5">and let seethe the limbs in the midst of it.’ <verse eid="EZK 24:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 24:6"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:6">‘Woe to the city of blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:6">the pot that has rust in it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:6">and its corrosion has not gone out from it! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:6">Piece after piece bring out from it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:6">a lot has not fallen on it.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">let no lot fall upon it</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 24:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 24:7"/>For her blood is in her midst; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:7">upon a clear place of a rock she set it; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:7">she has not poured it out on the ground </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:7">to cover over it with dust. <verse eid="EZK 24:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 24:8"/>To cause fury to come up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:8">to avenge <char style="add">with</char> vengeance, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:8">I have given her blood upon a clear place of a rock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:8">that it should not be covered.’ <verse eid="EZK 24:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 24:9"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:9">‘Woe to the city of blood! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:9">Even I will make great the pyre! <verse eid="EZK 24:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 24:10"/>Heap on the wood, kindle the fire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:10">consume the flesh, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:10">and mix in the spices, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:10">and let the bones be burned up. <verse eid="EZK 24:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 24:11"/>And set it on its coals empty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:11">so that it may become hot and its bronze may burn, it will be melted in the midst </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:11">of its impurity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:11">its corrosion consumed. <verse eid="EZK 24:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 24:12"/><char style="add">With</char> toiling she has grown weary, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:12">and the abundance of her corrosion has not gone out from her—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:12">into the fire <char style="add">with</char> her corrosion! <verse eid="EZK 24:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 24:13"/>In your uncleanness <char style="add">is</char> wickedness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:13">because I have cleansed you </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:13">and you would not be cleansed </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:13">from your uncleanness, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:13">you will not be cleansed anymore, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:13">until I have caused to rest My fury on you. <verse eid="EZK 24:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 24:14"/>I, YHWH, have spoken <char style="add">it</char>—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:14">it is coming, and I will do <char style="add">it</char>! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:14">I will not hold back, and I will not show pity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:14">and I will not relent. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 24:14">According to your ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 24:14">and according to your deeds they will judge you,’ </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 24:14">a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 24:14"/></para>

<para style="s">Ezekiel’s Wife Dies</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 24:15"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 24:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 24:16"/>“Son of man, behold—I am taking away from you the desire of your eyes with a stroke, and you will not mourn and you will not weep, and your tears will not run down. <verse eid="EZK 24:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 24:17"/>Groan, keep silent, you shall make no mourning for the dead. Bind your turban on you, and place your sandals on your feet; do not put a wrap over the lip, and the bread of men do not eat.” <verse eid="EZK 24:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 24:18"/>And I spoke to the people in the morning, and my wife died in the evening, and in the morning I did as I was commanded. <verse eid="EZK 24:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 24:19"/>And the people said to me: “Will you not declare to us what these <char style="add">things</char> <char style="add">are</char> to us, that you are doing <char style="add">this</char>?” <verse eid="EZK 24:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 24:20"/>And I gave the answer to them: “The word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 24:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 24:21"/>Speak to the house of Israel, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I am going to profane My sanctuary, the pride of your⁺ strength, the desire of your⁺ eyes, and the delight of your⁺ soul; and your⁺ sons and daughters, whom you⁺ left behind, will fall by the sword.’ <verse eid="EZK 24:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 24:22"/>And you⁺ will do as I have done: Upon the lip you⁺ shall not put a wrap, and bread of men you⁺ shall not eat; <verse eid="EZK 24:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 24:23"/>and your⁺ turbans will be on your⁺ heads, and your⁺ sandals on your⁺ feet. You⁺ will not mourn nor weep; and you⁺ will waste away in your⁺ iniquities, and a man will groan toward his brother. <verse eid="EZK 24:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 24:24"/>And Ezekiel will be to you⁺ as a sign; according to all that he has done, you⁺ will do. And in its coming to pass, you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> the Lord YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 24:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 24:25"/>And you, son of man, <char style="add">is it</char> not in the day of My taking from them their stronghold, their joy, their glory, the desire of their eyes, and the burden of their soul—their sons and their daughters— <verse eid="EZK 24:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 24:26"/>on that day will come one who escapes to you as a cause to hear the ears? <verse eid="EZK 24:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 24:27"/>On that day your mouth will be opened <char style="add">to</char> the one who has escaped, and you will speak, and you will not be mute any longer; and you will be for them as a sign, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 24:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 24"/>

<chapter number="25" style="c" sid="EZK 25"/>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Ammon</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 25:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 25:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 25:2"/>“Son of man, set your face against the sons of Ammon, and prophesy against them. <verse eid="EZK 25:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 25:3"/>And say to the sons of Ammon, hear the word of the Lord YHWH, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because you said, “Aha!” Against My sanctuary when it was profaned, and against the land of Israel when it became desolate, and against the house of Judah when they went, into captivity; <verse eid="EZK 25:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 25:4"/>therefore behold, I am giving you to the sons of the East as a possession, and they will settle their encampments among you, and they will put their tents among you; they will eat your fruit, and they will drink your milk. <verse eid="EZK 25:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 25:5"/>And I will give Rabbah as a habitation of camels, and the sons of Ammon as a resting place for the flock. And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 25:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 25:6"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because of your clapping hands and your stomping with feet, and you rejoiced with all contempt of heart against the land of Israel, <verse eid="EZK 25:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 25:7"/>therefore behold, I am stretching out My hand against you, and will give you as plunder to the nations, and I will cut you off from the peoples, and I will cause you to perish from the lands; I will destroy you, and you will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH!’ <verse eid="EZK 25:7"/></para>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Moab</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 25:8"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because of the saying of Moab and Seir,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and Seir</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> “Behold, like all the nations <char style="add">is</char> the house of Judah,” <verse eid="EZK 25:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 25:9"/>therefore behold, I am going to lay open the shoulder of Moab from the cities, from its cities on its frontier, the glory of the land—Beth-jeshimoth, Baal-meon, and Kiriathaim— <verse eid="EZK 25:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 25:10"/>to the sons of the East, along with the sons of Ammon, and I will give it as a possession, so that the sons of Ammon may not be remembered among the nations. <verse eid="EZK 25:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 25:11"/>And against Moab I will make judgments, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 25:11"/></para>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Edom</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 25:12"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because Edom acted by taking vengeance against the house of Judah, so they incurred grievous guilt in the avenging themselves on them. <verse eid="EZK 25:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 25:13"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: I will stretch out My hand against Edom, and will cut off from it man and beast, and I will give it as a desolation; from Teman and to Dedan they will fall by the sword. <verse eid="EZK 25:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 25:14"/>And I will lay My vengeance on Edom by the hand of My people Israel, and they will act in Edom according to My anger and according to My fury, and they will know My vengeance, a declaration of the Lord YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 25:14"/></para>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against the Philistines</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 25:15"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because the Philistines acted with vengeance and took vengeance with scorn in the soul, to destroy with ancient hostility, <verse eid="EZK 25:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 25:16"/>therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I am stretching out My hand against the Philistines, and I will cut off the Cherethites, and I will destroy the remnant of the coast of the sea. <verse eid="EZK 25:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 25:17"/>And I will execute against them great vengeance, with rebukes of fury, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH when I lay My vengeance upon them!’” <verse eid="EZK 25:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 25"/>

<chapter number="26" style="c" sid="EZK 26"/>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Tyre</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 26:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Isaiah 23:1–18</char></note>And it came to pass in the eleventh <char style="add">month of the twelfth</char> year,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Likely reading of the original Hebrew text; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And it came to pass in the eleventh year</char></note> on the first of the month, <char style="add">that</char> came the word of YHWH to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 26:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 26:2"/>“Son of man, because that Tyre has said concerning Jerusalem, ‘Aha, she is broken, the gate of the peoples—she is turned over to me; I will be filled; she is destroyed,’ <verse eid="EZK 26:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 26:3"/>therefore thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you, O Tyre, and I will bring up against you many nations, as the sea brings up its waves. <verse eid="EZK 26:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 26:4"/>And they will destroy the walls of Tyre, and they will throw down her towers; and I will scrape her dust from her, and will give her as a clear place of a rock. <verse eid="EZK 26:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 26:5"/>She will be a spreading place of nets in the midst of the sea—for I have spoken, says the Lord YHWH—and she will become as plunder for the nations, <verse eid="EZK 26:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 26:6"/>and her daughters who are on her mainland will be slain by the sword, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 26:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 26:7"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I am bringing against Tyre Nebuchadnezzar<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Nebuchadrezzar</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, a variant of </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Nebuchadnezzar</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (king of Babylon). The latter spelling is used throughout Ezekiel for consistency.</char></note> king of Babylon from the north, the king of kings, with horses, and with chariots, and with horsemen, even an assembly, and a numerous people. <verse eid="EZK 26:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 26:8"/>Your daughters on the mainland he will slay with the sword, and he will set against you a siege mound, and he will build against you a wall and raise against you a buckler; <verse eid="EZK 26:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 26:9"/>and the blow of his battering ram he will place against your walls, and your towers he will tear down with his swords. <verse eid="EZK 26:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 26:10"/>From the abundance of his horses will cover you their dust, <char style="add">and</char> from the noise of the horsemen, and the wagons, and the chariots, your walls will shake in his coming in your gates, like those entering a city having been breached. <verse eid="EZK 26:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 26:11"/>With the hooves of his horses he will trample all your streets; your people he will slay with the sword, and the pillars of your strength will come down to the ground. <verse eid="EZK 26:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 26:12"/>And they will plunder your riches, and they will seize your merchandise; they will throw down your walls, and the houses of your desire they will tear down; and your stones and your timber and your soil they will put in the midst of the waters. <verse eid="EZK 26:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 26:13"/>And the roar of your songs I will make cease, and the sound of your harps will be heard no more. <verse eid="EZK 26:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 26:14"/>And I will give you as a clear place of a rock; you will be a spreading place of nets; you will not be rebuilt anymore! For I, YHWH, have spoken,’ a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 26:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 26:15"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH to Tyre: ‘Will not—at the sound of your downfall, with the groaning of the wounded, with the great slaughter in your midst—the coastlands quake? <verse eid="EZK 26:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 26:16"/>And will come down from upon their thrones all the princes of the sea, and they will lay aside their robes, and the garments of their embroidery they will strip off; with trembling they will clothe themselves, <char style="add">and</char> upon the ground they will sit and tremble at <char style="add">every</char> moment, and they will be appalled over you. <verse eid="EZK 26:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 26:17"/>And they will take up over you a lamentation, and they will say to you: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 26:17">“How you have perished, one inhabited from the seas, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:17">O city renowned, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 26:17">who was strong on the sea—she and those dwelling in her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:17">who gave out their terror to all those dwelling by her! <verse eid="EZK 26:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 26:18"/>Now the coastlands tremble </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:18">on the day of your downfall, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 26:18">and are dismayed the islands that <char style="add">are</char> in the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 26:18">at your going out.”’ <verse eid="EZK 26:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 26:19"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘In My making you a desolate city, like the cities that are not inhabited, in bringing up upon you the deep, that the great waters should cover you, <verse eid="EZK 26:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 26:20"/>I will bring you down with those going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit, to the people of old, and I will make you dwell within the earth, <char style="add">in</char> the places below, like the ruins of old—with those going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit, so that you will not be inhabited or set in splendor<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">or take your place</char></note> in the land of the living. <verse eid="EZK 26:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 26:21"/>I will make you a terror, and you will be no more; and you will be sought, and you will not be found anymore forever,’ a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 26:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 26"/>

<chapter number="27" style="c" sid="EZK 27"/>

<para style="s">A Lament for Tyre</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 27:1"/>And the word came of YHWH to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 27:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 27:2"/>“And you, son of man, take up concerning Tyre a lamentation, <verse eid="EZK 27:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 27:3"/>and to Tyre, the one dwelling at the entrances of the sea, being merchant of the peoples on many coasts, say, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:3">O Tyre, you have said: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:3">‘I <char style="add">am</char> perfect in beauty.’ <verse eid="EZK 27:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 27:4"/>In the midst of the seas <char style="add">are</char> your borders, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:4"><char style="add">and</char> your builders have perfected your beauty. <verse eid="EZK 27:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 27:5"/>With cypress<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">pine</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">juniper</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">fir</char></note> from Senir<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Mount Hermon</char></note> they have built for you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:5">all <char style="add">your</char> planks; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:5">a cedar from Lebanon they took </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:5">to make a mast for you. <verse eid="EZK 27:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 27:6"/>Of oaks from Bashan </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:6">they made your oars; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:6">your boards they have made with ivory, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:6">of the daughter of the Ashurites from the coasts of Kittim.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Cyprus</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 27:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 27:7"/>Of fine linen with embroidery from Egypt </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:7">was your sail, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:7">to be for you a banner; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:7">blue and purple from the coasts of Elishah </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:7">was your awning. <verse eid="EZK 27:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 27:8"/>Those dwelling in Sidon and Arvad </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:8">were the rowers for you; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:8">your wise men, O Tyre, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:8">were in you—they <char style="add">were</char> your pilots. <verse eid="EZK 27:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 27:9"/>Elders of Gebal and her wise men were in you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:9">strengthening your breaches; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:9">all the ships of the sea and their sailors were in you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:9">to offer merchandise to you. <verse eid="EZK 27:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 27:10"/>Persia and Lydia and Libya were in your force, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:10">as men of war for you; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:10">shield and helmet they hung within you—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:10">they gave splendor to you. <verse eid="EZK 27:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 27:11"/>The sons of Arvad and Helech </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:11"><char style="add">were</char> on your walls round about, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:11">and the Gammadites </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:11">were on your towers; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:11">their shields they hung on your walls round about—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:11">they perfected your beauty. <verse eid="EZK 27:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 27:12"/>Tarshish <char style="add">was</char> your merchant, from the abundance of all wealth—in silver, iron, tin, and lead—they gave <char style="add">for</char> your wares. <verse eid="EZK 27:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 27:13"/>Javan,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Greece</char></note> Tubal, and Meshech, they traded in souls of man and vessels of bronze—they gave <char style="add">for</char> your merchandise. <verse eid="EZK 27:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 27:14"/>From the house of Togarmah, horses and steeds and mules they gave <char style="add">for</char> your wares. <verse eid="EZK 27:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 27:15"/>The sons of Dedan<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Rhodes</char></note> were your traders, many coastlands <char style="add">were</char> your market of your hand; horns of ivory and ebony they returned as your payment. <verse eid="EZK 27:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 27:16"/>Aram<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Most Hebrew manuscripts; some Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Edom</char></note> <char style="add">was</char> your merchant, from the abundance of your works in turquoise, purple, and embroidery, and fine linen, and corals, and rubies—they gave <char style="add">for</char> your wares. <verse eid="EZK 27:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 27:17"/>Judah and the land of Israel they traded with you in wheat of Minnith, and meal, and honey, and oil, and balm—they gave <char style="add">for</char> your merchandise. <verse eid="EZK 27:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 27:18"/>Damascus traded with you for the abundance of your works, from the abundance of all <char style="add">your</char> wealth—with wine of Helbon and with wool of Sahar. <verse eid="EZK 27:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 27:19"/>And casks of wine from Izal they gave for your wares;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Probable reading; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And Dan and Javan from Uzal gave for your wares</char></note> smoothed iron, cassia,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">calamus</char></note> and cane were among your merchandise.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">were for your merchandise</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 27:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 27:20"/>Dedan was your merchant in saddlecloths for riding. <verse eid="EZK 27:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 27:21"/>Arabia and all the princes of Kedar, they <char style="add">were</char> trading with you in lambs, and rams, and goats—in these they were your merchants. <verse eid="EZK 27:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 27:22"/>The traders of Sheba and Raamah, they traded with you in the choicest of all spice, and in every of precious stone, and gold—they gave <char style="add">for</char> your wares. <verse eid="EZK 27:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 27:23"/>Haran, and Canneh, and Eden, were traders of Sheba, Assyria, <char style="add">and</char> Chilmad traded with you; <verse eid="EZK 27:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 27:24"/>they traded with you—in fine, garments of blue, embroidered work, rugs and multicolored, with cords tightly twisted and knotted—for your marketplace. <verse eid="EZK 27:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 27:25"/>The ships of Tarshish<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A fleet of trading ships</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:25">were the transporters of your merchandise, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:25">and you were full and very heavy </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:25">in the midst of the seas. <verse eid="EZK 27:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 27:26"/>Into many waters they have brought you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:26">those rowing for you; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:26">a wind from the east has broken you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:26">in the midst of the seas. <verse eid="EZK 27:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 27:27"/>Your riches, and your wares, your merchandise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:27">your mariners, and your pilots, the repairers of your breach<char style="add">es</char>, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:27">and those offering your merchandise, and all <char style="add">your</char> men of war who <char style="add">are</char> in you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:27">and all your assembled <char style="add">force</char> which <char style="add">is</char> in your midst, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:27">will fall into the midst of the seas </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:27">on the day of your downfall! <verse eid="EZK 27:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 27:28"/>At the sound of the cry of your sailors </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:28">the common lands will shake, <verse eid="EZK 27:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 27:29"/>and they will come down from their ships—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:29">all those handling the oar, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:29">the mariners <char style="add">and</char> all the sailors of the sea </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:29">will stand at the shore. <verse eid="EZK 27:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 27:30"/>And they will make heard over you their voice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:30">and they will cry out bitterly, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:30">and they will bring up dust upon their heads; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:30">they will roll about in ashes. <verse eid="EZK 27:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 27:31"/>And they will shave themselves bald because of you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:31">and they will gird themselves with sackcloth </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:31">and weep for you with bitterness of heart—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:31">bitter wailing. <verse eid="EZK 27:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 27:32"/>And they will lift up a lamentation for you in their wailing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:32">and they will lament over you: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:32">‘Who <char style="add">was</char> like Tyre, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:32">silenced in the midst of the sea? <verse eid="EZK 27:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 27:33"/>In the going forth of your wares from the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:33">you satisfied many people; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:33">with the abundance of your wealth and your merchandise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:33">you enriched the kings of the earth. <verse eid="EZK 27:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 27:34"/>In time <char style="add">you</char> are broken by the seas, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:34">in the depths of the waters; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:34">your merchandise and all your assembly </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:34">have fallen in your midst. <verse eid="EZK 27:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 27:35"/>All those dwelling in the coasts </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:35">are appalled over you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:35">and their kings bristle <char style="add">with</char> bristling; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:35">the faces trembled. <verse eid="EZK 27:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 27:36"/>The traders among the nations </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:36">hiss at you; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 27:36">you have become a horror, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 27:36">and you will be no more, even to forever!’” <verse eid="EZK 27:36"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 27"/>

<chapter number="28" style="c" sid="EZK 28"/>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against the Ruler of Tyre</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 28:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 28:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 28:2"/>“Son of man, say to the prince of Tyre, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:2">Because your heart is lifted up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:2">and you say, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:2">‘I <char style="add">am</char> a god; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:2">I sit in the seat of gods, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:2">in the midst of the seas,’ </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:2">and you <char style="add">are</char> a man and not a god, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:2">and you give your heart </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:2">as the heart of a god, <verse eid="EZK 28:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 28:3"/>behold, you <char style="add">are</char> wiser than Daniel—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:3">anything hidden is not in the dark for you! <verse eid="EZK 28:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 28:4"/>With your wisdom and with your understanding </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:4">you have made for yourself wealth, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:4">and you have made gold and silver </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:4">in your treasuries. <verse eid="EZK 28:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 28:5"/>By the abundance of your wisdom in trading </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:5">you have increased your wealth, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:5">and your heart is lifted high </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:5">in your wealth. <verse eid="EZK 28:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 28:6"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:6">Because you have given your heart </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:6">as the heart of a god, <verse eid="EZK 28:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 28:7"/>therefore, behold, I am bringing upon you strangers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:7">the ruthless of the nations! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:7">And they will draw out their swords </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:7">against the beauty of your wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:7">and they will defile your splendor. <verse eid="EZK 28:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 28:8"/>They bring you down into the Pit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:8">and you will die the death of the slain </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:8">in the midst of the seas! <verse eid="EZK 28:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 28:9"/>Will you really say, ‘I <char style="add">am</char> a god,’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:9">before the face of the One slaying you </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:9">and you <char style="add">are</char> a man and not a god </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:9">in the hand of the One slaying you? <verse eid="EZK 28:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 28:10"/>You will die the death of the uncircumcised, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:10">by the hand of strangers. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:10">For I have spoken, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 28:10">a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 28:10"/></para>

<para style="s">A Lament for the King of Tyre</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 28:11"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 28:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 28:12"/>“Son of man, take up a lamentation for the king of Tyre, and say to him, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:12">‘You were the seal of perfection, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:12">full of wisdom and perfect in beauty! <verse eid="EZK 28:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 28:13"/>You were in Eden, the garden of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13"><char style="add">with</char> every precious stone your covering—<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The precise identification of some of these gemstones is uncertain.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:13">ruby, topaz, and diamond; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13">beryl, onyx, and jasper; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13">sapphire,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">lapis lazuli</char></note> turquoise, and emerald; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:13">and of gold <char style="add">was</char> the workmanship of your timbrels and pipes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:13">established for you on the day of your creation. <verse eid="EZK 28:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 28:14"/>You <char style="add">were</char> a cherub </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:14">anointed as a guardian, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:14">and I set you on the mountain of the holiness of God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:14">you were in the midst of the stones of fire; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:14">you walked about. <verse eid="EZK 28:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 28:15"/>Perfect you <char style="add">were</char> in your ways </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:15">from the day you were created, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:15">until iniquity was found in you. <verse eid="EZK 28:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 28:16"/>With the abundance of your trading, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:16">your midst became filled with violence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:16">and you sinned; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:16">and I drove you in disgrace </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:16">from the mountain of God, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:16">and I made you depart, O guardian cherub, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:16">from the midst of the stones of fire. <verse eid="EZK 28:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 28:17"/>Your heart was lifted up in your beauty; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:17">you corrupted your wisdom for the sake of your splendor! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:17">Upon the ground I cast you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:17">before the faces of kings I set you that they might gaze at you. <verse eid="EZK 28:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 28:18"/>By the multitude of your iniquities, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:18">with the injustice of your trading, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:18">you have profaned your holy places. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:18">And I have brought forth fire from your midst; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:18">it has devoured you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:18">and I have given you to ashes upon the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:18">before the eyes of all those looking at you! <verse eid="EZK 28:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 28:19"/>All knowing you among the peoples </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:19">are appalled over you; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:19">you have become a horror, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:19">and you will be no more, even to forever!’” <verse eid="EZK 28:19"/></para>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Sidon</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 28:20"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 28:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 28:21"/>“Son of man, set your face toward Sidon, and prophesy against her. <verse eid="EZK 28:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 28:22"/>And say, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:22">‘Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you, O Sidon, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:22">and I will be glorified in your midst; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:22">and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:22">in my making judgments against her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:22">and I display My holiness against her. <verse eid="EZK 28:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 28:23"/>For I will send against her pestilence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:23">and blood in her streets; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:23">and the slain will fall in her midst, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 28:23">by the sword against her on every side—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 28:23">and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH! <verse eid="EZK 28:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 28:24"/>And there will be no longer for the house of Israel a brier bringing malice or a thorn giving pain from all those around them <char style="add">who</char> despise them; and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> the Lord YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 28:24"/></para>

<para style="s">The Restoration of IsraelJeremiah 30:1–17</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 28:25"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘In My gathering the house of Israel from the peoples, among whom they are scattered, and I will show Myself holy among them before the eyes of the nations, and they will dwell in their own land that I gave to My servant Jacob. <verse eid="EZK 28:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 28:26"/>And they will dwell upon it in safety, and they will build houses and plant vineyards, and they will dwell in safety, with My making judgments against all those despising them from around them. And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH their God.’” <verse eid="EZK 28:26"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 28"/>

<chapter number="29" style="c" sid="EZK 29"/>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Pharaoh</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 29:1"/>In the tenth year, in the tenth <char style="add">month</char>, on the twelfth of the month, the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 29:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 29:2"/>“Son of man, set your face against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and prophesy against him and against all Egypt. <verse eid="EZK 29:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 29:3"/>Speak and say, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:3">Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:3">O Pharaoh king of Egypt, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:3">O great monster stretching out </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:3">in the midst of his rivers, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:3">who has said, ‘Unto me <char style="add">is</char> my River, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:3">and I—have made <char style="add">it</char> for myself!’ <verse eid="EZK 29:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 29:4"/>And I will put hooks in your jaws, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:4">and the fish of your rivers I will cause to cling </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:4">on your scales; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:4">and I will bring you up from the midst of your rivers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:4">and all the fish of your rivers </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:4">to your scales will cling. <verse eid="EZK 29:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 29:5"/>And I will leave you in the desert—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:5">you and all the fish of your rivers; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:5">you will fall on the face of the ground, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:5"><char style="add">and</char> you will not be gathered up </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:5">and you will not be gathered together, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:5">for the beasts of the land </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:5">and for the birds of the heavens </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:5">I will give you as food! <verse eid="EZK 29:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 29:6"/>And all those dwelling in Egypt will know </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:6">that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:6">because they have been a staff of a reed </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:6">to the house of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 29:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 29:7"/>In their grabbing hold of you with the hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:7">you broke and would tear every shoulder of theirs; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 29:7">and in their leaning on you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 29:7">you broke and wrenched all their backs.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Syriac (see also LXX and Vulgate); Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and you caused their loins to shake.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 29:7"/></para>

<para style="s">The Desolation of Egypt</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 29:8"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I am bringing upon you a sword, and I will cut off from you man and beast. <verse eid="EZK 29:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 29:9"/>And the land of Egypt will become a desolation and a ruin, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. Because he said, ‘The River <char style="add">is</char> unto me, and I have made <char style="add">it</char>,’ <verse eid="EZK 29:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 29:10"/>therefore, behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you and against your rivers, and I will give the land of Egypt as a ruin, a desolate wasteland, from Migdol <char style="add">to</char> Syene and to the border of Cush.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the upper Nile region</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 29:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 29:11"/>The foot of man will not pass through it, and the foot of beast will not pass through it, and it will not be inhabited forty years. <verse eid="EZK 29:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 29:12"/>And I will give the land of Egypt to <char style="add">be</char> a desolation in the midst of desolate lands, and her cities, in the midst of the cities laid waste, will be a desolation forty years; and I will disperse Egypt among the nations, and I will scatter them among the lands. <verse eid="EZK 29:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 29:13"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: At the end of forty years I will gather Egypt from the peoples among whom they were scattered there, <verse eid="EZK 29:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 29:14"/>and I will turn back the captivity of Egypt,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and I will restore the fortunes of Egypt</char></note> and will return them <char style="add">to</char> the land of Pathros, to the land of their origin; and there they will be a lowly kingdom. <verse eid="EZK 29:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 29:15"/>It will be the lowest of the kingdoms, and it will not lift itself again over the nations—and I will diminish them; they will no longer rule over the nations. <verse eid="EZK 29:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 29:16"/>And it will be no longer the confidence of the house of Israel, bringing to mind the iniquity in their turning after them; and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 29:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Egypt the Reward of Nebuchadnezzar</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 29:17"/>And it came to pass, in the twenty-seventh year, in the first <char style="add">month</char>, on the first of the month, <char style="add">that</char> the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 29:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 29:18"/>“Son of man, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon caused to labor his army <char style="add">with</char> great labor against Tyre—every head having been made bald and every shoulder rubbed bare. And wages did not were unto him and unto his army from Tyre for the labor <char style="add">with</char> which they labored over it. <verse eid="EZK 29:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 29:19"/>Therefore thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I am giving to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon the land of Egypt; and he will carry away her wealth, and he will draw out her plunder, and he will spoil her loot—and it will be the wages for his army. <verse eid="EZK 29:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 29:20"/><char style="add">As</char> his wage that he has labored over, I have given to him the land of Egypt, because they worked for Me, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 29:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 29:21"/>On that day I will cause to spring forth a horn for the house of Israel, and unto you I will give an opening of your mouth in their midst, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 29:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 29"/>

<chapter number="30" style="c" sid="EZK 30"/>

<para style="s">A Lament for Egypt</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 30:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 30:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 30:2"/>“Son of man, prophesy and say, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:2">‘Wail, alas, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:2">for the day!’ <verse eid="EZK 30:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 30:3"/>For near <char style="add">is</char> the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:3">near <char style="add">is</char> the day of YHWH—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:3">a day of clouds, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:3">a time of the nations it will be! <verse eid="EZK 30:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 30:4"/>And a sword will come against Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:4">and there will be anguish in Cush<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the upper Nile region; also in verses 5 and 9</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:4">at the falling of the slain in Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:4">and they will take away her wealth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:4">and they will tear down her foundations. <verse eid="EZK 30:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 30:5"/>Cush, and Put, and Lud,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Lydia</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:5">and all the mixture, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:5">and libya, and the sons of the land of the covenant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:5">they will fall with them by the sword. <verse eid="EZK 30:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 30:6"/>Thus says YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:6">And will fall those upholding Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:6">and will come down the pride of her strength; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:6">from Migdol <char style="add">to</char> Syene,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Aswan; see Isaiah 49:12</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:6">they will fall by the sword within her, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 30:6">a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 30:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 30:7"/>And they will be desolate in the midst of desolate lands, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:7">and her cities will be in the midst of the cities laid waste. <verse eid="EZK 30:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 30:8"/>And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:8">in My giving forth a fire in Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:8">so that are broken all her helpers. <verse eid="EZK 30:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 30:9"/>On that day messengers will go forth from before My face in ships, to make tremble the confident Cush, and there will be anguish among them, as on the day of Egypt, for behold, it is coming! <verse eid="EZK 30:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 30:10"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:10">The wealth of Egypt I will bring to an end </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:10">by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon. <verse eid="EZK 30:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 30:11"/>He and his people with him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:11">the <char style="add">most</char> ruthless of the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:11">will be brought to destroy the land; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:11">and they will draw out their swords against Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:11">and they will fill the land <char style="add">with</char> the slain. <verse eid="EZK 30:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 30:12"/>I will make the rivers into dry ground, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:12">and will sell the land into the hand of the wicked; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:12">I will make desolate the land and its fullness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:12">by the hand of strangers. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 30:12">I, YHWH, have spoken. <verse eid="EZK 30:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 30:13"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:13">And I will destroy the idols, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:13">and I will put end to the images from Memphis;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Noph</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 16</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:13">and a prince from the land of Egypt will be no more, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:13">and I will put a fear in the land of Egypt. <verse eid="EZK 30:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 30:14"/>And Pathros I will make desolate, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:14">and I will give forth fire against Zoan, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:14">and I will make judgments on Thebes.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">No</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 15 and 16</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 30:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 30:15"/>And I will pour out My fury on Pelusium,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Sin</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 16</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:15">the strength of Egypt; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:15">and I will cut off the crowd of Thebes. <verse eid="EZK 30:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 30:16"/>And I will give forth a fire in Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:16">Pelusium will writhe in anguish, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:16">and Thebes will be split open, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:16">and Memphis <char style="add">has</char> daily distress. <verse eid="EZK 30:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 30:17"/>The young men of On and Pi-Beseth<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Heliopolis and Bubastis</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, as in LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Aven and Pi-beseth</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:17">will fall by the sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:17">and they will go into captivity. <verse eid="EZK 30:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 30:18"/>And at Tahpanhes will be held back the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:18">in my breaking there the yoke of Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:18">and will cease in her the pride of her strength; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 30:18"><char style="add">as for</char> her, a cloud will cover her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:18">and her daughters will go into captivity. <verse eid="EZK 30:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 30:19"/>And I will make judgments against Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 30:19">and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 30:19"/></para>

<para style="s">Pharaoh’s Power Broken</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 30:20"/>And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the first <char style="add">month</char>, on the seventh of the month, <char style="add">that</char> the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 30:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 30:21"/>“Son of man, I have broken the arm of Pharaoh king of Egypt, and behold, it has not been bound up to give healing, to put a bandage to bind it, for strength to hold the sword. <verse eid="EZK 30:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 30:22"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and I will break his arms, the strong one and the broken one, and I will make the sword fall from his hand. <verse eid="EZK 30:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 30:23"/>And I will disperse Egypt among the nations, and I will scatter them among the lands. <verse eid="EZK 30:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 30:24"/>And I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and I will put My sword in his hand. And I will break the arms of Pharaoh, and he will groan the groans of a wounded one before him. <verse eid="EZK 30:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 30:25"/>And I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and the arms of Pharaoh will fall down. And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH in My putting My sword into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he will stretch it out against the land of Egypt. <verse eid="EZK 30:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 30:26"/>And I will disperse Egypt among the nations, and will scatter them among the lands, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 30:26"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 30"/>

<chapter number="31" style="c" sid="EZK 31"/>

<para style="s">Egypt Will Fall like Assyria</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 31:1"/>And it came to pass, in the eleventh year, in the third <char style="add">month</char>, on the first of the month, <char style="add">that</char> the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 31:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 31:2"/>“Son of man, say to Pharaoh king of Egypt and to his multitude: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:2">‘To whom do you compare </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:2">your greatness? <verse eid="EZK 31:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 31:3"/>Behold, Assyria <char style="add">was</char> a cedar in Lebanon, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:3">beautiful of branches and giving shade to the forest </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:3">and high of stature, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:3">and among the clouds was its top. <verse eid="EZK 31:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 31:4"/>The waters made it grow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:4">the deep gave it height </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:4">with her rivers running around the place of her planting, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:4">and her conduits she sent out to all the trees of the field. <verse eid="EZK 31:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 31:5"/>Upon thus its height was exalted </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:5">above all the trees of the field, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:5">and its boughs were multiplied, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:5">and its branches became long </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:5">from the abundant waters </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:5">in its sending forth. <verse eid="EZK 31:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 31:6"/>In its boughs made their nests </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:6">all the birds of the heavens, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:6">and under its branches gave birth </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:6">all the beasts of the field, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:6">and in its shade dwelt </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:6">all the great nations. <verse eid="EZK 31:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 31:7"/>And it was beautiful in its greatness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:7">in the length of its branches, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:7">because its root was </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:7">to abundant waters. <verse eid="EZK 31:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 31:8"/>The cedars could not darken it </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:8">in the garden of God; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:8">the fir trees<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">pines</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">junipers</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">firs</char></note> were not like unto its boughs, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:8">and the plane trees<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Possibly </char><char style="fq" closed="false">chestnut</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">juniper</char></note> were not like its branches; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 31:8">there was no tree in the garden of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:8">not <char style="add">any</char> like it in its beauty. <verse eid="EZK 31:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 31:9"/>Beautiful I made it with an abundance of branches, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:9">and envied all the trees of Eden </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 31:9">that <char style="add">were</char> in the garden of God.’ <verse eid="EZK 31:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 31:10"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Because that you became great in height, and it set its top to among the thick boughs,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">among the clouds</char></note> and was lifted up its heart in its height, <verse eid="EZK 31:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 31:11"/>so I will give it into the hand of the mighty one of the nations, and he will deal severely with it according to its wickedness! I have driven it out, <verse eid="EZK 31:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 31:12"/>and foreigners have cut it down, the most ruthless of the nations. And they have left it on the mountains, and in all the valleys its branches have fallen, and its boughs lie broken by all the rivers of the land. And all the peoples of the earth have gone out from its shade, and they have left it. <verse eid="EZK 31:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 31:13"/>On its carcass will dwell all the birds of the heavens, and on its branches will be all the beasts of the field, <verse eid="EZK 31:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 31:14"/>in order that not any trees by the waters will exalt in their height, and they will not give their tops to among the thick boughs. All those drinking from the waters should not reach their oaks to their height, for they all have been given to death, to the land <char style="add">far</char> below, in the midst of the sons of men, with those going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit.’ <verse eid="EZK 31:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 31:15"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘On the day of its going down to Sheol, I caused mourning; I covered over it the deep, and I held back its rivers, and were cut off the great waters; and Lebanon I caused to mourn over it, and all the trees of the field fainted because of it. <verse eid="EZK 31:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 31:16"/>At the sound of its fall, I made the nations quake, in My casting it down to Sheol together with those going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit. And were comforted in the land below all the trees of Eden, the choicest and best of Lebanon, all those drinking the waters. <verse eid="EZK 31:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 31:17"/>They also went down with it to Sheol, with those slain by the sword—and its arm who had dwelt in its shade in the midst of nations. <verse eid="EZK 31:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 31:18"/>To whom, then, will you be compared, in glory and in greatness, among the trees in Eden? You also will be brought down with the trees of Eden to the land below; in the midst of the uncircumcised you will lie, with those slain by the sword. That <char style="add">is</char> Pharaoh and all his multitude, a declaration of the Lord YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 31:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 31"/>

<chapter number="32" style="c" sid="EZK 32"/>

<para style="s">A Lament for Pharaoh King of Egypt</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 32:1"/>And it came to pass, in the twelfth year, in the twelfth month, on the first of the month, <char style="add">that</char> the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 32:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 32:2"/>“Son of man, take up a lamentation for Pharaoh king of Egypt, and say to him: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:2">‘To a young lion of the nations you may be compared, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:2">and you <char style="add">are</char> like the monster in the seas. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:2">You burst forth in your rivers </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:2">and you stir up the waters with your feet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:2">and you muddy their rivers.’ <verse eid="EZK 32:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 32:3"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:3">‘And I will spread over you My net </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:3">with a throng of many peoples, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:3">and they will draw you up in My net. <verse eid="EZK 32:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 32:4"/>And I will leave you on the land; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:4">upon the face of the field I will throw you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:4">and I will make dwell upon you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:4">all the birds of the heavens, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:4">and I will give the fill of you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:4"><char style="add">to</char> the beasts of all the earth. <verse eid="EZK 32:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 32:5"/>And I will lay your flesh upon the mountains, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:5">and I will fill the valleys with your remains.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with your lofty stature</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 32:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 32:6"/>And I will water the land </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:6">with the flow of your blood, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:6">up to the mountains, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:6">and the ravines will be full of you. <verse eid="EZK 32:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 32:7"/>And in My quenching of you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:7">I will cover the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:7">and I will make dark their stars; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:7">I will cover the sun with a cloud, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:7">and the moon will not radiate her light. <verse eid="EZK 32:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 32:8"/>All luminaries of light in the heavens </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:8">I will make dark because of you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:8">and I will put darkness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:8">over your land,’ </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 32:8">a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 32:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 32:9"/>‘And I will trouble the hearts of many peoples, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:9">in My bringing your destruction among the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:9">over lands<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">when I lead you into captivity among the nations, into countries</char></note> that you have not known. <verse eid="EZK 32:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 32:10"/>And many peoples </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:10">I will cause to be appalled over you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:10">and their kings will shudder over you <char style="add">with</char> shuddering, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:10">in My making fly My sword in front of their faces; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:10">and they will tremble at every moment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:10">each man for his soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:10">on the day of your fall!’ <verse eid="EZK 32:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 32:11"/>For thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:11">‘The sword of the king of Babylon </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:11">will come against you. <verse eid="EZK 32:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 32:12"/>By the swords of mighty ones </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:12">your multitude I will cause to fall—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:12">the most ruthless of nations, all of them. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:12">And they will plunder the pride of Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:12">and all will be destroyed her multitude. <verse eid="EZK 32:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 32:13"/>And I will destroy all her animals </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:13">from beside her great waters; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:13">and no foot of man will stir them up anymore, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:13">and the hooves of animals will not stir them up. <verse eid="EZK 32:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 32:14"/>Then their waters I will let settle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:14">and their rivers I will make run like oil,’ </para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 32:14">a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 32:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 32:15"/>‘In My making the land of Egypt a desolation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:15">and the land being desolate of its fullness, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:15">in My striking all those dwelling in it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:15">they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH!’ <verse eid="EZK 32:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 32:16"/>It <char style="add">is</char> a lamentation they will lament her; the daughters of the nations will lament her, over Egypt and over all her multitude, they will lament her, a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 32:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Egypt Cast into the Pit</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 32:17"/>And it came to pass, in the twelfth year, on the fifteenth of the month,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Presumably the fifteenth day of the twelfth month (see verse 1); LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on the fifteenth day of the first month</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> that the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 32:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 32:18"/>“Son of man, wail over the multitude of Egypt, and send it down—her and the daughters of the mighty nations—to the land below, with those going down to the Pit. <verse eid="EZK 32:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 32:19"/>Whom are you pleasing? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:19">Go down, and lie down with the uncircumcised! <verse eid="EZK 32:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 32:20"/>In the midst of those slain by the sword they will fall; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:20"><char style="add">to</char> the sword she is given—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:20">let her be dragged away </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:20">and all her multitudes. <verse eid="EZK 32:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 32:21"/>The chiefs of the mighty ones will speak concerning him from the midst of Sheol, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:21">with his helpers: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:21">‘They have gone down, they have lain down with the uncircumcised, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:21">those slain by the sword.’ <verse eid="EZK 32:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 32:22"/>There <char style="add">is</char> Assyria and all her throng </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:22">surrounding it with its graves, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:22">all of them slain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:22">having fallen by the sword, <verse eid="EZK 32:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 32:23"/>of whom her graves are appointed in the far sides of the Pit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:23">and her assembly is all around her grave, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:23">all of them slain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:23">having fallen by the sword, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:23">those who gave forth terror </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:23">in the land of the living. <verse eid="EZK 32:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 32:24"/>There <char style="add">is</char> Elam </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:24">and all her multitude, surrounding her grave, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:24">all of them slain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:24">having fallen by the sword, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:24">those who have gone down uncircumcised </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:24">to the land below, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:24">those who gave forth their terror </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:24">in the land of the living; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:24">and they bear their shame </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:24">with those going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit. <verse eid="EZK 32:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 32:25"/>In the midst of the slain they set </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:25">a bed for her, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:25">with all her multitude </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:25">all around it with her graves, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:25">all of them uncircumcised </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:25">slain by the sword. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:25">Though their terror was given forth </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:25">in the land of the living, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:25">they bear their shame </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:25">with those going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:25">in the midst of the slain they are placed. <verse eid="EZK 32:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 32:26"/>There <char style="add">are</char> Meshech and Tubal, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:26">and all her multitude </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:26">around it with her graves, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:26">all of them uncircumcised </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:26">slain by the sword, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:26">though they gave forth their terror </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:26">in the land of the living. <verse eid="EZK 32:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 32:27"/>And they lie down, not with the mighty ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:27">those having fallen of old,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">those having fallen of the uncircumcised</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:27">who have gone down <char style="add">to</char> Sheol </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:27">with their weapons of war; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:27">and they have laid their swords under their heads, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:27">and their shields<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Likely reading of the original Hebrew text; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">iniquities</char></note> will be upon their bones, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:27">for the terror of the mighty ones </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:27">in the land of the living. <verse eid="EZK 32:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 32:28"/>And you, in the midst of the uncircumcised, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:28">you will be broken, and you will lie </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:28">with those slain by the sword. <verse eid="EZK 32:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 32:29"/>There <char style="add">is</char> Edom—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:29">her kings, and all her princes, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:29">who were given </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:29">in their strength among those slain by the sword; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:29">they will lie down with the uncircumcised, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:29">and with those going down to the Pit. <verse eid="EZK 32:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 32:30"/>There <char style="add">are</char> the princes of the north, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:30">all of them and every Sidonian, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:30">those who have gone down ashamed with the slain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:30">with their terror by their might; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:30">they lie uncircumcised </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:30">with those slain by the sword, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:30">and they must bear their shame </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:30">with those going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit. <verse eid="EZK 32:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 32:31"/>Them Pharaoh will see, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:31">and he will be comforted over all his multitude </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:31">slain by the sword—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:31">Pharaoh and all his force—</para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 32:31">a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 32:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 32:32"/>For I give forth My terror </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:32">in the land of the living, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 32:32">and he will be made to lie down in the midst of the uncircumcised, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:32">with those slain by the sword—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 32:32">Pharaoh and all his throng—</para>

<para style="qs" vid="EZK 32:32">a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 32:32"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 32"/>

<chapter number="33" style="c" sid="EZK 33"/>

<para style="s">Ezekiel the Watchman for Israel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 33:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 33:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 33:2"/>“Son of man, speak to the sons of your people, and say to them: ‘A land, when I bring upon it the sword, and the people of the land take a single man from their borders and set him to them as watchman, <verse eid="EZK 33:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 33:3"/>and he sees the sword coming upon the land, and he blows on the shofar and warns the people, <verse eid="EZK 33:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 33:4"/>then if anyone at all hears the voice of the shofar and has not heeded the warning, when the sword comes and takes him away, his blood will be on his head. <verse eid="EZK 33:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 33:5"/>He heard the voice of the shofar and he did not heed the warning; his blood will be upon himself. And he <char style="add">who</char> has heeded the warning has saved his soul. <verse eid="EZK 33:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 33:6"/>And the watchman, if he sees the sword coming and does not blow on the shofar, and the people are not warned, and the sword comes and takes from among them a soul, he will be taken away in his iniquity, and I will seek his blood from the hand of the watchman.’ <verse eid="EZK 33:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 33:7"/>And you, O son of man, I have made you a watchman for the house of Israel, and you will hear a word from My mouth, and you will give a warning <char style="add">to</char> them from Me. <verse eid="EZK 33:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 33:8"/>In My saying to the wicked, ‘O wicked one, you will surely die,’ <char style="add">if</char> you do not speak to warn the wicked from his way, <char style="add">then</char> that wicked one will die in his iniquity, and I will seek his blood from your hand. <verse eid="EZK 33:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 33:9"/>And you, if if you warn the wicked from his way, to turn from it, and he does not turn from his way, <char style="add">then</char> he will die in his iniquity, and you will have delivered your soul. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">33.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Acts 20:25–26</char></note><verse eid="EZK 33:9"/></para>

<para style="s">The Message of the Watchman</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 33:10"/>Now you, son of man, say to the house of Israel: Thus you⁺ have spoken, saying, ‘Surely our transgressions and our sins <char style="add">are</char> upon us, and in them we rot away! How then can we live?’ <verse eid="EZK 33:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 33:11"/>Say to them: ‘<char style="add">As</char> I live, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, I have no delight in the death of the wicked, but only in turning the wicked from his way that he should live. Turn back, turn back from your⁺ evil ways! For why should you⁺ die, O house of Israel?’ <verse eid="EZK 33:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 33:12"/>And you, son of man, say to the sons of your people: ‘The righteousness of the righteous man will not snatch him up in the day of his transgression, and the wickedness of the wicked will not cause him to stumble because of it in the day of his turning from his wickedness. And the righteous one will not be able to live by it in the day of his sinning.’ <verse eid="EZK 33:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 33:13"/>In My saying to the righteous, ‘He will surely live,’ and he trusts in his righteousness and does iniquity, all his righteousnesses will not be remembered; and because of the iniquity that he did, by it he will die. <verse eid="EZK 33:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 33:14"/>And in My saying to the wicked, ‘You will surely die,’ and he turns from his sin and does what is just and right, <verse eid="EZK 33:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 33:15"/><char style="add">if</char> a wicked one restores a pledge for what he has stolen, makes restitution in the statutes of life, <char style="add">and</char> he walks without doing iniquity, he will surely live; he will not die. <verse eid="EZK 33:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 33:16"/>All his sins that he had sinned, they will not be remembered for him; what is just and right he has done; he will surely live. <verse eid="EZK 33:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 33:17"/>And the sons of your people may say, ‘The way of the Lord is not balanced.’ And they—their way is not balanced. <verse eid="EZK 33:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 33:18"/>In the turning of the righteous from his righteousness, and he has done iniquity, he will die because of it. <verse eid="EZK 33:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 33:19"/>And in the turning of the wicked from his wickedness, and he has done what is just and righteous, because of it he will live. <verse eid="EZK 33:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 33:20"/>And you⁺ say, ‘The way of the Lord is not balanced!’ Each man—according to his ways will I judge you⁺, O house of Israel.” <verse eid="EZK 33:20"/></para>

<para style="s">Word of Jerusalem’s Fall</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 33:21"/>And it came to pass, in the twelfth year of our captivity, in the tenth <char style="add">month</char>, on the fifth of the month, <char style="add">that</char> an escapee came to me from Jerusalem, and he said, “The city has been struck!” <verse eid="EZK 33:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 33:22"/>And the hand of YHWH had been upon me in the evening, before the coming of the escapee, and He had opened my mouth until <char style="add">his</char> coming to me in the morning, and my mouth was opened, and I was not mute any longer. <verse eid="EZK 33:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 33:23"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 33:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 33:24"/>“Son of man, those dwelling in these ruins in the land of Israel are speaking, saying: ‘Abraham was one, and he possessed the land; and we <char style="add">are</char> many—to us the land has been given as a possession!’ <verse eid="EZK 33:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 33:25"/>Therefore say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘You⁺ eat that with the blood, and you⁺ lift up your⁺ eyes toward your⁺ idols, and you⁺ pour out blood—and you⁺ would possess the land? <verse eid="EZK 33:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 33:26"/>You⁺ rely on your⁺ sword, you⁺ commit abominations, and each man defiles the wife of his neighbor—and you⁺ would possess the land?’ <verse eid="EZK 33:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 33:27"/>Thus you shall say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘<char style="add">As</char> I live, surely those who <char style="add">are</char> in the ruins will fall by the sword, and the one who <char style="add">is</char> upon the face of the field I will give to the beasts to eat him, and those who <char style="add">are</char> in the strongholds and in the caves will die by the pestilence. <verse eid="EZK 33:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 33:28"/>And I will give the land as a desolation and a horror, and will cease the pride of its strength, and the mountains of Israel will be desolate, with no one passing through! <verse eid="EZK 33:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 33:29"/>And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, in My giving the land as a desolation and a horror, because of all their abominations that they have done.’ <verse eid="EZK 33:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 33:30"/>And you, son of man, the sons of your people are speaking about you beside the walls and in the doors of the houses, and they speak one to to another, a man to his brother, saying: ‘Come, now, and hear what <char style="add">is</char> the word coming forth from YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 33:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 33:31"/>And they come to you, like the coming of people, and they sit before you—My people, and they hear your words, and they will not do them; for they do loves with their mouth; their heart is pursuing after dishonest gain. <verse eid="EZK 33:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 33:32"/>And behold, you <char style="add">are</char> to them as a song of loves, one beautiful of voice, and playing well on a stringed instrument; for they hear your words, and nthey do ot do them. <verse eid="EZK 33:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 33:33"/>And in the coming of this—<char style="add">and</char> behold, it is coming—they will know that a prophet has been in their midst.” <verse eid="EZK 33:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 33"/>

<chapter number="34" style="c" sid="EZK 34"/>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Israel’s Shepherds</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 34:1"/>And the word came of YHWH to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 34:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 34:2"/>“Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel. Prophesy and say to them—to the shepherds—thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Woe to the shepherds of Israel who have been feeding themselves. Should <char style="add">it</char> not <char style="add">be</char> <char style="add">that</char> the shepherds shepherd the flock? <verse eid="EZK 34:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 34:3"/>You⁺ eat the fat and in wool you⁺ clothe yourselves; you⁺ slaughter the fatlings; you⁺ do not feed the flock. <verse eid="EZK 34:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 34:4"/>Those being weak you⁺ have not strengthened, and those being sick you⁺ have not healed, and those being broken you⁺ have not bandaged, and those driven off you⁺ have not returned, and those being lost you⁺ have not sought, and you⁺ have ruled them with force and with harshness. <verse eid="EZK 34:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 34:5"/>And they were scattered for lack of a shepherd, and they became as food for all the beasts of the field; indeed, they were scattered. <verse eid="EZK 34:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 34:6"/>My flock went astray through all the mountains, and on every high hill; and My flock was scattered over all the face of the earth, and there was not one searching or seeking <char style="add">them</char>.’ <verse eid="EZK 34:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 34:7"/>Therefore, shepherds, hear the word of YHWH! <verse eid="EZK 34:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 34:8"/>‘<char style="add">As</char> I live—a declaration of the Lord YHWH—surely because My flock became as prey, and My flock became as food for every beast of the field, for lack of a shepherd, and My shepherds did not search <char style="add">for</char> My flock, and the shepherds shepherded themselves, and My flock they did not feed. <verse eid="EZK 34:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 34:9"/>Therefore, O shepherds, hear the word of YHWH: <verse eid="EZK 34:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 34:10"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH, ‘Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against the shepherds, and I will require My flock from their hands, and I will make them cease from shepherding the sheep, and the shepherds no longer will shepherd themselves; for I will snatch My flock from their mouths, and they will not be for them as food.’ <verse eid="EZK 34:10"/></para>

<para style="s">The Good ShepherdPsalm 23:1–6</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 34:11"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 10:1–21</char></note>For thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I—I Myself—will search for My flock, and I will seek them. <verse eid="EZK 34:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 34:12"/>As a shepherd seeks out his flock on the day of his being in the midst of his sheep <char style="add">that</char> are scattered, so will I seek out My flock, and I will deliver them from all the places to which they were scattered there on the day of cloud and darkness. <verse eid="EZK 34:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 34:13"/>And I will bring them out from the peoples, and I will gather them from the lands, and I will bring them to their own land, and I will let them graze on the mountains of Israel, in the valleys, and in all the inhabited places of the land. <verse eid="EZK 34:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 34:14"/>I will feed them in good pasture, and on the mountains of the height of Israel will be their grazing land; there they will lie down in good grazing land, and they will feed in rich pasture on the mountains of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 34:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 34:15"/>I will feed My flock, and I will make them lie down, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 34:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 34:16"/>The one being lost I will seek, and the one driven away I will return, and the broken I will bind up, and the one being sick I will strengthen, and the fat one and the strong one I will destroy; I will shepherd her with justice.’ <verse eid="EZK 34:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 34:17"/>And you⁺, My flock, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I am going to judge between sheep and sheep, the rams and the goats. <verse eid="EZK 34:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 34:18"/><char style="add">Is it</char> a little thing for you⁺ to feed on the good pasture, that the remainder of your⁺ pasture-land you⁺ would trample with your⁺ feet? And the clear waters you⁺ drink, that that the remainder you⁺ would muddy with your⁺ feet? <verse eid="EZK 34:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 34:19"/>And My flock, they feed on what you have trampled with your⁺ feet, and they drink what you have muddied with your⁺ feet!’ <verse eid="EZK 34:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 34:20"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH to them: ‘Behold, I—I Myself—will judge between the fat of the flock and between the lean of the flock. <verse eid="EZK 34:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 34:21"/>Because you⁺ have pushed with flank and shoulder, and you⁺ have thrust with your⁺ horns all the weak ones, until that you⁺ have scattered them to the outside, <verse eid="EZK 34:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 34:22"/>I will bring salvation to My flock, and will they be no longer for prey; and I will judge between a sheep and a sheep. <verse eid="EZK 34:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 34:23"/>And I will raise up over them one shepherd, My servant David, and he will feed them—He will feed them and he will be unto them as shepherd. <verse eid="EZK 34:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 34:24"/>And I, YHWH, will be unto them God, and My servant David a prince in their midst. I, YHWH, have spoken. <verse eid="EZK 34:24"/></para>

<para style="s">The Covenant of Peace</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 34:25"/>And I will cut with them a covenant of peace, and the evil beast I will make cease from the land, and they will dwell in the wilderness in safety, and they will sleep in the forests. <verse eid="EZK 34:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 34:26"/>And I will make them and the places around My hill <char style="add">to be</char> a blessing, and I will send down showers in their season; there will be showers of blessing. <verse eid="EZK 34:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 34:27"/>And the trees of the field will give forth their fruit, and the earth will give forth her produce, and they will be upon their land in safety; and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, when I have broken the bands of their yoke and delivered them from the hand of those enslaving them. <verse eid="EZK 34:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 34:28"/>And they will be no longer as prey for the nations, and the beasts of the land will not devour them; and they will dwell in safety, and no one will frighten them. <verse eid="EZK 34:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 34:29"/>And I will raise up for them a planting of renown, and will they be no longer consumed by hunger in the land, and they will bear no more the shame of the nations! <verse eid="EZK 34:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 34:30"/>And they will know that I, YHWH their God, <char style="add">am</char> with them, and they <char style="add">are</char> the house of Israel, My people,’ a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 34:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 34:31"/>‘And you⁺ <char style="add">are</char> My flock, the flock of My pasture. You⁺ <char style="add">are</char> men, I <char style="add">am</char> your⁺ God,’ a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 34:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 34"/>

<chapter number="35" style="c" sid="EZK 35"/>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Mount Seir</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 35:1"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 35:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 35:2"/>“Son of man, set your face against Mount Seir, and prophesy against it. <verse eid="EZK 35:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 35:3"/>And say to it, thus says the Lord YHWH: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 35:3">Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 35:3">O Mount Seir, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 35:3">and I will stretch out My hand against you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 35:3">and I will make you a desolation and a waste. <verse eid="EZK 35:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 35:4"/>I will make your cities a ruin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="EZK 35:4">and you will become a desolation. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 35:4">And you will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 35:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 35:5"/>Because there has been for you an ancient hatred and you have poured out the sons of Israel upon the hands of the sword at the time of their calamity, at the time of the iniquity of the end, <verse eid="EZK 35:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 35:6"/>therefore, <char style="add">as</char> I live, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, now unto blood I appoint you, and blood will pursue you; since you did not hate blood, blood will pursue you. <verse eid="EZK 35:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 35:7"/>And I will make Mount Seir into an utter desolation, and I will cut off from it the one passing by and the one returning. <verse eid="EZK 35:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 35:8"/>And I will fill its mountains with the slain. On your hills, and in your valleys, and in all your ravines, those slain by the sword will fall in them. <verse eid="EZK 35:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 35:9"/>I will make you a desolation forever, and your cities will not be inhabited. You⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 35:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 35:10"/>Because you have said, ‘The two nations and the two lands will be unto me, and we will possess them,’ and YHWH has been there, <verse eid="EZK 35:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 35:11"/>therefore, <char style="add">as</char> I live, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, I will do according to your anger, and according to the jealousy <char style="add">with</char> which you acted in your hatred against them, and I will make Myself known among them when I judge you. <verse eid="EZK 35:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 35:12"/>And you will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. I have heard all your despisings that you have said about the mountains of Israel, saying, ‘They are desolate; they are given to us for food.’ <verse eid="EZK 35:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 35:13"/>Thus you⁺ have boasted against Me with your⁺ mouth, and you⁺ have multiplied against Me your⁺ words—I have heard it Myself. <verse eid="EZK 35:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 35:14"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: According to the rejoicing of all the earth, I will make for you a desolation. <verse eid="EZK 35:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 35:15"/>According to your rejoicing at the inheritance of the house of Israel, upon that it has become desolate, so will I do to you! You will become a desolation, O Mount Seir, and all of Edom—all of it—and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 35:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 35"/>

<chapter number="36" style="c" sid="EZK 36"/>

<para style="s">A Prophecy to the Mountains of Israel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 36:1"/><char style="add">“</char> And you, son of man, prophesy to the mountains of Israel, and say: O mountains of Israel, hear the word of YHWH! <verse eid="EZK 36:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 36:2"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: Because the enemy has said of you⁺, ‘Aha, the heights of old have become as a possession unto us,’ <verse eid="EZK 36:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 36:3"/>therefore prophesy and say, thus says the Lord YHWH: Because, even because of making <char style="add">you⁺</char> desolate and swallowing you⁺ up from all around for your⁺ being the possession of the rest of the nations, and you⁺ were taken up on the lip of the tongue in slander of the people, <verse eid="EZK 36:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 36:4"/>therefore, O mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord YHWH, thus says the Lord YHWH to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys, and to the desolate ruins, and to the abandoned cities that became as plunder and as derision to the rest of the nations that <char style="add">are</char> all around, <verse eid="EZK 36:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 36:5"/>therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: Surely in the burning of My jealousy <char style="add">that</char> I have spoken against the rest of the nations and against Edom—all those who gave My land to themselves as a possession, with joy in all of the heart, <char style="add">and</char> with scorn in the soul, in order to graze upon it as prey. <verse eid="EZK 36:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 36:6"/>Therefore prophesy concerning the land of Israel and say to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys, thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I, in My jealousy and in My fury, have spoken, because you⁺ have carried the shame of the nations. <verse eid="EZK 36:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 36:7"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: I—I have lifted up My hand <char style="add">that</char> surely the nations that <char style="add">are</char> surrounding you⁺, they will bear their own shame! <verse eid="EZK 36:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 36:8"/>And you⁺, O mountains of Israel, your⁺ branches you⁺ will give forth, and your⁺ fruit you⁺ will bear for My people Israel, for they are soon to come in! <verse eid="EZK 36:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 36:9"/>For behold, I <char style="add">am</char> toward you⁺, and I will turn to you⁺, and you⁺ will be tilled and sown. <verse eid="EZK 36:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 36:10"/>And I will multiply upon you⁺ man—all the house of Israel, all of it—and the cities will be inhabited, and the ruins will be rebuilt. <verse eid="EZK 36:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 36:11"/>And I will multiply upon you⁺ man and beast, and they will multiply and will be fruitful; and I will make you⁺ inhabited as of old, and I will make you⁺ prosper more than before, and you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 36:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 36:12"/>And I will cause man to walk over you⁺—My people Israel—they will possess you, and you will be unto them as an inheritance, and you will no more bereave them. <verse eid="EZK 36:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 36:13"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: Because of their saying to you⁺, ‘You are devouring man, and you are bereaving your nations!’ <verse eid="EZK 36:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 36:14"/>Therefore man you will devour no more, and your nations you will not bereave any longer, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 36:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 36:15"/>And I will not let you hear anymore the taunt of the nations, and the reproach of the peoples you will bear no more, and your nation will be made to stumble no longer, a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 36:15"/></para>

<para style="s">A New Heart and a New SpiritRomans 8:9–11</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 36:16"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Galatians 5:16–26</char></note>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 36:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 36:17"/>“Son of man, the house of Israel were dwelling in their own land, and they defiled it by their ways and by their deeds; like the uncleanness of a <char style="add">woman’s</char> impurity was their way before My face. <verse eid="EZK 36:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 36:18"/>And I poured out My fury upon them for the blood that they had poured out upon the land and because they had defiled her with their idols. <verse eid="EZK 36:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 36:19"/>And I dispersed them among the nations, and they were scattered among the lands; according to their ways and according to their deeds I judged them. <verse eid="EZK 36:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 36:20"/>And they came to the nations, <char style="add">to</char> which they came there, and they profaned name of My holiness by saying to them, ‘These <char style="add">are</char> the people of YHWH, and from His land they have gone out!’ <verse eid="EZK 36:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 36:21"/>And I had pity for the name of My holiness, which the house of Israel had profaned among the nations to which they had gone in there. <verse eid="EZK 36:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 36:22"/>Therefore say to the house of Israel, thus says the Lord YHWH: <char style="add">It is</char> not for your⁺ sake <char style="add">that</char> I am doing <char style="add">this</char>, O house of Israel, for but the name of My holiness, which you⁺ have profaned among the nations to which you⁺ have gone in there. <verse eid="EZK 36:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 36:23"/>And I will sanctify My great name, which has been profaned among the nations, which you⁺ have profaned in their midst, and the nations will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, in My showing <char style="add">My</char> holiness in you⁺ before their eyes. <verse eid="EZK 36:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 36:24"/>For I will take you⁺ from the nations, and I will gather you⁺ from all of the lands, and I will bring you⁺ into your⁺ own land. <verse eid="EZK 36:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 36:25"/>And I will sprinkle on you⁺ pure water, and you⁺ will be pure from all your⁺ uncleannesses, and from all your⁺ idols I will purify you⁺. <verse eid="EZK 36:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 36:26"/>And I will give to you⁺ a new heart, and a new spirit I will put within you⁺; and I will take away the heart of stone from your⁺ flesh, and I will give to you⁺ a heart of flesh. <verse eid="EZK 36:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 36:27"/>And My Spirit I will put within you⁺, and I will make <char style="add">it</char> that you⁺ will walk in My statutes and My ordinances you⁺ will keep and you⁺ will do <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="EZK 36:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 36:28"/>And you⁺ will dwell in the land that I gave to your⁺ fathers and you⁺ will be unto Me a people, and I will be unto you⁺ God. <verse eid="EZK 36:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 36:29"/>And I will deliver you⁺ from all your⁺ uncleannesses, and I will call for the grain, and I will multiply it, and I will not put famine upon you⁺. <verse eid="EZK 36:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 36:30"/>And I will multiply the fruit of the tree and the produce of the field, so that you⁺ will no longer receive the reproach of famine among the nations. <verse eid="EZK 36:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 36:31"/>And you⁺ will remember your⁺ evil ways and your⁺ deeds that <char style="add">were</char> not good, and you⁺ will loathe in your⁺ faces over your⁺ iniquities and over your⁺ abominations. <verse eid="EZK 36:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 36:32"/><char style="add">It is</char> not for your⁺ sake <char style="add">that</char> I am doing <char style="add">this</char>, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, let it be known to you⁺. Be ashamed and disgraced for your⁺ ways, O house of Israel! <verse eid="EZK 36:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 36:33"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: On the day of My cleansing you⁺ from all your⁺ iniquities, I will make you dwell in the cities, and the ruins will be rebuilt. <verse eid="EZK 36:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 36:34"/>And the land that was desolate will be tilled, instead of that it has been a desolation before the eyes of all passing by. <verse eid="EZK 36:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 36:35"/>And they will say, ‘This land that was desolate has become like the garden of Eden, and the ruined cities, desolate and overthrown, <char style="add">are</char> fortified <char style="add">and</char> they are inhabited.’ <verse eid="EZK 36:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 36:36"/>And the nations that remain all around you⁺ will know that I, YHWH, have rebuilt the ruins, <char style="add">and</char> I have replanted what was desolate. I, YHWH, have spoken, and I will do <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="EZK 36:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 36:37"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: Again <char style="add">in</char> this I will be sought out by the house of Israel, to do <char style="add">this</char> for them; I will increase them like a flock of people. <verse eid="EZK 36:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 36:38"/>Like a flock of consecration, like the flock at Jerusalem on its feast s, so the ruined cities will be filled with a flock of people. And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 36:38"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 36"/>

<chapter number="37" style="c" sid="EZK 37"/>

<para style="s">The Valley of Dry Bones</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 37:1"/>And the hand of YHWH came upon me, and He brought me out in the Spirit of YHWH, and He set me down in the midst of the valley; and it <char style="add">was</char> full of bones. <verse eid="EZK 37:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 37:2"/>And He caused me to pass among them all around, and behold, very many <char style="add">were</char> upon the face of the valley; and behold, <char style="add">they were</char> very dry. <verse eid="EZK 37:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 37:3"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, Can these bones live?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 37:3">And I said, “O Lord YHWH, You know.” <verse eid="EZK 37:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 37:4"/>And He said to me: “Prophesy to these bones and say to them, ‘O dry bones, hear the word of YHWH! <verse eid="EZK 37:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 37:5"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH to these bones: Behold, I am causing to enter into you⁺ breath,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">spirit</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 6, 9, and 10</char></note> and you⁺ will live. <verse eid="EZK 37:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 37:6"/>And I will put upon you⁺ sinews, and I will bring up flesh over you⁺, and I will cover over you⁺ with skin; and I will put within you⁺ breath, and you⁺ will live. And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 37:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 37:7"/>And I prophesied as I had been commanded. And there was a noise at my prophesying, and behold, a shaking, and the bones drew together, bone to bone. <verse eid="EZK 37:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 37:8"/>And I looked, and behold, upon them <char style="add">were</char> sinews, and flesh came up and skin covered over them above it, and <char style="add">there was</char> no breath in them. <verse eid="EZK 37:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 37:9"/>And He said to me, “Prophesy to the breath; prophesy, son of man, and say to the breath, thus says the Lord YHWH: From the four winds come, O breath, and breathe on these slain, that they may live.” <verse eid="EZK 37:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 37:10"/>And I prophesied as He had commanded me. And the breath came into them, and they lived; and they stood on their feet—an exceedingly greatly great army. <verse eid="EZK 37:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 37:11"/>And He said to me, “Son of man, these bones, they <char style="add">are</char> the whole the house of Israel. Behold, they are saying, ‘Our bones have dried up and our hope has perished; we have been cut off by ourselves.’ <verse eid="EZK 37:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 37:12"/>Therefore prophesy and say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I am opening your⁺ graves, and I will bring you⁺ up from your⁺ graves, O My people, and I will bring you⁺ into the land of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 37:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 37:13"/>And you⁺ will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, in My opening your⁺ graves, and in My bringing you⁺ up from your⁺ graves, O My people. <verse eid="EZK 37:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 37:14"/>And I will put My Spirit in you⁺, and you⁺ will live; and I will settle you⁺ in your⁺ own land. And you⁺ will know that I, YHWH, have spoken, and I have done <char style="add">it</char>, a declaration of YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 37:14"/></para>

<para style="s">One Nation with One King</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 37:15"/>And the word of YHWH came to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 37:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 37:16"/>“And you, son of man, take for yourself one stick,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">branch</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; three times in this verse; also in verses 17, 19, and 20</char></note> and write on it, ‘For Judah and for the sons of Israel, his companions.’ And take one stick and write on it, ‘For Joseph, the stick of Ephraim, and for all the house of Israel, his companions.’ <verse eid="EZK 37:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 37:17"/>And join them one to one for yourself into one stick, and they will become as one in your hand. <verse eid="EZK 37:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 37:18"/>And when the sons of your people speak to you, saying, ‘Will you not show to us what these <char style="add">are</char> to you??’ <verse eid="EZK 37:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 37:19"/>Say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I I am taking the stick of Joseph, which <char style="add">is</char> in the hand of Ephraim, and the tribes of Israel, his companions, and I will join them upon it with the stick of Judah, and I will make them one stick; and they will become one in My hand.’ <verse eid="EZK 37:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 37:20"/>And the sticks on which you write will be in your hand before their eyes. <verse eid="EZK 37:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 37:21"/>And you shall say to them, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Behold, I am taking the sons of Israel from the nations to which they have gone there, and I will gather them from all around, and I will bring them into their own land. <verse eid="EZK 37:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 37:22"/>And I will make them one nation in the land, on the mountains of Israel, and one king will be over them all as king; and will they be no longer as two nations, and they will not be divided anymore as two kingdoms again. <verse eid="EZK 37:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 37:23"/>And they will not defile themselves anymore with their idols, and with their abominations, and with all their transgressions; and I will save them from all their apostasies<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Many Hebrew manuscripts (see also LXX); most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their dwelling places</char></note> in which they have sinned, and I will cleanse them; and they will be unto Me as a people, and I will be unto them as God. <verse eid="EZK 37:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 37:24"/>And My servant David <char style="add">shall be</char> king over them, and there will be one shepherd over them all; and in My ordinances they will walk, and My statutes they will keep, and they will do them. <verse eid="EZK 37:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 37:25"/>And they will dwell in the land that I have given to My servant, to Jacob, where your⁺ fathers dwelt in it; and they will dwell upon it, they and their children, and the children of their children, even to forever; and David My servant <char style="add">shall be</char> the prince for them forever. <verse eid="EZK 37:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 37:26"/>And I will cut with them a covenant of peace; it will be covenant with them forever; and I will establish them, and I will multiply them, and I will set My sanctuary in their midst forever. <verse eid="EZK 37:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 37:27"/>And My dwelling place will be with them, and I will be unto them God, and they will be unto Me for a people.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My tabernacle</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 2 Corinthians 6:16</char></note><verse eid="EZK 37:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 37:28"/>And the nations will know that I, YHWH, am sanctifying Israel, when My sanctuary comes to be in their midst forever.’” <verse eid="EZK 37:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 37"/>

<chapter number="38" style="c" sid="EZK 38"/>

<para style="s">A Prophecy against Gog</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 38:1"/>And the word came of YHWH to me, saying: <verse eid="EZK 38:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 38:2"/>“Son of man, set your face against Gog, of the land of Magog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Magog, the prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal</char></note> and prophesy against him, <verse eid="EZK 38:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 38:3"/>and say, thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you, O Gog, chief prince of Meshech and Tubal!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Gog, the prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 38:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 38:4"/>And I will turn you around, and I will put hooks in your jaws, and I will bring you out and all your army—horses and horsemen, all clothed in perfection, a great company, <char style="add">with</char> bucklers and shields, all of them handling swords. <verse eid="EZK 38:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 38:5"/>Persia, Cush,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the upper Nile region</char></note> and Libya <char style="add">are</char> with them, all of them <char style="add">with</char> shield and helmet. <verse eid="EZK 38:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 38:6"/>Gomer and all her troops, the house of Togarmah from the extremities of the north, and all his troops—many peoples <char style="add">are</char> with you. <verse eid="EZK 38:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 38:7"/>Ready yourself, and be ready yourself—you and all your company gathered around you—and be unto them as a guard. <verse eid="EZK 38:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 38:8"/>After many days you will be mustered; in the latter years, you will come into a land having returned from the sword, having been gathered from many peoples, upon the mountains of Israel, which had been continually as a desolation. From the nations it has been brought out, and they will dwell in safety, all of them. <verse eid="EZK 38:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 38:9"/>And you will come up, like a storm you will come in, like a cloud to cover the land, you and all your troops, and many peoples with you. <verse eid="EZK 38:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 38:10"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: And it will come to pass on that day, <char style="add">that</char> will come up thoughts upon your heart, and you will devise an evil plan. <verse eid="EZK 38:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 38:11"/>And you will say, ‘I will go up against a land of unwalled villages, I will go in to those living quietly, dwelling in security—all of them dwelling with no walls, and bars and gates not unto them— <verse eid="EZK 38:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 38:12"/>to draw out the plunder and to prey <char style="add">on</char> the prey, to stretch out my hand against the desolate places now inhabited, and against a people gathered from the nations, having gained livestock and possessions, dwelling in the center of the land.’ <verse eid="EZK 38:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 38:13"/>Sheba, and Dedan, and the merchants of Tarshish, and all her villages,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">young lions</char></note> will say to you, ‘Have you come to draw out the plunder? Is it to prey on prey <char style="add">that</char> you have assembled your company—to carry <char style="add">off</char> silver and gold, to take away livestock and goods, to draw out great plunder?’ <verse eid="EZK 38:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 38:14"/>Therefore, prophesy, son of man, and say to Gog—thus says the Lord YHWH: On that day, with the dwelling of My people Israel in safety, will you not know <char style="add">it</char>?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">will you not rouse yourself?</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 38:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 38:15"/>And you will come from your place, from the extremities of the north, you and many peoples with you, riding on horses all of them, a great company, and a numerous army. <verse eid="EZK 38:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 38:16"/>And you will come up against My people Israel, like a cloud to cover the land. In the latter days it will come to pass that I will bring you against My land, so that the nations may know Me, in My showing <char style="add">My</char> holiness in you before their eyes, O Gog! <verse eid="EZK 38:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 38:17"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: Are you he of whom I have spoken in former days by My servants, the prophets of Israel, those having prophesied in those days, <char style="add">for</char> years, of My bringing you against them? <verse eid="EZK 38:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 38:18"/>And it will come to pass in that day <char style="add">that</char> in the day of the coming of Gog against the land of Israel, says the Lord YHWH, My fury of My nose will rise up. <verse eid="EZK 38:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 38:19"/>And in My zeal <char style="add">and</char> in the fire of My wrath, I have spoken: Surely in that day <char style="add">that</char> there will be a great shaking upon the land of Israel, <verse eid="EZK 38:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 38:20"/>and they will shake before My face—the fish of the sea, and the birds of the heavens, and the beasts of the field, and every creeping <char style="add">thing</char> that creeps upon the earth, and every man who <char style="add">is</char> on the face of the earth. And the mountains will be thrown down, and the steep places will fall, and every wall will fall to the ground. <verse eid="EZK 38:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 38:21"/>And I will call for a sword against him on all My mountains, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, <char style="add">and</char> the sword of each man will be against his brother. <verse eid="EZK 38:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 38:22"/>And I will bring judgment <char style="add">on</char> him with pestilence and with blood, and flooding rain and stones of hail. I will rain down fire and brimstone on him, and on his troops, and on the many peoples who <char style="add">are</char> with him. <verse eid="EZK 38:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 38:23"/>And I will magnify Myself, and will sanctify Myself, and I will make Myself known before the eyes of many nations, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 38:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 38"/>

<chapter number="39" style="c" sid="EZK 39"/>

<para style="s">The Slaughter of Gog’s Armies</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 39:1"/><char style="add">“</char> And you, son of man, prophesy against Gog, and say, thus says the Lord YHWH: Behold, I <char style="add">am</char> against you, O Gog, chief prince of Meshech and Tubal.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Gog, prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 39:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 39:2"/>And I will turn you around, and will lead you on, and I will bring you up from the extremities of the north, and I will bring you against the mountains of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 39:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 39:3"/>And I will strike the bow from your left hand, and the arrows from your right hand I will make fall. <verse eid="EZK 39:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 39:4"/>You will fall upon the mountains of Israel, you and all your troops and the nations who <char style="add">are</char> with you, to <char style="add">be</char> the prey of birds of every sort, and <char style="add">to</char> the beasts of the field I will give you as food. <verse eid="EZK 39:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 39:5"/>You will fall upon the face of the field, for I have spoken, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 39:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 39:6"/>And I will send fire on Magog, and on those dwelling in the islands in security, and they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 39:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 39:7"/>And My holy name I will make known in the midst of My people Israel, and I will not let the name of My holiness be profaned anymore; and the nations will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH, the Holy One in Israel. <verse eid="EZK 39:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 39:8"/>Behold, it is coming, and it will come to pass, a declaration of the Lord YHWH; it <char style="add">is</char> the day of which I have spoken! <verse eid="EZK 39:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 39:9"/>And those dwelling in the cities of Israel will go out, and they will set on fire and will burn the weapons—the shields and bucklers, the bows and arrows, and the javelins and spears—and they will burn them with fire seven years; <verse eid="EZK 39:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 39:10"/>and they will not carry wood from the field, and they will not cut down from the forests, because they will burn the weapons with fire. And they will plunder those who plundered them, and they will pillage those who pillaged them, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 39:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 39:11"/>And it will come to pass on that day, <char style="add">that</char> I will give for Gog a place there <char style="add">for</char> burial in Israel, the valley of those passing by east of the sea;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Dead Sea</char></note> and it will block those passing by, and for they will bury there Gog and all his multitude. And they will call <char style="add">it</char> the Valley of Hamon-gog.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hamon-gog</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">multitude of Gog</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 39:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 39:12"/>And the house of Israel will be burying them, in order to cleanse the land, seven months. <verse eid="EZK 39:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 39:13"/>All the people of the land will be burying, and they will be unto them for renown on the day of My being glorified,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and the day I display My glory will be a day of renown</char></note> a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 39:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 39:14"/>And they will set apart men to continually pass through the land, burying the passers-by remaining on the face of the ground, to cleanse it; at the end of seven months they will make a search. <verse eid="EZK 39:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 39:15"/>And those passing by will pass through the land, and having seen a bone of a man, he will construct beside it a sign, until those burying have buried it in the Valley of Hamon-gog. <verse eid="EZK 39:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 39:16"/>(Also the name of the city <char style="add">is</char> Hamonah.)<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hamonah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">multitude</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">horde</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> And they will cleanse the land. <verse eid="EZK 39:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 39:17"/>And you, son of man, thus says the Lord YHWH: Say to the bird of every wing, and to every beast of the field, ‘Gather yourselves, and come; gather together from all around to My sacrifice that I am sacrificing for you⁺, a great sacrifice on the mountains of Israel, that you⁺ may eat flesh and drink blood! <verse eid="EZK 39:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 39:18"/>The flesh of the mighty ones you⁺ will eat, and the blood of the princes of the earth you⁺ will drink—rams, lambs, and goats, and bulls, fatlings of Bashan—all of them! <verse eid="EZK 39:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 39:19"/>And you⁺ will eat fat to fullness, and you⁺ will drink blood to drunkenness, at My sacrifice that I am sacrificing for you⁺. <verse eid="EZK 39:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 39:20"/>And you⁺ will be filled at My table <char style="add">with</char> horses and riders, with mighty ones, and with all the men of war,’ a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 39:20"/></para>

<para style="s">Israel to Be Restored</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 39:21"/>And I will give forth My glory among the nations, and all the nations will see My judgment that I have made, and My hand that I have set upon them. <verse eid="EZK 39:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 39:22"/>And the house of Israel will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH their God, from that day and forward. <verse eid="EZK 39:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 39:23"/>And the nations will know that for their iniquity the house of Israel went into captivity, upon that they were unfaithful to Me; and I hid My face from them, and I gave them into the hand of their enemies, and they all fell by the sword. <verse eid="EZK 39:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 39:24"/>According to their uncleanness and according to their transgressions I have dealt with them, and I have hidden My face from them. <verse eid="EZK 39:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 39:25"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord YHWH: Now I will turn back the captivity of Jacob,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I will restore the fortunes of Jacob</char></note> and I will have compassion on all the house of Israel, and I will be jealous for My holy name. <verse eid="EZK 39:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 39:26"/>And they will forget<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">39.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> A few Hebrew manuscripts; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">They will bear</char></note> their shame, and all their unfaithfulness by which they were unfaithful with Me in their dwelling upon their own land in safety, and there will not be one to frighten them. <verse eid="EZK 39:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 39:27"/>In My returning them from the peoples, I have gathered them from the lands of their enemies, and I will show My holiness in them before the eyes of the many nations. <verse eid="EZK 39:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 39:28"/>And they will know that I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH their God, in My sending them into captivity among the nations. And I will gather them upon their land, and no longer will I leave them to remain there. <verse eid="EZK 39:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 39:29"/>And I will not hide My face anymore from them, when I pour out My Spirit on the house of Israel, a declaration of the Lord YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 39:29"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 39"/>

<chapter number="40" style="c" sid="EZK 40"/>

<para style="s">The Man with a Measuring Rod</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 40:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Zechariah 2:1–5</char></note>In the twenty-fifth year of our captivity, at the beginning of the year, on the tenth of the month, in the fourteenth year after that the city was captured, on this very day, the hand of YHWH was upon me, and He took me there. <verse eid="EZK 40:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 40:2"/>In visions of God, He brought me to the land of Israel, and made me rest on a very high mountain; and on it <char style="add">was</char> like the structure of a city on the south. <verse eid="EZK 40:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 40:3"/>And He brought me there, and behold, a man whose appearance <char style="add">was</char> like the appearance of bronze, and He had a cord of flax in his hand, and a rod for measuring, and he was standing in the gateway. <verse eid="EZK 40:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 40:4"/>And the man said to me: “Son of man, look with your eyes, and with your ears hear, and set your heart to all that I am going to show you; for that I might show <char style="add">it</char> to you, you were brought here. Declare all that you see to the house of Israel!” <verse eid="EZK 40:4"/></para>

<para style="s">The East Gate</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 40:5"/>And behold, a wall on the outside of the temple all around, and in the hand of the man <char style="add">was</char> a rod measuring six cubits,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">6 long cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, the length of the reed used for measuring, is approximately 10.5 feet or 3.2 meters; similarly in verses 6, 7, and 12. The long cubit of about 21 inches or 53.3 centimeters is the basic unit of length throughout Ezekiel 40 to 48.</char></note> by a cubit and a handbreadth. And he measured the width of the structure, one rod, and the height, one rod. <verse eid="EZK 40:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 40:6"/>And he went to the gateway of which its face <char style="add">was</char> toward the east, and he went up on its steps and measured the threshold of the gateway, one rod deep, even one threshold, one rod deep. <verse eid="EZK 40:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 40:7"/>And the gate chamber <char style="add">was</char> one rod long, and one rod wide; and between the gate chambers five cubits;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">5 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 8.75 feet or 2.7 meters; also in verses 30 and 48.</char></note> and the threshold of the gateway by the porch of the gate inside <char style="add">was</char> one rod. <verse eid="EZK 40:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 40:8"/>And He measured the porch of the gate inside, one rod. <verse eid="EZK 40:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 40:9"/>And he measured the porch of the gate, eight cubits;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">8 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 14 feet or 4.3 meters.</char></note> and the gateposts, two cubits;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">2 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 3.5 feet or 1.1 meters.</char></note> and the porch of the gateway <char style="add">was</char> on the inside. <verse eid="EZK 40:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 40:10"/>And the chambers of the gateway toward the east <char style="add">were</char> three on this side, and three on this side; a single measure unto the three, and a single measure <char style="add">was</char> unto the gateposts on this side and on this side. <verse eid="EZK 40:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 40:11"/>And He measured the width of the entrance of the gateway, ten cubits,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">10 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 17.5 feet or 5.3 meters.</char></note> <char style="add">and</char> the length of the gate, thirteen cubits.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">13 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 22.75 feet or 6.9 meters.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 40:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 40:12"/>And <char style="add">there was</char> a space before the face of the gate chambers, one cubit and one cubit on this side, and the chambers <char style="add">were</char> six cubits on this side, and six cubits on this side. <verse eid="EZK 40:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 40:13"/>And he measured the gateway from the roof of the one chamber to the roof of the, <char style="add">and</char> the width <char style="add">was</char> twenty-five cubits,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">25 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 43.75 feet or 13.3 meters; also in verses 21, 25, 29, 30, 33, and 36.</char></note> door over against door. <verse eid="EZK 40:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 40:14"/>And He measured the porticos,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">jambs</char></note> sixty cubits <char style="add">high</char>,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">60 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 105 feet or 32 meters.</char></note> and to the gatepost of the court <char style="add">was</char> the gateway all around. <verse eid="EZK 40:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 40:15"/>And <char style="add">from</char> the front of the gate at the entrance to the front of the porch of the inner gate <char style="add">was</char> fifty cubits.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">50 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 87.5 feet or 26.7 meters; also in verses 21, 25, 29, 33, and 36.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 40:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 40:16"/>And <char style="add">were</char> beveled windows in the gate chambers,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">gateposts</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">jambs</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">projecting walls</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; here and throughout Ezekiel 40 and 41.</char></note> and in their side pillars on the inside of the gateway all around, and likewise in the porticos; and <char style="add">were</char> windows all around on the inside, and on each side pillar <char style="add">were</char> palm trees. <verse eid="EZK 40:16"/></para>

<para style="s">The Outer Court</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 40:17"/>And he brought me into the outer court, and behold, chambers, and a pavement made for the court all around; thirty chambers <char style="add">were</char> toward the pavement. <verse eid="EZK 40:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 40:18"/>And the pavement <char style="add">was</char> by the side of the gateways corresponding to the length of the gateways; <char style="add">this was</char> the lower pavement. <verse eid="EZK 40:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 40:19"/>And he measured the width from the front of the lower gateway to the front of the inner court on the outside, a hundred cubits<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">100 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 175 feet or 53.3 meters; also in verses 23, 27, and 47.</char></note> <char style="add">toward</char> the east and the north. <verse eid="EZK 40:19"/></para>

<para style="s">The North Gate</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 40:20"/>And the gateway of the outer court that <char style="add">had</char> its face toward the north, he also measured its length and its width. <verse eid="EZK 40:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 40:21"/>And its chambers <char style="add">were</char> three on this side and three on this side; and <char style="add">for</char> its side pillars and its porticos it was according to the measure of the first gate—fifty cubits its length, and its width five and twenty by the cubit. <verse eid="EZK 40:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 40:22"/>And its windows, and its porticos, and its palm trees, <char style="add">were</char> according to the measure of the gateway that <char style="add">had</char> its face toward the east; and with seven steps they ascend on it, and its portico <char style="add">was</char> opposite them. <verse eid="EZK 40:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 40:23"/>And a gate <char style="add">was</char> for the inner court opposite the gateway to the north, like <char style="add">that</char> to the east; and he measured from gateway to gateway a hundred cubits. <verse eid="EZK 40:23"/></para>

<para style="s">The South Gate</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 40:24"/>And he brought me toward the south, and behold, a gateway toward the south, and he measured its side pillars and its porticos according to these measurements. <verse eid="EZK 40:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 40:25"/>And windows <char style="add">were</char> for it and for its porticos all around, like these windows—fifty cubits <char style="add">was</char> its length, and its width five and twenty cubits. <verse eid="EZK 40:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 40:26"/>And seven steps <char style="add">were</char> its ascent, and its portico <char style="add">was</char> in front of them; and palm trees <char style="add">were</char> unto it, one on this side, and one on this side, on its side pillars. <verse eid="EZK 40:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 40:27"/>And a gateway <char style="add">was</char> for the inner court toward the south, and he measured from gateway to gateway toward the south, a hundred cubits. <verse eid="EZK 40:27"/></para>

<para style="s">The Gates of the Inner Court</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 40:28"/>And he brought me to the inner court through the south gate, and he measured the south gate according to these measurements. <verse eid="EZK 40:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 40:29"/>And its gate chambers and its side pillars and its porticos <char style="add">were</char> also according to these measurements. Windows <char style="add">were</char> for it and for its porticos all around—fifty cubits long, and twenty-five cubits wide. <verse eid="EZK 40:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 40:30"/>And porticos <char style="add">were</char> all around, five and twenty cubits long, and five cubits wide.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The porticoes were approximately 43.75 feet long and 8.75 feet deep (13.3 meters long and 2.7 meters deep).</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 40:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 40:31"/>And its porticos <char style="add">were</char> toward the outer court; palm trees <char style="add">were</char> on its side pillars, and eight steps <char style="add">were</char> its ascent. <verse eid="EZK 40:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 40:32"/>And he brought me into the inner court toward the east, and he measured the gateway according to these measurements. <verse eid="EZK 40:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 40:33"/>And its gate chambers and its side pillars and its porticos <char style="add">were</char> also according to these measurements. And windows <char style="add">were</char> for it and for its porticos all around, fifty cubits long, and five and twenty cubits wide. <verse eid="EZK 40:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 40:34"/>And its porticos <char style="add">were</char> toward the outer court; palm trees <char style="add">were</char> on its side pillars on this side and on this side, and eight steps <char style="add">were</char> its ascent. <verse eid="EZK 40:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 40:35"/>And he brought me to the north gate, and he measured <char style="add">it</char> according to these measurements— <verse eid="EZK 40:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="EZK 40:36"/>its gate chambers its side pillars and its porticos. And windows <char style="add">were</char> for it all around; its length <char style="add">was</char> fifty cubits, and its width five and twenty cubits. <verse eid="EZK 40:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="EZK 40:37"/>And its porticos<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX and Vulgate (see also verses 26, 31, and 34); Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">jambs</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">dividing wall</char></note> <char style="add">were</char> toward the outer court; palm trees <char style="add">were</char> on its side pillars on this side and on this side, and eight steps <char style="add">were</char> its ascent. <verse eid="EZK 40:37"/></para>

<para style="s">Eight Tables for Sacrifices</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="EZK 40:38"/>And a chamber and its entrance <char style="add">were</char> by the porticos<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">by the jambs</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see verse 14</char></note> of the gateways, where they washed the burnt offering. <verse eid="EZK 40:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="EZK 40:39"/>And in the portico of the gateway <char style="add">were</char> two tables on this side and two tables on this side, to slaughter on them the burnt offering and the sin offering and the guilt offering. <verse eid="EZK 40:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="EZK 40:40"/>And at the shoulder on the outside, as one goes up to the entrance of the north gateway, <char style="add">were</char> two tables; and on the other side of the portico of the gateway <char style="add">were</char> two tables. <verse eid="EZK 40:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="EZK 40:41"/>Four tables <char style="add">were</char> on this side, and four tables on this side, by the side of the gateway—eight tables, <char style="add">and</char> on them they slaughtered. <verse eid="EZK 40:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="EZK 40:42"/>And four tables <char style="add">were</char> for the burnt offering, hewn stones one cubit and a half long, and one cubit and a half wide, and one cubit high;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The tables were approximately 2.6 feet in length and width, and 1.75 feet high (79.2 centimeters in length and width, and 53.3 centimeters high).</char></note> and on them they laid the instruments with which they slaughtered the burnt offering and the sacrifice. <verse eid="EZK 40:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="EZK 40:43"/>And hooks,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">shelves</char></note> one handbreadth,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A handbreadth</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 2.9 inches or 7.4 centimeters long.</char></note> were fastened on the inside all around; and on the tables <char style="add">was</char> the flesh of the sacrifices. <verse eid="EZK 40:43"/></para>

<para style="s">Chambers for Ministry</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="EZK 40:44"/>And on the outside of the inner gate <char style="add">were</char> two chambers in the inner court,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.44 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">within the inner court were chambers for the singers</char></note> at the side of the gateway to the north; and their faces <char style="add">were</char> toward the south, one at the side of the south<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.44 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the east</char></note> gate <char style="add">were</char> facing toward the north. <verse eid="EZK 40:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="EZK 40:45"/>And he said to me, “This chamber that faces toward the south <char style="add">is</char> for the priests keeping guard of the temple. <verse eid="EZK 40:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="EZK 40:46"/>And the chamber that faces toward the north <char style="add">is</char> for the priests keeping guard of the altar; they <char style="add">are</char> the sons of Zadok, those coming near from <char style="add">all</char> the sons of Levi, unto YHWH to minister to Him.” <verse eid="EZK 40:46"/></para>

<para style="s">The Inner Court</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="EZK 40:47"/>And he measured the court, a hundred cubits long, and a hundred cubits wide, being square; and the altar <char style="add">was</char> before the face of the temple. <verse eid="EZK 40:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="EZK 40:48"/>And he brought me to the portico of the temple, and he measured the doorposts of the portico, five cubits on this side, and five cubits on this side; and the width of the gateway was <char style="add">fourteen cubits and its sidewalls were</char> three cubits on this side, and three cubits on this side.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.48 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; the gateway was approximately 24.5 feet or 7.5 meters wide, with sidewalls approximately 5.25 feet or 1.6 meters wide on either side. Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and the width of the gateway was three cubits on either side.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 40:48"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="EZK 40:49"/>The length of the portico <char style="add">was</char> twenty cubits,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">20 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 35 feet or 10.7 meters.</char></note> and the width <char style="add">was</char> twelve cubits,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; </char><char style="fq" closed="false">12 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 21 feet or 6.4 meters; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">eleven cubits deep</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; that is, approximately 19.25 feet or 5.9 meters.</char></note> and by the <char style="add">ten</char> steps that they went up to it;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and by the steps that went up to it</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char></note> and pillars <char style="add">were</char> by the doorposts, one on this side, and one on this side. <verse eid="EZK 40:49"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 40"/>

<chapter number="41" style="c" sid="EZK 41"/>

<para style="s">inside the Temple</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 41:1"/>And he brought me into the sanctuary and measured the doorposts, six cubits wide<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">6 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 10.5 feet or 3.2 meters; also in verses 3, 5, and 8.</char></note> on each side.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> One Hebrew manuscript and LXX; most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on each side—the width of the tent</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 41:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 41:2"/>And the width of the entryway <char style="add">was</char> ten cubits;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">10 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 17.5 feet or 5.3 meters.</char></note> and the side walls of the entrance <char style="add">were</char> five cubits<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">5 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 8.75 feet or 2.7 meters; also in verses 9, 11, and 12.</char></note> on this side, and five cubits on this side. And he measured its length, forty cubits, and its width, twenty cubits.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The outer sanctuary was approximately 70 feet long and 35 feet wide (21.3 meters long and 10.7 meters wide).</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 41:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 41:3"/>And he went inside and measured the post for the door, two cubits;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">2 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 3.5 feet or 1.1 meters.</char></note> and the entrance, <char style="add">was</char> six cubits; and the width of the entrance <char style="add">was</char> seven cubits.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">7 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 12.25 feet or 3.7 meters.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 41:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 41:4"/>And he measured the length,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the length of the inner sanctuary</char></note> twenty cubits, and the width, twenty cubits,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The room was approximately 35 feet long and 35 feet wide (10.7 meters long and 10.7 meters wide).</char></note> to beyond the sanctuary. And he said to me: “This <char style="add">is</char> the Holy of Holies.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Most Holy Place</char></note>” <verse eid="EZK 41:4"/></para>

<para style="s">Outside the Temple</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 41:5"/>And he measured the wall of the temple, six cubits; and the width of each side chamber <char style="add">was</char> four cubits,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">4 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 7 feet or 2.1 meters.</char></note> all around the temple on every side. <verse eid="EZK 41:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 41:6"/>And the side chambers <char style="add">were</char> side chamber above side chamber <char style="add">in</char> three <char style="add">stories</char>, thirty per level; and they rested on the ledges that <char style="add">were</char> unto the house for the side chambers all around, to be supports; they were not fastened to the wall of the temple. <verse eid="EZK 41:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 41:7"/>And it became wider, and went around above <char style="add">and</char> above to the side chambers, because the turning round of the house <char style="add">went</char> above <char style="add">and</char> above round <char style="add">and</char> round the house; upon thus the width of the structure <char style="add">was</char> above, and the lowest went up to the highest through the middle. <verse eid="EZK 41:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 41:8"/>And I saw for the temple an elevation round <char style="add">and</char> round; the foundation of the side chambers <char style="add">was</char> a full rod, six great cubits. <verse eid="EZK 41:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 41:9"/>The thickness of the wall of the side chambers to the outside <char style="add">was</char> five cubits, and also the open area between the side rooms that <char style="add">were</char> of the house <verse eid="EZK 41:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 41:10"/>and between the chambers <char style="add">was</char> a width of twenty cubits all around the house, round <char style="add">and</char> round. <verse eid="EZK 41:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 41:11"/>And the doors of the side chambers <char style="add">were</char> toward the open area, one door toward the north, and one door toward the south; and the width of the space that <char style="add">was</char> open <char style="add">was</char> five cubits all around. <verse eid="EZK 41:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 41:12"/>And the building that <char style="add">was</char> toward the face of the separating courtyard <char style="add">at</char> the end toward the west <char style="add">was</char> seventy cubits wide;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">70 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 122.5 feet or 37.3 meters.</char></note> and the wall of the building <char style="add">was</char> five cubits thick all around, and its length <char style="add">was</char> ninety cubits.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">90 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 157.5 feet or 48 meters.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 41:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 41:13"/>And he measured the temple, a hundred cubits long;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">100 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 175 feet or 53.3 meters; similarly in verses 14 and 15.</char></note> and the separating courtyard, and the building, and its walls, a hundred cubits long. <verse eid="EZK 41:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 41:14"/>And the width of the face of the temple, and the separating courtyard to the east, <char style="add">was</char> a hundred cubits. <verse eid="EZK 41:14"/></para>

<para style="s">The Interior Structures</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 41:15"/>And he measured the length of the building to the face of the separating courtyard that <char style="add">was</char> at its back, with its galleries on this side and on this side, a hundred cubits; the outer sanctuary, the inner, and the porches of the court, <verse eid="EZK 41:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 41:16"/>their doorposts, and the beveled windows, and the galleries all around for the three of them, opposite the threshold, <char style="add">were</char> paneled with wood round about, <char style="add">from</char> the ground to the windows, and the windows were covered, <verse eid="EZK 41:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 41:17"/>from above the door, and to the inner room, and on the outside; and on every wall round about, on the inside and on the outside, <char style="add">were</char> measured patterns. <verse eid="EZK 41:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 41:18"/>And it was made <char style="add">with</char> cherubim and palm trees, a palm tree between a cherub and a cherub; and two faces <char style="add">were</char> unto each cherub: <verse eid="EZK 41:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 41:19"/>And the face of a man <char style="add">was</char> toward the palm tree on this side, and the face of a young lion toward the palm tree on this side; so <char style="add">it was</char> made throughout all the temple round <char style="add">and</char> round. <verse eid="EZK 41:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 41:20"/>From the floor to the space above the door, the cherubim and the palm trees <char style="add">were</char> made, and the wall of the sanctuary. <verse eid="EZK 41:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 41:21"/>The temple doorframe <char style="add">was</char> square, and <char style="add">at</char> the face of the sanctuary, the appearance <char style="add">was</char> as the appearance. <verse eid="EZK 41:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 41:22"/>An altar <char style="add">was</char> of wood, three cubits high, and its length <char style="add">was</char> two cubits;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The altar was approximately 5.25 feet high and 3.5 feet square (1.6 meters high and 1.1 meters square)</char></note> and its corners for it, and its length, and its sides <char style="add">were</char> of wood. And he said to me, “This <char style="add">is</char> the table that <char style="add">is</char> before the face of YHWH.” <verse eid="EZK 41:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 41:23"/>And two doors <char style="add">were</char> for the temple and for the sanctuary. <verse eid="EZK 41:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 41:24"/>And two door-panels <char style="add">were</char> for the doors, two turning door-panels—two for the one door, and two door-panels for the other. <verse eid="EZK 41:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 41:25"/>And <char style="add">were</char> made onto them, onto the doors of the temple, cherubim and palm trees, as they <char style="add">were</char> made on the walls; and a canopy of wood <char style="add">was</char> at the face of the portico on the outside. <verse eid="EZK 41:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 41:26"/>And beveled windows and palm trees <char style="add">were</char> on this side and on this side, on the sides of the portico, and <char style="add">on</char> the side chambers of the temple, and the canopies. <verse eid="EZK 41:26"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 41"/>

<chapter number="42" style="c" sid="EZK 42"/>

<para style="s">Chambers for the Priests</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 42:1"/>And he brought me out into the outer court, the way toward the north; and he brought me into the chamber that <char style="add">was</char> opposite the separating courtyard, and that opposite the building toward the north. <verse eid="EZK 42:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 42:2"/>Toward the face of <char style="add">its</char> length <char style="add">was</char> a hundred cubits, with the door <char style="add">to</char> the north, and the width <char style="add">was</char> fifty cubits.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The building was approximately 175 feet long and 87.5 feet wide (53.3 meters long and 26.7 meters wide).</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 42:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 42:3"/>Opposite the twenty <char style="add">cubits</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">20 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 35 feet or 10.7 meters.</char></note> that <char style="add">were</char> for the inner court, and opposite the pavement for the outer court, <char style="add">was</char> a gallery to the face of a gallery in three parts. <verse eid="EZK 42:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 42:4"/>And before the face of the chambers <char style="add">was</char> a walkway, ten cubits wide and a <char style="add">hundred</char> cubits long;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX. The walkway was approximately 17.5 feet wide and 175 feet long (5.3 meters wide and 53.3 meters long). Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">ten cubits wide and a way of one cubit.</char></note> and their doors <char style="add">were</char> to the north. <verse eid="EZK 42:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 42:5"/>And the upper chambers <char style="add">were</char> shorter, for the galleries took away from them, on the lower and middle of the building. <verse eid="EZK 42:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 42:6"/>For they <char style="add">were</char> in three parts, and there was not unto them pillars like the pillars of the courts; upon thus it was shortened from the ground more than the lower and middle. <verse eid="EZK 42:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 42:7"/>And a wall that <char style="add">was</char> on the outside <char style="add">was</char> over against the chambers, toward the outer court, toward the face of the chambers; its length <char style="add">was</char> fifty cubits. <verse eid="EZK 42:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 42:8"/>For the length of the chambers that <char style="add">were</char> toward the outer court <char style="add">was</char> fifty cubits, and, behold, upon those facing the temple <char style="add">was</char> a hundred cubits. <verse eid="EZK 42:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 42:9"/>And below these chambers <char style="add">was</char> the entry on the east, as one enters them from the outer court. <verse eid="EZK 42:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 42:10"/>Along the length of the wall of the court toward the south,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">east</char></note> toward the face of the separating courtyard, and toward the face of the building, <char style="add">were</char> chambers <verse eid="EZK 42:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 42:11"/>and a pathway before them, the appearance of the chambers that <char style="add">were</char> toward the north, like their length so their width, and all their exits and according to their doors and according to their fashions, <verse eid="EZK 42:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 42:12"/>and according to their doors of the chambers that <char style="add">were</char> toward the south. A door <char style="add">was</char> at the head of the walkway, directly at the face of the wall toward the east in entering them. <verse eid="EZK 42:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 42:13"/>And he said to me: “The chambers to the north <char style="add">and</char> the chambers to the south, which <char style="add">are</char> toward the face of the separating courtyard, they <char style="add">are</char> the holy chambers <char style="add">in</char> which the priests, those who nearest to YHWH, will eat there the holy of holies;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the most holy</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; twice in this verse </char></note> they will lay the holy of holies there—the grain offering, and the sin offering, and the guilt offering—for the place <char style="add">is</char> holy. <verse eid="EZK 42:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 42:14"/>With the entering of the priests, they will not go out the holy <char style="add">area</char> into the outer court, and there they will leave their garments in which they minister—for they <char style="add">are</char> holy—and they will put on other garments, they may come near to <char style="add">that</char> which <char style="add">is</char> for the people.” <verse eid="EZK 42:14"/></para>

<para style="s">The Outer Measurements</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 42:15"/>And he had completed the measurements of the inner temple, and he brought me out through the gateway that <char style="add">has</char> its face toward the east, and he measured it round about. <verse eid="EZK 42:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 42:16"/>He measured the side to the east with a measuring rod, five hundred <char style="add">cubits</char>,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See LXX; </char><char style="fq" closed="false">five hundred cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> from verse 17 LXX and implied in verses 16, 18, 19, and 20 is approximately 875 feet or 266.7 meters in length. Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">five hundred rods</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, that is approximately 5,250 feet or 1,600 meters; similarly in verses 17, 18, 19, and 20.</char></note> by the measuring rod, all around. <verse eid="EZK 42:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 42:17"/>He measured the side to the north, five hundred <char style="add">cubits</char>, by the measuring rod, all around. <verse eid="EZK 42:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 42:18"/>The side to the south he measured, five hundred <char style="add">cubits</char>, by the measuring rod. <verse eid="EZK 42:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 42:19"/>He came around to the side to the west; he measured five hundred <char style="add">cubits</char>, by the measuring rod. <verse eid="EZK 42:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 42:20"/>At the four sides he measured it. A wall <char style="add">was</char> unto it round about, a length of five hundred <char style="add">cubits</char>, and a width of five hundred, to separate between the holy <char style="add">and</char> the common. <verse eid="EZK 42:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 42"/>

<chapter number="43" style="c" sid="EZK 43"/>

<para style="s">The Glory of Yahweh Returns to the Temple</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 43:1"/>And he brought me to the gate—the gate that is facing toward the east. <verse eid="EZK 43:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 43:2"/>And behold, the glory of the God of Israel came from the way of the east, and His voice <char style="add">was</char> like the voice of many waters, and the earth shone with His glory. <verse eid="EZK 43:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 43:3"/>And <char style="add">it was</char> according to the appearance of the vision that I had seen, like the vision that I had seen when He came<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some Hebrew manuscripts and Vulgate; most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">when I came</char></note> to destroy the city; and the visions <char style="add">were</char> like the vision that I saw at the River Kebar. And I fell on my face. <verse eid="EZK 43:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 43:4"/>And the glory of YHWH came into the temple <char style="add">by</char> the way of the gate that <char style="add">has</char> its face toward the east. <verse eid="EZK 43:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 43:5"/>And the Spirit lifted me up and brought me into the inner court, and behold, the glory of YHWH filled the temple. <verse eid="EZK 43:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 43:6"/>And I heard one speaking to me from the temple, and the man was standing beside me. <verse eid="EZK 43:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 43:7"/>And He said to me: “Son of man, the place of My throne, and the place for the soles of My feet, <char style="add">in</char> which I will dwell there in the midst of the sons of Israel forever; and the house of Israel will defile no more My holy name, they and their kings with their prostitution, and the corpses<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the monuments</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 9 </char></note> of their kings at their deaths,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">or their kings on their high places</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 43:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 43:8"/>by their giving their threshold next to My threshold, and their doorpost beside My doorpost, and the wall between Me and between them. And they have defiled My holy name by the abominations that they did, and I finished them off in My anger. <verse eid="EZK 43:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 43:9"/>Now let them remove their prostitution, and the corpses of their kings, away from Me, and I will dwell in their midst forever. <verse eid="EZK 43:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 43:10"/>You, son of man, describe to the house of Israel the temple, so that they may be ashamed of their iniquities; and let them measure the pattern. <verse eid="EZK 43:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 43:11"/>And if they are ashamed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And they will be ashamed</char></note> of all that they have done, the design of the temple, and its arrangement, and its exits, and its entrances, and all its design, and all its statutes, and all its forms, and all its laws, make known to them. And write <char style="add">it</char> before their eyes, so that they may keep all its design and all its ordinances, and do them. <verse eid="EZK 43:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 43:12"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the law of the temple: On the top of the mountain, all its border round about, <char style="add">is</char> the holy of holies.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the most holy</char></note> Behold, this <char style="add">is</char> the law of the temple. <verse eid="EZK 43:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Altar of Sacrifice</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 43:13"/>And these <char style="add">are</char> the measurements of the altar in cubits<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The </char><char style="fq" closed="false">long cubit</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, about 21 inches or 53.3 centimeters, is the basic unit for linear measurement throughout Ezekiel 40–48. </char></note> (a cubit <char style="add">is</char> a cubit and a handbreadth): The base <char style="add">shall be</char> one cubit <char style="add">high</char> and one cubit wide, and its rim to its edge all around a span of one;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">One span</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 9 inches or 22.9 centimeters.</char></note> and this <char style="add">is</char> the height of the altar. <verse eid="EZK 43:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 43:14"/>And from the base on the ground up to the lower ledge <char style="add">shall be</char> two cubits, and the width one cubit;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The space was to be approximately 3.5 feet (1.1 meters), and the ledge was to be approximately 1.75 feet wide (53.3 centimeters wide).</char></note> and from the smaller ledge to the larger ledge, four cubits, and the width a cubit.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The space was to be approximately 7 feet (2.1 meters), and the ledge was to be approximately 1.75 feet wide (53.3 centimeters wide).</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 43:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 43:15"/>And the altar hearth <char style="add">shall be</char> four cubits <char style="add">high</char>, and from the hearth and upward <char style="add">are</char> four horns. <verse eid="EZK 43:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 43:16"/>And the altar hearth <char style="add">shall be</char> twelve long by twelve wide,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">12 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 21 feet or 6.4 meters.</char></note> being square at the four of its corners. <verse eid="EZK 43:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 43:17"/>And the ledge <char style="add">shall be</char> fourteen long,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">14 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 24.5 feet or 7.5 meters.</char></note> and fourteen wide, on the four of its sides, with a rim around it half a cubit,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">43.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A half cubit</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 10.5 inches or 26.7 centimeters.</char></note> and the base for it a cubit all around; and its steps shall face toward the east.” <verse eid="EZK 43:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 43:18"/>And he said to me: “Son of man, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘These <char style="add">are</char> the ordinances for the altar on the day of its being made to sacrifice burnt offerings on it, and to sprinkle blood on it. <verse eid="EZK 43:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 43:19"/>And you shall give to the priests, the Levites, those who <char style="add">are</char> of the seed of Zadok, who are near to Me, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, to minister to Me, a bull, a son of the herd, as a sin offering. <verse eid="EZK 43:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 43:20"/>And you shall take from its blood and put <char style="add">it</char> upon the four horns of it, and on the four corners of the ledge, and on the rim around it; and you will cleanse it from sin and make atonement for it. <verse eid="EZK 43:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 43:21"/>And you shall take the bull of the sin offering and burn it in the appointed place of the temple, outside of the sanctuary. <verse eid="EZK 43:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 43:22"/>And on the second day, you shall offer a kid of the goats, unblemished, for a sin offering; and they shall cleanse from sin the altar, as they cleansed <char style="add">it</char> from sin with the bull. <verse eid="EZK 43:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 43:23"/>When you have finished cleansing from sin, you shall bring near a bull, a son of the herd, unblemished, and a ram from the flock, unblemished. <verse eid="EZK 43:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 43:24"/>And you shall present them before YHWH, and the priests shall throw on them salt, and they shall offer them up <char style="add">as</char> a burnt offering to YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 43:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 43:25"/>Seven days you shall prepare a goat <char style="add">for</char> a sin offering, day by day, and a bull, a son of the herd and a ram from the flock, unblemished, they shall prepare. <verse eid="EZK 43:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 43:26"/>Seven days they shall make atonement for the altar and purify it, and they shall fill its hands. <verse eid="EZK 43:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 43:27"/>And are completed these days, and it shall come to pass on the eighth day and thereafter, <char style="add">that</char> the priests shall make upon the altar your⁺ burnt offerings and your⁺ peace offerings, and will I accept you⁺, a declaration of the Lord YHWH.’” <verse eid="EZK 43:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 43"/>

<chapter number="44" style="c" sid="EZK 44"/>

<para style="s">The East Gate Assigned to the Prince</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 44:1"/>And He brought me back the way of the gate of the outer sanctuary that faced east, and it <char style="add">was</char> shut. <verse eid="EZK 44:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 44:2"/>And YHWH said to me: “This gate will be kept shut; it shall not be opened, and no man will enter by it, because YHWH, God of Israel has entered by it; and it will be kept shut. <verse eid="EZK 44:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 44:3"/>The prince—the prince himself—he may sit in it to eat bread before YHWH; by way of the portico of the gateway he will enter, and by its way he will go out.” <verse eid="EZK 44:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 44:4"/>And He brought me by way of the north gate toward the face of the temple. And I looked, and behold, the glory of YHWH filled the house of YHWH, and I fell on my face. <verse eid="EZK 44:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 44:5"/>And YHWH said to me: “Son of man, set your heart, and see with your eyes, and hear with your ears all that I am saying to you concerning all the statutes of the house of YHWH, and concerning all its laws; and set your heart concerning those entering the house and all those going out of the sanctuary. <verse eid="EZK 44:5"/></para>

<para style="s">Reproof of the Levites</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 44:6"/>And say to the rebellious one, to the house of Israel, thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Enough for you⁺ from all your⁺ abominations, O house of Israel— <verse eid="EZK 44:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 44:7"/>your⁺ bringing in the sons of a foreigner, uncircumcised in heart and uncircumcised in flesh, to be in My sanctuary, to defile My house in your⁺ offering My food, the fat and the blood. And they have broken My covenant because of all your⁺ abominations. <verse eid="EZK 44:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 44:8"/>And you⁺ have not kept guard over My holy things, and you⁺ set <char style="add">them</char> to keep guard over My sanctuary for you⁺!’ <verse eid="EZK 44:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 44:9"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: Any son of a foreigner, uncircumcised in heart and uncircumcised in flesh, will not come into My sanctuary—any son of a foreigner who <char style="add">is</char> in the midst of the sons of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 44:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 44:10"/>Oh how the Levites who went far from Me in the straying of Israel, who went astray from Me after their idols, will indeed bear their iniquity! <verse eid="EZK 44:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 44:11"/>And they shall be in My sanctuary, ministering <char style="add">as</char> attendants at the gates of the house, and ministering in the house; they shall slaughter the burnt offering and the sacrifice for the people, and they shall stand before them to minister to them. <verse eid="EZK 44:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 44:12"/>Because that they ministered to them before their idols, and they became for the house of Israel a stumbling block of iniquity, upon thus I have lifted My hand concerning them, a declaration of the Lord YHWH, that they shall bear their iniquity. <verse eid="EZK 44:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 44:13"/>And they will not come near to Me to minister as priest to Me, or come near to any of My holy things, to the holies of the holies, and they shall bear their shame and their abominations which they have done. <verse eid="EZK 44:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 44:14"/>And I will give them to keep charge of the temple, for all its service and for all that is done in it. <verse eid="EZK 44:14"/></para>

<para style="s">The Duties of the Priests</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 44:15"/>And the Levite priests, the sons of Zadok, who kept guard over My sanctuary in the wandering away of the sons of Israel from Me, they will come near to Me to minister to Me, and they will stand before Me to offer to Me the fat and the blood, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 44:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 44:16"/>They shall enter into my sanctuary, and they shall come near to My table to minister to Me, and they shall keep My charge. <verse eid="EZK 44:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 44:17"/>And it will come to pass, in their going into the gates of the inner court, <char style="add">that</char> they will put on garments of linen and no wool will come up upon them in their ministering within the gates of the inner court, and within it. <verse eid="EZK 44:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 44:18"/>Turbans of linen will be on their heads, and undergarments of linen will be on their bodies; they will not gird themselves with sweat. <verse eid="EZK 44:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 44:19"/>And in their going out to the outer court, to the outer court unto the people, they shall take off their garments which they have ministered in them, and they shall leave them in the holy chambers, and they shall put on other garments, so that they do not sanctify the people with their garments. <verse eid="EZK 44:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 44:20"/>And their head, they shall not shave <char style="add">it</char>; their hair they shall not grow long; they must carefully trim their heads. <verse eid="EZK 44:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 44:21"/>And no priest shall drink any wine in their coming into the inner court. <verse eid="EZK 44:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 44:22"/>And a widow or a divorced woman they shall not take to themselves as wife, but only virgins from the seed of the house of Israel, or the widow who is a widow of a priest, they may take. <verse eid="EZK 44:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 44:23"/>And they will teach My people between the holy <char style="add">and</char> the common, and between the unclean <char style="add">and</char> the clean they shall make them know. <verse eid="EZK 44:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 44:24"/>And in a dispute they will stand in judgment; according to My ordinances they shall judge it, and My laws and My statutes in all My appointed feasts they shall keep, and My Sabbaths they shall sanctify. <verse eid="EZK 44:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 44:25"/>And unto a dead person they shall not come to defile themselves, but only for a father or for a mother, for a son or for a daughter, or for a brother or for a sister who has not been unto a man, may they defile themselves. <verse eid="EZK 44:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 44:26"/>And after he is cleansed, they shall count for him seven days. <verse eid="EZK 44:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 44:27"/>And on the day of his coming into the sanctuary, into the inner court, to minister in the sanctuary, he must offer his sin offering, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 44:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 44:28"/>And it shall be unto them for an inheritance: I am their inheritance. You⁺ shall give to them no possession in Israel; I am their possession. <verse eid="EZK 44:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 44:29"/>The grain offering, and the sin offering, and the guilt offering they shall eat, and every devoted thing in Israel shall be unto them. <verse eid="EZK 44:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 44:30"/>And the first of all the firstfruits of all things, and every contribution of all things from all your⁺ contributions, it will be for the priests. And the first of your⁺ dough you⁺ shall give to the priest, to cause to rest a blessing on your house. <verse eid="EZK 44:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 44:31"/>Every carcass and torn thing from the bird or from the beast, the priests shall not eat. </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 44:31"> Or <char style="add">the most holy</char><verse eid="EZK 44:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 44"/>

<chapter number="45" style="c" sid="EZK 45"/>

<para style="s">Consecration of the Land</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 45:1"/><char style="add">“</char> And in your⁺ allotting the land as an inheritance, you⁺ shall set apart a contribution to YHWH, a holy <char style="add">portion</char> of the land; its length <char style="add">shall be</char> five and twenty thousand, and the width twenty thousand.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; the holy portion was to be approximately 8.3 miles long and 6.6 miles wide (13.3 kilometers long and 10.7 kilometers wide). Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">25,000 cubits long and 10,000 wide</char><char style="ft" closed="false">. See also verses 3 and 5 and Ezekiel 48:9.</char></note> It <char style="add">is</char> holy in all its borders all around. <verse eid="EZK 45:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 45:2"/>There shall be from this for the sanctuary five hundred by five hundred,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">500 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 875 feet or 266.7 meters.</char></note> a square plot, around, <char style="add">with</char> fifty cubits<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">50 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 87.5 feet or 26.7 meters.</char></note> open space for it all around. <verse eid="EZK 45:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 45:3"/>And from this measure, you shall measure a length of five and twenty thousand, and a width of ten thousand;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The portion was to be approximately 8.3 miles long and 3.3 miles wide (13.3 kilometers long and 5.3 kilometers wide); similarly in verse 5.</char></note> and in it will be the sanctuary, the Holy of Holies.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Most Holy Place</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 45:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 45:4"/>It <char style="add">is</char> a holy <char style="add">portion</char> of the land; it is for the priests ministering in the sanctuary, who draw near to minister to YHWH; and it shall be unto them a place for houses and a holy place for the sanctuary. <verse eid="EZK 45:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 45:5"/>And five and twenty thousand long, and ten thousand wide, shall be unto the Levites ministering in the temple, as a possession for them, twenty towns in which to live.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their possession, twenty chambers</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 45:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 45:6"/>And as the possession of the city you⁺ shall give five thousand wide, <char style="add">with</char> a length of five and twenty thousand,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The property of the city was to be approximately 1.7 miles wide and 8.3 miles long (2.7 kilometers wide and 13.3 kilometers long).</char></note> adjacent to the portion of the holy <char style="add">portion</char>; it shall be unto all of the house of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 45:6"/></para>

<para style="s">The Prince’s Portion</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 45:7"/>And for the prince, on this side and on this side of the portion of the holy <char style="add">area</char>, and of the possession of the city, toward the faces of the portion of the holy <char style="add">area</char>, and toward the faces of the property of the city, from the west side westward, from the east side eastward; and the length <char style="add">is</char> parallel to one of the portions, from the west border to the east border <verse eid="EZK 45:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 45:8"/>of the land. It will be unto him as a possession in Israel. And My princes will not oppress My people anymore, and the land they will give to the house of Israel according to their tribes. <verse eid="EZK 45:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 45:9"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘Enough to you⁺, O princes of Israel, turn aside violence and destruction and do justice and righteousness. Stop your⁺ evictions upon My people, a declaration of the Lord YHWH.’ <verse eid="EZK 45:9"/></para>

<para style="s">Honest ScalesDeuteronomy 25:13–16</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 45:10"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Proverbs 11:1–3</char></note>Righteous scales and a righteous ephah<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">An ephah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is a dry measure of approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters.</char></note> and a righteous bath<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A bath</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> was a liquid measure of approximately 5.8 gallons or 22 liters.</char></note> shall be unto you⁺. <verse eid="EZK 45:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 45:11"/>The ephah and the bath shall be of one measure, the bath to bear a tenth of a homer, and the ephah a tenth of a homer. Their measure will be according to the homer.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A homer</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> was a dry measure of approximately 6.24 bushels or 220 liters; also in verses 13 and 14.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 45:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 45:12"/>And the shekel <char style="add">shall be</char> twenty gerahs;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">20 gerahs</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is equivalent to one shekel (approximately 0.4 ounces or 11.4 grams).</char></note> twenty shekels, five and twenty shekels, ten and five shekels,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, 60 shekels total; elsewhere, the common mina was 50 shekels. Sixty shekels weighed approximately 1.5 pounds or 683.8 grams.</char></note> will be unto you⁺ the mina. <verse eid="EZK 45:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Offerings and Feasts</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 45:13"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the contribution that you⁺ shall lift up: A sixth of an ephah from a homer of wheat, and a sixth of an ephah from a homer of barley.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, a sixtieth of the harvest of wheat and of barley; </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a sixth of an ephah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> was approximately 3.3 dry quarts or 3.7 liters.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 45:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 45:14"/>And the ordinance for the oil, the bath of oil, <char style="add">is</char> a tenth of a bath from each kor<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, one percent of one’s oil; </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a tenth of a bath</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> was approximately 2.3 quarts or 2.2 liters.</char></note> (a homer <char style="add">is</char> ten baths, for ten baths <char style="add">are</char> a homer); <verse eid="EZK 45:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 45:15"/>and <char style="add">will be</char> one lamb from the flock, from two hundred, from the watering places of Israel, for each grain offering, and burnt offering, and peace offering, to make atonement upon them, a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 45:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 45:16"/>All the people of the land shall be toward this contribution for the prince in Israel. <verse eid="EZK 45:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 45:17"/>And concerning the prince, it shall be the burnt offerings and the grain offering and the drink offering, at the feasts and the New Moons and the Sabbaths and at all the appointed feasts of the house of Israel; he shall prepare the sin offering,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">purification offering</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 19, 22, 23, and 25</char></note> and the grain offering, and the burnt offering, and the peace offerings, to make atonement for the house of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 45:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 45:18"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘In the first <char style="add">month</char>, on the first of the month, you shall take a bull, a son of the herd, unblemished, and you shall cleanse from sin the sanctuary. <verse eid="EZK 45:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 45:19"/>And the priest shall take from the blood of the sin offering, and put <char style="add">it</char> onto the doorposts of the temple, and onto the four corners of the ledge of the altar, and onto the doorposts of the gate of the inner court. <verse eid="EZK 45:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 45:20"/>And so you shall do on the seventh of the month, for each man who errs<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">sins unintentionally</char></note> and is ignorant, and you⁺ will make atonement for the temple. <verse eid="EZK 45:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 45:21"/>In the first <char style="add">month</char>, on the fourteenth day of the month, will be for you⁺ the Passover, a feast of seven days; unleavened <char style="add">bread</char> shall be eaten. <verse eid="EZK 45:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 45:22"/>And the prince shall prepare on that day, for himself and for all the people of the land, a bull as a sin offering. <verse eid="EZK 45:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 45:23"/>And on the seven days of the feast he shall prepare a burnt offering to YHWH, seven bulls and seven rams unblemished day by day—seven days—and a sin offering, a kid of the goats, day by day. <verse eid="EZK 45:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 45:24"/>And a grain offering of one ephah for each bull, and one ephah for each ram he shall prepare, and a hin of oil for each ephah.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A hin of oil for each ephah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 0.97 gallons or 3.67 liters of oil for each ephah of grain</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 45:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 45:25"/>In the seventh <char style="add">month</char>, on the fifteenth day of the month, during the feast,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Feast of Tabernacles</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Feast of Shelters</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> and originally called </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Feast of Ingathering</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (see Exodus 23:16 and Exodus 34:22).</char></note> he shall do like these seven days, for the sin offering, for the burnt offering, and the grain offering, and the oil.’ <verse eid="EZK 45:25"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 45"/>

<chapter number="46" style="c" sid="EZK 46"/>

<para style="s">The Prince’s Offerings</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 46:1"/><char style="add">“</char> Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘The gateway of the inner court facing the east shall be shut <char style="add">for</char> the six days of work; and on the day of the Sabbath it shall be opened, and on the day of the New Moon it shall be opened. <verse eid="EZK 46:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 46:2"/>And the prince shall enter by way of the portico of the gateway from the outside, and stand by the doorpost of the gate; and the priests shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, and he shall worship at the threshold of the gate and go out, and the gate shall not be shut until the evening. <verse eid="EZK 46:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 46:3"/>And the people of the land will bow down at the entrance to that gateway, on the Sabbaths and the New Moons, before YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 46:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 46:4"/>And the burnt offering that the prince shall offer to YHWH on the day of the Sabbath <char style="add">is</char> six lambs unblemished, and a ram unblemished. <verse eid="EZK 46:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 46:5"/>And the grain offering <char style="add">is</char> an ephah<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">An ephah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters (probably about 38.3 pounds or 17.4 kilograms of grain); also in verses 7 and 11.</char></note> for a ram, and for the lambs the grain offering <char style="add">is</char> a gift of his hand, and a hin of oil for the ephah. <verse eid="EZK 46:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 46:6"/>And on the day of the New Moon <char style="add">it is</char> a bull, a son of the herd, unblemished, and six lambs and a ram—they shall be unblemished. <verse eid="EZK 46:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 46:7"/>And an ephah for a bull, and an ephah for a ram, he shall prepare <char style="add">as</char> a grain offering, and for the lambs as that his hand can take, and a hin of oil to an ephah. <verse eid="EZK 46:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 46:8"/>And in the coming in of the prince, he shall come <char style="add">in</char> by way of the portico of the gateway, and the same way he shall go out. <verse eid="EZK 46:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 46:9"/>And in the coming in of the people of the land before YHWH at the appointed feasts, the one coming in by way of the north gate to worship will go out by way of the south gate, and the one coming in by way of the south gate will go out by way of the north gate; he will not return by way of the gate by that he entered, but he will go out straight ahead of him. <verse eid="EZK 46:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 46:10"/>And the prince will be in their midst; at their coming in, he will go in, and at their going out, he will go out. <verse eid="EZK 46:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 46:11"/>And at the festivals, and the appointed feasts the grain offering will be an ephah for a bull, and an ephah for a ram, and for the lambs a gift of his hand, and a hin of oil to an ephah. <verse eid="EZK 46:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 46:12"/>When the prince makes a freewill offering—a burnt offering or peace offerings—a freewill offering to YHWH, then shall be opened for him the gate facing the east, and he shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings as he did on the day of the Sabbath; and he will go out, and the gate will be shut after his going out. <verse eid="EZK 46:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 46:13"/>And a lamb, a son of a year, unblemished, you shall make <char style="add">as</char> a burnt offering day by day to YHWH; morning by morning you shall make it. <verse eid="EZK 46:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 46:14"/>And a grain offering you shall prepare with it, morning by morning, a sixth of an ephah,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A sixth of an ephah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 3.3 dry quarts or 3.7 liters (probably about 4.2 pounds or 1.9 kilograms of flour).</char></note> and a third of a hin of oil<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a third of a hin of olive oil</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; that is, approximately 1.3 quarts or 1.2 liters</char></note> to moisten the fine flour, <char style="add">as</char> a grain offering to YHWH. <char style="add">This is</char> a statute forever, in perpetuity. <verse eid="EZK 46:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 46:15"/>They shall prepare the lamb, and the grain offering, and the oil, morning by morning, <char style="add">as</char> a continual burnt offering.’ <verse eid="EZK 46:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 46:16"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: ‘If the prince gives a gift to man of his sons <char style="add">as</char> his inheritance, it shall belong to his sons; it <char style="add">is</char> their possession by inheritance. <verse eid="EZK 46:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 46:17"/>And if he gives a gift from his inheritance to one of his servants, it will be unto him until the year of liberty; then it will return to the prince; surely <char style="add">it is</char> his inheritance <char style="add">for</char> his sons; unto them it shall be. <verse eid="EZK 46:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 46:18"/>And the prince shall not take from inheritance of the people by evicting them from their property; from his own property he shall provide an inheritance for his sons, so that My people will not be scattered, a man from his property.’” <verse eid="EZK 46:18"/></para>

<para style="s">The Courts for Boiling and Baking</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 46:19"/>And he brought me through the entrance that <char style="add">was</char> at the side of the gate, into the chambers of holiness for the priests, facing toward the north; and behold, there <char style="add">was</char> a place at the extremities of the west. <verse eid="EZK 46:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 46:20"/>And he said to me: “This <char style="add">is</char> the place where the priests shall boil there the guilt offering and the sin offering, and where they shall bake the grain offering, so as not to bring <char style="add">them</char> out into the outer court to sanctify the people.” <verse eid="EZK 46:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 46:21"/>And he brought me out into the outer court, and he caused me to pass by the four corners of the court; and behold, a court in each corner of the court, a court in the corner of the court. <verse eid="EZK 46:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 46:22"/>In the four corners of the court <char style="add">were</char> courts enclosed, forty long and thirty wide,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The enclosed courts were approximately 70 feet long and 52.5 feet wide (21.3 meters long and 16 meters wide).</char></note> a single measure for their four corners. <verse eid="EZK 46:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 46:23"/>And a row <char style="add">was</char> all around in them, all around the four of them, and cooking hearths were made under the rows all around. <verse eid="EZK 46:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 46:24"/>And he said to me, “These <char style="add">are</char> the kitchens of those boiling, where the ministers of the temple will boil there the sacrifices of the people.” <verse eid="EZK 46:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 46"/>

<chapter number="47" style="c" sid="EZK 47"/>

<para style="s">Waters from under the Temple</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 47:1"/>And he brought me back to the door of the temple, and behold, waters were flowing from under the threshold of the temple toward the east (for the face of the temple <char style="add">is</char> eastward), and the waters were flowing from under the side of the temple <char style="add">on</char> the right, at the south of the altar. <verse eid="EZK 47:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 47:2"/>And he brought me out by way of the north gate, and he led me around the way on the outside to the outer gateway, the way facing east, and behold, waters were flowing on the right side. <verse eid="EZK 47:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 47:3"/>At the going out of the man to the east, and the line in his hand, he measured a thousand by the cubit;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">1,000 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 1,750 feet or 533.4 meters.</char></note> and he brought me through the waters—waters to the ankles. <verse eid="EZK 47:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 47:4"/>And he measured a thousand, and he brought me through the waters—waters to the knees; </para>

<para style="p" vid="EZK 47:4">and again he measured a thousand, and he brought me through waters to the loins. <verse eid="EZK 47:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 47:5"/>And he measured a thousand—a river that I was not able to cross; for the waters had risen—waters for swimming, a river that could not be crossed. <verse eid="EZK 47:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 47:6"/>And he said to me, “Have you seen, son of man?” And he brought me and returned me <char style="add">to</char> the bank of the river. <verse eid="EZK 47:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 47:7"/>In my returning, behold, along the bank of the river <char style="add">were</char> very many trees, on this side and on this side. <verse eid="EZK 47:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 47:8"/>And He said to me: “These waters are flowing toward the eastern border, and they go down upon the Arabah and enter the Sea;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Dead Sea</char></note> and having gone out into the sea, <char style="add">its</char> waters are healed.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">become fresh</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; similarly in verses 9 and 11</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 47:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 47:9"/>And it will come to pass <char style="add">that</char> every soul living that moves, at every <char style="add">place</char> where the rivers should come there, will live. And there will be a great abundance of fish, because these waters come there, and they will be healed. And will live everything wherever the river comes there. <verse eid="EZK 47:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 47:10"/>And it will come to pass <char style="add">that</char> fishermen will stand upon it. From En-gedi unto En-eglaim will be a spreading place of nets; their fish will be according to their kind as the fish of the Great Sea,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Mediterranean Sea; also in verses 15, 19, and 20</char></note> exceedingly many. <verse eid="EZK 47:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 47:11"/>And its swamps and marshes will still not be healed; they will be given to salt. <verse eid="EZK 47:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 47:12"/>And alongside the river will come up along the bank, on this side and on this side, every of tree for food; its leaf will not wither, and its fruit will not fail. According to its months it will bear fruit, because its waters, they <char style="add">are</char> flowing from the sanctuary, and its fruit will be for food, and its leaf for healing.” <verse eid="EZK 47:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Borders of the Land</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 47:13"/>Thus says the Lord YHWH: “These <char style="add">are</char> the borders by which you⁺ shall divide as an inheritance the land among the twelve tribes of Israel. Joseph <char style="add">shall have</char> portions,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Since Levi had no portion, Joseph’s sons Ephraim and Manasseh received land as two tribes.</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 47:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 47:14"/>and you⁺ shall divide it one with another, for I lifted up My hand to give it to your⁺ fathers, and this land will fall to you⁺ as an inheritance. <verse eid="EZK 47:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 47:15"/>And this <char style="add">is</char> the border of the land on the side of the north, from the Great Sea, <char style="add">by</char> the way of Hethlon, through Lebo-hamath to Zedad, <verse eid="EZK 47:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 47:16"/>Berothah, and Sibraim,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">15</char><char style="fq" closed="false"> …at the coming in to Zedad, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">16</char><char style="fq" closed="false"> Hamath, Berothah, and Sibraim</char></note> which <char style="add">is</char> between the border of Damascus and between the border of Hamath; Hazar-Hatticon, which <char style="add">is</char> on the border of Hauran. <verse eid="EZK 47:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 47:17"/>And will be the boundary from the Sea to Hazar-enan, the border of Damascus and to the north, to the north, and the border of Hamath. And <char style="add">this is</char> the side to the north. <verse eid="EZK 47:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 47:18"/>And on the side of the east from between Hauran, and between Damascus, and between Gilead, and between the land of Israel, <char style="add">along</char> the Jordan; from <char style="add">this</char> border to the Eastern Sea<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Dead Sea</char></note> as far as Tamar.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Syriac; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to Eastern Sea you shall mark out.</char></note> And <char style="add">this is</char> the side of the east. <verse eid="EZK 47:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 47:19"/>And the side of the Negev toward the south: From Tamar unto the waters of Meribah Kadesh, <char style="add">along</char> the brook <char style="add">of Egypt</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Egypt</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> to the Great Sea. And <char style="add">this is</char> the side of the Negev toward the south. <verse eid="EZK 47:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 47:20"/>And <char style="add">on</char> the side of the west, the Great Sea, from the border until over against the coming in Hamath. This <char style="add">is</char> the side of the west. <verse eid="EZK 47:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 47:21"/>And you⁺ shall divide this land among yourselves, according to the tribes of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 47:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 47:22"/>And it will come to pass <char style="add">that</char> you⁺ will allot it as an inheritance for yourselves and for the sojourners who are sojourning in your⁺ midst who give birth to sons in your⁺ midst, and they will be unto you⁺ as a native among the sons of Israel; with you⁺ they shall be allotted an inheritance in the midst of the tribes of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 47:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 47:23"/>And it will come to pass in the tribe with which the sojourner sojourned, <char style="add">that</char> there you⁺ will give his inheritance,” a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 47:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 47"/>

<chapter number="48" style="c" sid="EZK 48"/>

<para style="s">The Portions for the Tribes</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="EZK 48:1"/>“And these <char style="add">are</char> the names of the tribes: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 48:1">From the border of the north, along the coast of the way of Hethlon, at the entrance of Hamath, <char style="add">unto</char> Hazar-enan, <char style="add">on</char> the border of Damascus northward, toward the hand of Hamath, there will be from the side of the east <char style="add">to</char> the west <char style="add">for</char> Dan one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="EZK 48:2"/>And along the border of Dan, from the side of the east to the side of the west, <char style="add">for</char> Asher one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="EZK 48:3"/>And along the border of Asher, from the side of the east to the side of the west, <char style="add">for</char> Naphtali one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="EZK 48:4"/>And along the border of Naphtali, from the side of the east to the side of the west, <char style="add">for</char> Manasseh one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="EZK 48:5"/>And along the border of Manasseh, from the side of the east to the side of the west, <char style="add">for</char> Ephraim one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="EZK 48:6"/>And along the border of Ephraim, from the side of the east to the side of the west, <char style="add">for</char> Reuben one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="EZK 48:7"/>And along the border of Reuben, from the side of the east to the side of the west, <char style="add">for</char> Judah one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:7"/></para>

<para style="s">The Portions for the Priests and Levites</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="EZK 48:8"/>And along the border of Judah, from the side of the east to the side of the west, will be the portion that you⁺ will lift up—five and twenty thousand in width,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">25,000 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 8.3 miles or 13.3 kilometers; also in verses 9, 10, 13, 15, 20, and 21.</char></note> and <char style="add">in</char> length as one of the portions, from the side of the east to the side of the west, with the sanctuary in the middle of it. <verse eid="EZK 48:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="EZK 48:9"/>The portion that you⁺ shall lift up for YHWH <char style="add">shall be</char> five and twenty thousand in length, and ten thousand in width. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">10,000 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 3.3 miles or 5.3 kilometers; also in verses 10, 13, and 18.</char></note><verse eid="EZK 48:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="EZK 48:10"/>And to these will be the holy portion for the priests: To the north five and twenty thousand, and to the west ten thousand in width, and to the east ten thousand in width, and to the south five and twenty thousand in length; and the sanctuary of YHWH will be in the middle of it <verse eid="EZK 48:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="EZK 48:11"/>for the priests who are sanctified from the sons of Zadok, those who have kept My charge, who did not go astray in the straying of the sons of Israel, as the Levites went astray. <verse eid="EZK 48:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="EZK 48:12"/>And a special portion will be for them from the portion of the land, a holy of holies,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a Most Holy Place</char></note> toward the border of the Levites. <verse eid="EZK 48:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="EZK 48:13"/>And the Levites <char style="add">shall be</char> next to the border of the priests, five and twenty thousand in length, and ten thousand in width; all the length <char style="add">shall be</char> five and twenty thousand, and the width ten thousand. <verse eid="EZK 48:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="EZK 48:14"/>And they shall not sell of it, and not exchange <char style="add">it</char>; and they must not cause to pass through the firstfruit of the land, for <char style="add">it is</char> holy to YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 48:14"/></para>

<para style="s">The Common Portion</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="EZK 48:15"/>And the five thousand<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">5,000 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 1.7 miles or 2.7 kilometers.</char></note> that are remaining in width, along the edge of the five and twenty thousand, <char style="add">is</char> for common use; it <char style="add">is</char> for the city, for dwellings, and for pastureland; and the city will be in the middle of it. <verse eid="EZK 48:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="EZK 48:16"/>And these <char style="add">shall be</char> its measurements: The side of the north, five hundred and four thousand; and the side of the south, five <char style="add">and</char> five hundred and four thousand;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">4,500 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 1.5 miles or 2.4 kilometers; also in verses 30, 32, 33, and 34.</char></note> and the side of the east, five hundred and four thousand; and the side of the west, five hundred and four thousand. <verse eid="EZK 48:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="EZK 48:17"/>And the pastureland for the city will be to the north fifty and two hundred, and to the south fifty and two hundred,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">250 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 437.5 feet or 133.4 meters.</char></note> and to the east fifty and two hundred, and to the west fifty and two hundred. <verse eid="EZK 48:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="EZK 48:18"/>And the remainder of the length alongside the holy portion <char style="add">shall be</char> ten thousand to the east, and ten thousand to the west; and it will be adjacent to the holy portion, and its produce will be for food for the workers of the city. <verse eid="EZK 48:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="EZK 48:19"/>And the workers of the city will work it from all the tribes of Israel. <verse eid="EZK 48:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="EZK 48:20"/>All the portion <char style="add">shall be</char> five and twenty thousand by five and twenty thousand, foursquare; you⁺ shall lift up the holy portion along with the property of the city. <verse eid="EZK 48:20"/></para>

<para style="s">The Portion for the Prince</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="EZK 48:21"/>And the remainder <char style="add">is</char> unto the prince, on this side and on this side of the holy portion and the property of the city; toward the faces of the five and twenty thousand portion alongside the border of the east, and westward alongside the faces of the five and twenty thousand along the border of the west, adjacent to the allotments, <char style="add">is</char> unto the prince. The holy portion and the sanctuary of the temple will be in the midst of it. <verse eid="EZK 48:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="EZK 48:22"/>And apart from the possession of the Levites, and from the possession of the city, in the midst of what will be unto the prince, between the border of Judah and between the border of Benjamin, will be unto the prince. <verse eid="EZK 48:22"/></para>

<para style="s">The Portions for the Remaining Tribes</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="EZK 48:23"/>And the rest of the tribes: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="EZK 48:23">From the side of the east to the side of the west, Benjamin <char style="add">has</char> one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="EZK 48:24"/>And along the border of Benjamin, from the side of the east to the side of the west, Simeon <char style="add">has</char> one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="EZK 48:25"/>And along the border of Simeon, from the side of the east to the side of the west, Issachar <char style="add">has</char> one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="EZK 48:26"/>And along the border of Issachar, from the side of the east to the side of the west, Zebulun <char style="add">has</char> one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="EZK 48:27"/>And along the border of Zebulun, from the side of the east to the side of the west, Gad <char style="add">has</char> one <char style="add">portion</char>. <verse eid="EZK 48:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="EZK 48:28"/>And along the border of Gad, on the side of the Negev, toward the south, the border will be from Tamar <char style="add">to</char> the waters of Meribah Kadesh, along the brook <char style="add">of Egypt</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Egypt</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> to the Great Sea.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Mediterranean Sea</char></note> <verse eid="EZK 48:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="EZK 48:29"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the land that you⁺ shall allot as an inheritance among the tribes of Israel, and these <char style="add">are</char> their portions,” a declaration of the Lord YHWH. <verse eid="EZK 48:29"/></para>

<para style="s">The City Gates and Dimensions</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="EZK 48:30"/>“And these <char style="add">are</char> the exits of the city: On the side of the north, <char style="add">which is</char> five hundred and four thousand <char style="add">by</char> measure, <verse eid="EZK 48:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="EZK 48:31"/>and <char style="add">these</char> gates of the city <char style="add">are</char> according to the names of the tribes of Israel: Three gates to the north—one gate for Reuben, one gate for Judah, and one gate for Levi. <verse eid="EZK 48:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="EZK 48:32"/>And on the side of the east, five hundred and four thousand, also three gates—one gate for Joseph, one gate for Benjamin, and one gate for Dan. <verse eid="EZK 48:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="EZK 48:33"/>And on the side of the south, five hundred and four thousand <char style="add">by</char> measure, also three gates—one gate for Simeon, one gate for Issachar, and one gate for Zebulun. <verse eid="EZK 48:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="EZK 48:34"/>On the side of the west, five hundred and four thousand, their three gates—one gate for Gad, one gate for Asher, and one gate for Naphtali. <verse eid="EZK 48:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="EZK 48:35"/>All around <char style="add">it</char> eighteen thousand.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">18,000 (long) cubits</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 6 miles or 9.6 kilometers.</char></note> And the name of the city from <char style="add">that</char> day <char style="add">is</char>: <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">YHWH Shammah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">YHWH IS THERE</char></note><verse eid="EZK 48:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="EZK 48"/>

</usx>
